// Terms follow the Notion 术语主表 and the T0 tables (places, posts, factions, names).
// Bracketed notes: the author's working marks (作者定, 作者核, 待核, 月份待核, 系年暂定, source
// and dating notes, writing instructions) are left out; story points still open (……待定, 未定)
// are kept as “undecided”; facts inside a note, cross-references and sources are translated.
export const eventsEn = {
  // 651
  "大食（阿拉伯）入攻，萨珊波斯四百年至此名存实亡——昔复兴波斯、建萨珊王朝（波斯第二帝国）之阿尔达希尔一世，出琐罗亚斯德教祭司世家：其祖萨珊为阿那希特神庙祭司（王朝得名于此），父帕帕克为伊斯塔赫尔城主；举兵之前尝为安息（帕提亚）末王阿尔达班五世之法尔斯总督（约208年起）":
    "The Arabs invaded, and four hundred years of Sasanian Persia survived from then on in name only. Ardashir I, who had revived Persia and founded the Sasanian dynasty (the second Persian empire), came of a family of Zoroastrian priests: his grandfather Sasan was a priest of the temple of Anahita (the dynasty took its name from him), and his father Papak was lord of Istakhr; before he rose in arms he had served the last Parthian (Arsacid) king, Artabanus V, as governor of Fars (from about 208).",
  // 654
  "波斯王卑路斯两度遣使入唐告难求援；时唐未平西突厥，不应":
    "The Persian king Peroz twice sent envoys to the Tang to report his plight and ask for help; the Tang, which had not yet subdued the Western Türks, did not answer.",
  // 661
  "卑路斯又求援；时葱岭东西原属突厥诸小国宗主权转归于唐，唐始行羁縻，置羁縻都督府州，并于卑路斯所在之疾陵城立波斯都督府":
    "Peroz asked for help again. By now suzerainty over the small states east and west of the Pamirs, once held by the Türks, had passed to the Tang, which began its loose-rein (jimi) administration, setting up loose-rein area commands and prefectures, and established a Persian Area Command at Zaranj, where Peroz was.",
  // 663
  "唐任卑路斯为波斯都督，流亡政府始成":
    "The Tang named Peroz Area Commander of Persia, and the government in exile took shape.",
  // 674
  "大食侵逼，卑路斯逃入长安；萨珊王室成员、贵族教士或同往，或流落居于西域——随王奔走、往来长安西域的王室族裔中，有陆羽鸣祖辈父辈，早与陆危楼有交，无论在琐教中还是行商":
    "Pressed by the Arabs, Peroz fled to Chang’an; members of the Sasanian royal house, nobles and priests went with him or were left scattered in the Western Regions. Among the royal kin who followed the king and travelled between Chang’an and the Western Regions were Lu Yuming’s forebears, long on good terms with Lu Weilou, both within the Zoroastrian faith and in trade.",
  // 678
  "唐册卑路斯长子泥涅师师为波斯王":
    "The Tang invested Peroz’s eldest son Narsieh as king of Persia.",
  // 679
  "唐命裴行俭为「安抚大食使」，发波斯道行军，册送泥涅师师归吐火罗——唐认卑路斯—泥涅师师一脉为萨珊波斯正统代表":
    "The Tang made Pei Xingjian Commissioner for Pacifying the Arabs, sent out a Persia Route field army and escorted Narsieh back to Tokharistan as king: the Tang recognised the line of Peroz and Narsieh as the rightful representatives of Sasanian Persia.",
  // 707
  "景龙元年，琐教「影月」长老陆危楼立明教，为教主——萨珊既亡（651），火祆教托庇于唐而东传；教势顶峰约在开元二十三年（735）前后":
    "In the first year of Jinglong, Lu Weilou, an elder of the “Shadow Moon” in the Zoroastrian faith, founded the Mingjiao and became its leader. With the fall of the Sasanians (651), Zoroastrianism had come east under the Tang’s protection; the order was at its height around the twenty-third year of Kaiyuan (735).",
  // 708
  "泥涅师师在吐火罗地区与大食抗战二十余年后返唐，病死长安，唐以为「其国遂灭」；然于卑路斯及同亡波斯人礼遇有加，长安有波斯人社区":
    "After more than twenty years of resisting the Arabs in Tokharistan, Narsieh came back to the Tang and died of illness in Chang’an, and the Tang held that “his kingdom thus came to an end”. Yet Peroz and the Persians who fell with him were treated with great courtesy, and Chang’an had a Persian community.",
  // 715
  "陆羽鸣出生——萨珊流亡王室族裔，入教即逢盛时（教势顶峰约在开元二十三年735前后），少小听长辈讲长安事":
    "Lu Yuming was born, of the exiled Sasanian royal kin. He entered the faith at its height (the order peaked around the twenty-third year of Kaiyuan, 735), and as a child heard his elders talk of Chang’an.",
  "程广成婚；新婚夜夫人焚稿（夫人696年生，时年二十）":
    "Cheng Guang married; on the wedding night his wife burned her writings (she was born in 696, and was twenty).",
  // 716
  "程锋出生（嫡长子）":
    "Cheng Feng was born (the eldest son of the principal wife).",
  // 717
  "开元五年，岚川靖彦（716年为元正天皇选为遣唐留学生）随左大臣多治比县守使团自难波港出发，四船并联、一行五百五十七人西渡东海，扬州登陆赴长安苦读——同行有阿倍仲麻吕（晁衡）、学问僧玄昉、吉备真备；后授秘书监校书郎，累迁中书省主书":
    "In the fifth year of Kaiyuan, Lanchuan Jingyan (chosen by Empress Genshō in 716 as a student with the Japanese embassy to the Tang) set out from Naniwa with the embassy of the Minister of the Left, Tajihi no Agatamori: four ships sailing together, five hundred and fifty-seven people crossing the Eastern Sea, landing at Yangzhou and going on to Chang’an to study hard. With him went Abe no Nakamaro (Chao Heng), the scholar-monk Genbō and Kibi no Makibi. He was later made Collator in the Palace Library, and rose to be a Clerk of the Secretariat.",
  "程钊出生——庶出，生母为夫人陪嫁婢，生子后放良为妾":
    "Cheng Zhao was born, a secondary son: his mother was a maid who had come with the wife at her marriage, freed after the birth and made a concubine.",
  // 721
  "开元九年，六胡州不堪税负、徭役而叛乱，败后残部流散南北诸州；剿逆期间消息迟滞、任命重复，陇右、朔方节度争功，一方招降胡众、一方反纵兵击之，归降胡人嫉恨，相率复叛":
    "In the ninth year of Kaiyuan the Six Hu Prefectures, crushed by taxes and labour service, rose in revolt; after their defeat the remnants scattered to prefectures north and south. During the suppression news travelled late and appointments overlapped, and the Longyou and Shuofang commissioners vied for credit, one taking the Hu into surrender while the other loosed troops on them; the surrendered Hu, embittered, rose again together.",
  "六胡州乱中，荔非父辈屡被点名带路搜山寻叛胡、协助清点户籍、收缴兵器；一族叔因押送归降胡众不利被枭首（时荔非四五岁，被母亲按在怀里，抬头看见父亲双眼通红）；此后一二年族中惶惶终日，父辈因教少年存活于边镇之道——少习汉话、略通书字，熟识地名、驿路、边军旗号":
    "In the Six Hu Prefectures revolt the Lifei elders were named again and again to guide searches of the hills for rebel Hu, to help count households and to collect weapons; a clan uncle was beheaded for failing to bring a column of surrendered Hu through (Lifei was four or five; pressed into his mother’s arms, he looked up and saw his father’s eyes red). For a year or two the clan lived in dread, and so the elders taught the boys how to survive in the frontier garrisons: learn Chinese young, know a few written characters, know the place names, the post roads and the banners of the frontier armies.",
  // 722
  "程广回东都面圣受赏（是年玄宗驻跸东都），入歌楼遇阿玉":
    "Cheng Guang came back to the Eastern Capital for an audience with the emperor and a reward (that year Xuanzong was staying at the Eastern Capital), went into a house of song and met A-Yu.",
  "程凯出生于洛阳歌楼——开元十年腊月，早产八个多月":
    "Cheng Kai was born in a house of song in Luoyang, in the twelfth month of the tenth year of Kaiyuan, premature at a little over eight months.",
  // 723
  "冬，高垣高堑兄弟为叔父家所弃，雪夜负幼弟跋涉，黎明遭狼群围咬；黍梁（宣康）链刃退狼救下二人，安置远门沟——「路呢，有。不过要卖命的。」「但凡可以谋生，不怕。都好过冻毙风雪。」":
    "Winter. Abandoned by their uncle’s family, the brothers Gao Yuan and Gao Qian struggled through the snow at night, the elder carrying the younger on his back, and at dawn were set upon by a pack of wolves; Shuliang (Xuan Kang) drove the wolves off with his chain blade, saved them and settled them in Yuanmen Gully: “A road? There is one. But you have to sell your life for it.” “So long as it’s a living, we’re not afraid. Anything is better than freezing to death in the snow.”",
  // 724
  "高垣受训参试，三回方入凌雪阁（绊在机关与鸟不归的杂念上）；入门后力道刚劲而身法总不及，侦讯之敏见长，归入机枢府，从识字学起——训练、外勤，懂规矩，耐严刑":
    "Gao Yuan trained and sat the trials, and got into the Lingxue Pavilion only at the third attempt (tripped up by the mechanisms, and by stray thoughts in the Birds-Never-Return, the Pavilion’s steep trial forest). Once in, his strength was hard and forceful but his footwork never quite enough; his gift was for interrogation, and he was assigned to the Jishu Bureau, where he began by learning to read: training, field work, knowing the rules, enduring harsh interrogation.",
  // 725
  "程广回东都，随驾东封泰山（史：十一月封禅），公务缠身，未往歌楼；夫人于此时有孕（程钧）":
    "Cheng Guang came back to the Eastern Capital and went east with the emperor for the feng sacrifice at Mount Tai (historically, the sacrifice was in the eleventh month); busy with official duties, he did not go to the house of song. His wife became pregnant at this time (with Cheng Jun).",
  // 726
  "程钧出生（夫人所出），比程凯小三四岁":
    "Cheng Jun was born (to the principal wife), three or four years younger than Cheng Kai.",
  // 727
  "陆晚月出生":
    "Lu Wanyue was born.",
  "阿玉亡故":
    "A-Yu died.",
  // 728
  "阿辉被岚川夫妇收留（按：原编年此条与「在奈良出生」并系一年，而岚川云生年经作者更正为724，收留之年仍从原文728，作者已确认无误）":
    "Ahui was taken in by the Lanchuan couple.",
  "开元十六年，宣康（黍梁）于巢县成婚，翌年得一子；有他在，妻子温饱、不忧税赋——籍贯人口悉上报留档，此即后来高垣按档寻访之据":
    "In the sixteenth year of Kaiyuan Xuan Kang (Shuliang) married in Chao County, and had a son the next year; with him there, his wife was fed and clothed and never worried about taxes. The household’s registration and members were all reported and kept on file, and this was what Gao Yuan later went by when he traced them through the records.",
  "靖彦于奈良西郊宅后河边救起重伤漂流的少年斥候，夫妇照料收留；赵盈贞以早夭幼弟之名为其命名「辉」——「这就是了，人间哪…没有无端相逢」。阿辉自此为岚川家帮工护院，待之如家人无二；两年间带幼年岚川云跑遍林野，以九宫桩石授其轻功底子":
    "On the riverbank behind his house in the western outskirts of Nara, Jingyan pulled out a badly wounded young scout who had drifted downstream, and he and his wife nursed him and took him in; Zhao Yingzhen named him Hui, after a little brother of hers who had died young: “There it is. In this world… no meeting comes without a reason.” From then on Ahui worked for the Lanchuan household and guarded it, and was treated no differently from family; for two years he took the young Lanchuan Yun all over the woods and fields, and on nine-palace stepping posts taught her the foundations of qinggong.",
  "端午，洛阳南市，程凯救下被掳的幼年沈含英（右腕被刺伤留疤）；程广见其颈间玉坠，带程凯入程府":
    "The Duanwu festival, at Luoyang’s Southern Market: Cheng Kai rescued the young Shen Hanying from kidnappers (a stab wound to his right wrist left a scar); Cheng Guang saw the jade pendant at his neck and took Cheng Kai into the Cheng household.",
  "程家有意对外称程凯为姬妾所出，记在程钊生母名下；她不肯出面——这是她头一回开口":
    "The Cheng family meant to give out that Cheng Kai was a concubine’s son and to enter him under the name of Cheng Zhao’s mother; she would not lend herself to it: the first time she ever spoke up.",
  // 729
  "荔非承烈十二三岁，始随驿队行走，北抵灵、夏边口，送军书、押粮车、牵马骡；驿卒教认路，父亲教认旗——朔方、陇右、河东来兵、受降城兵马，旗号口令盘查各异；一次清查被士兵按头在地，额头磕破，父亲呈谱牒催他复述驿路关口方得脱":
    "At twelve or thirteen Lifei Chenglie began to travel with the post caravans, north as far as the frontier passes of Lingzhou and Xiazhou, carrying army dispatches, escorting grain carts, leading horses and mules. The post riders taught him the roads; his father taught him the banners: the troops of Shuofang, Longyou and Hedong and the men of the Shouxiang Fortresses each had their own banners, passwords and checks. Once, at an inspection, soldiers pinned his head to the ground and split his forehead; only when his father produced the family register and made him recite the post roads and passes was he let go.",
  // 730
  "吕定仪十五岁母丧，随父戍边，在中受降城学习政务、军籍编录、粮草分配；因字迹峭丽、心性严整，被提拔为笔吏":
    "At fifteen Lü Dingyi lost his mother and followed his father to the frontier, learning administration, the compiling of army rolls and the allocation of grain and fodder at the Middle Shouxiang Fortress; his sharp, elegant hand and strict, orderly nature got him promoted to clerk.",
  // 731
  "春，岚川一家自奈良返唐（靖彦723年前后因家事携赵盈贞返乡，居平城京西郊数年，岚川云与阿辉皆在彼间入家）——海上遇风浪偏离航线，漂至江南，登岸遇海寇，阿辉袖间雪光杀退众寇护主；一行北上长安，复居义宁坊。一家与晁衡（阿倍仲麻吕）有交情——晁衡与靖彦同窗":
    "Spring: the Lanchuan family came back to the Tang from Nara (around 723 Jingyan had taken Zhao Yingzhen home on family business and lived for some years in the western outskirts of Heijō-kyō, where Lanchuan Yun and Ahui both came into the family). At sea a storm drove them off course to Jiangnan; when they landed they met pirates, and a flash of snow-light from Ahui’s sleeve drove the pirates off and saved his masters. The family went north to Chang’an and lived again in the Yining Ward. They were friends of Chao Heng (Abe no Nakamaro), who had studied with Jingyan.",
  // 732
  "高堑入门，明山馆受训，武学要旨灵透颖悟，兄长指点之下愈成同辈佼佼，后入吴钩台——「哥，你平日是一句话不露啊，敢情早就是要员。我也不能差了。」「我的路，未见得就是你的路。」":
    "Gao Qian entered the Pavilion and trained at the Mingshan Hall; quick and perceptive in the essentials of the martial arts, under his elder brother’s guidance he became the best of his generation, and later joined the Wugou Terrace: “Brother, you never let slip a word, and all along you were someone important. I can’t fall behind.” “My road isn’t necessarily your road.”",
  "程锋受荫入天策府":
    "Cheng Feng entered the Tiance Command on his father’s privilege.",
  // 733
  "荔非十五六岁骨骼渐成，选为健儿巡守县境；驿道遇袭，胡人霸路劫粮，他推翻粮车作障、抄上侧坡夺刀相搏退敌，粮米终究无损；守关军官收为随从、授以功夫——「自此而始，刀在你手中」，荐往雁门":
    "At fifteen or sixteen, his frame filling out, Lifei was picked as a professional soldier (jian’er) to patrol the county. When Hu raiders held the post road and fell on a grain convoy, he overturned the carts as a barricade, ran up the side slope, wrested a blade from an enemy and fought them off; not a grain was lost. The officer holding the pass took him on as an orderly and taught him to fight (“From now on, the blade is in your hands”), and recommended him to Yanmen.",
  "程钊随生母赴北庭，比程锋早三年到边地（程锋736年至北庭）":
    "Cheng Zhao went with his mother to Beiting, reaching the frontier three years before Cheng Feng (who came to Beiting in 736).",
  // 734
  "荔非承烈入苍云":
    "Lifei Chenglie joined the Cangyun Army.",
  "黍梁离家临时调往京城，再未返乡；秋，幼女宣杨生于巢县——女儿出生之事他或许至死未知，档案不载":
    "Shuliang left home on a temporary posting to the capital and never came back. In autumn his younger daughter Xuan Yang was born in Chao County; he may never have known of her birth before he died, and the files do not record it.",
  // 735
  "薛褚父母早亡，薛直自觉有照拂后辈孤弱之责，约在此年将其与两三同辈兄弟一并带入苍云，少年在武库管理保养军械；数年后独以踏实沉默、体格气力留为兵员，同来者皆遣回":
    "Xue Chu lost his parents young. Xue Zhi, who felt bound to look after the orphaned and weak of the younger generation, brought him into the Cangyun Army around this year with two or three boys of his generation, and they kept the weapons in the armoury. Some years later he alone was kept on as a soldier, for his steadiness, his silence and his strength; the others who came with him were all sent home.",
  "陆晚月随父行商遭遇马贼袭击，借住人家舍命相救":
    "Travelling with her merchant father, Lu Wanyue was attacked by horse thieves; the family they were lodging with saved them at the risk of their own lives.",
  "明教大光明寺兴建于长安西市义宁坊":
    "The Mingjiao’s Great Bright Temple was built in the Yining Ward by Chang’an’s Western Market.",
  "程钧随三兄程铎习程家家传枪（槊）法（735—740）":
    "Cheng Jun learned the Cheng family’s spear (shuo lance) technique from his third brother Cheng Duo (735–740).",
  "突骑施寇北庭及安西拨换城（史）；程钊初上阵，随父守庭州——围城入冬，城头兵器遇寒脆折，他自请经管甲仗修补，此后一直留在甲仗上":
    "The Türgesh raided Beiting and Bohuan in Anxi (historical). Cheng Zhao saw battle for the first time, holding Tingzhou with his father; as the siege went into winter the weapons on the walls grew brittle in the cold and snapped, and he asked to take charge of repairing the arms and armour, and stayed with the arms and armour from then on.",
  // 736
  "景惠时遭遇死产 身体受损 几乎不能再生育":
    "Jing Huishi suffered a stillbirth that damaged her body; she could hardly bear another child.",
  "陆晚月入明教，拜「影月」掌事陆羽鸣为师；陆晓随鸿胪寺任职的父亲前往安西、居龟兹，始与明教接触，圣山下讲坛成为他的波斯语角（Notion 编年一处作「736陆晓入教」，人设文档以741年为正式入教，兹以736记初接触并注明）":
    "Lu Wanyue entered the Mingjiao and became the pupil of Lu Yuming, a master in charge under the “Shadow Moon” banner. Lu Xiao went to Anxi with his father, who served in the Court of State Ceremonial, lived at Kucha and first came into contact with the Mingjiao; the preaching platform at the foot of the Holy Mountain became the place where he practised his Persian.",
  "宣康任务中身亡（张九龄一事）——李林甫掌中书令、任凌雪阁外阁主，吴钩台长久在其辖下；黍梁因京城一案私向张九龄府中传信，为队友告发。其后不久，抚恤不到，妻与幼子不堪课税、死于酷吏兵痞；幼女为邻人背出得免，此后流浪，随巢县破庙老僧":
    "Xuan Kang died on a mission (the Zhang Jiuling affair). Li Linfu, as President of the Secretariat, was Master of the Lingxue Pavilion’s Outer Pavilion, and the Wugou Terrace had long been under his control; over a case in the capital Shuliang had privately sent word to Zhang Jiuling’s household, and a teammate informed on him. Soon after, with no death benefit paid, his wife and young son, unable to bear the taxes, died at the hands of harsh officials and thuggish soldiers; his little daughter was carried out by a neighbour and escaped, and from then on drifted, living with an old monk in a ruined temple in Chao County.",
  "曼冉出逃，途中加入五毒；来到这座西南山区村寨落脚，露出本事（据共创文本一：采蛛丝至溪山渡，遇村寨易主与毒蛛之祸，助卓沃平祸）":
    "Mait Rangs fled, joining the Wudu Order on the way; she came to settle in this hill village in the south-west and showed what she could do (gathering spider silk at Xishan Ford, she met a village that had changed hands and a plague of venomous spiders, and helped Zhod Vos put it down).",
  "程凯带程钧溜出府看夜市，教他躲避父兄责罚（约735—737）":
    "Cheng Kai took Cheng Jun sneaking out of the house to see the night market, and taught him how to dodge punishment from their father and brothers (around 735–737).",
  "北庭都护盖嘉运率兵击突骑施，破之（史）；程广、程钊从征——史书只记主帅之名，是程钊头一回有功不得封赏":
    "Gai Jiayun, Protector-General of Beiting, led troops against the Türgesh and routed them (historical); Cheng Guang and Cheng Zhao went with him. The histories record only the commander’s name: the first time Cheng Zhao earned merit and was given no reward.",
  "程锋天策三年期满，至北庭，时突骑施新破——小一岁的庶弟已是见过血的人；识陆灵":
    "Cheng Feng’s three years at the Tiance Command were up and he came to Beiting just after the Türgesh had been routed: his half-brother, a year younger, was already a man who had seen blood. He came to know Lu Ling.",
  "上秋，义宁坊茶铺争执延及岚川家铁器商铺，明教陆隐等数人闯铺夺器殴斗——赵盈贞时有孕七月，跌扑受惊不能安产，失血发痫，与子俱亡；官府依唐律斗讼条，元谋者陆隐减斗杀一等，科流三千里":
    "Early autumn: a quarrel at a teahouse in the Yining Ward spilled into the Lanchuan family’s ironware shop, and Lu Yin and several other Mingjiao men broke in, seized its wares and brawled. Zhao Yingzhen, seven months pregnant, fell and was badly frightened; the birth went wrong, she haemorrhaged and convulsed, and she and the child both died. Under the Tang Code’s articles on affrays the authorities sentenced Lu Yin, as the instigator, at one degree below homicide in an affray: exile to three thousand li.",
  // 737
  "玄甲军征召北地青壮，吕定仪身板见拒，以誊录军籍之便自写名于册；旋奉派五原，遭突厥围困，请郡守开府库，留什一存贮，按籍设配额、五日一校，四五十日城内大抵免于饥馑；事后玄甲军下帖，召至雁门为军师幕下参佐":
    "When the Xuanjia Army called up the young men of the north, Lü Dingyi was turned away for his slight build, and used his work copying the army rolls to write his own name in. Sent soon after to Wuyuan, he was besieged there by the Türks; he asked the governor to open the treasury and granaries, kept a tenth in reserve, set rations by the household register and checked them every five days, and for forty or fifty days the town was largely spared famine. Afterwards the Xuanjia Army sent him a summons to Yanmen as a staff assistant to the strategist.",
  "吕定仪入苍云／荔非武功渐成／闵方城在甘州放牧":
    "Lü Dingyi joined the Cangyun Army / Lifei’s martial skill came into its own / Min Fangcheng herded livestock at Ganzhou.",
  "景惠时与关山到雁门关安顿，邻女生子（即边赛远），景惠时协助，关山投军":
    "Jing Huishi and Guan Shan settled at Yanmen Pass; when the woman next door gave birth (the child was Bian Saiyuan), Jing Huishi helped; Guan Shan enlisted.",
  "王维在凉州河西节度使崔希逸幕下任节度判官，作《老将行》——「射杀中山白额虎，肯数邺下黄须儿」「卫青不败，李广无功」：荔非承烈「白额当关」之号与「无功」之字所本":
    "Wang Wei, on the staff of Cui Xiyi, Military Commissioner of Hexi at Liangzhou, as administrative assistant, wrote “Song of the Old General”: “He shot dead the white-browed tiger of Zhongshan; would he reckon with the yellow-bearded son of Ye?” and “Wei Qing never lost … Li Guang won no merit.” These lines are the source of Lifei Chenglie’s epithet, The White-Browed Tiger Holds the Pass, and of his courtesy name Wugong, “no merit”.",
  "冬，风雪夜巡线追奚骑，沟谷中伏，前队旗手中箭、旗杆斜折、队阵惊散；荔非不待军令提刀上前，一击劈中欲夺旗之敌骑马颈，掣旗振开、杆杵雪中，队伍在他身后收拢复为严整盾阵；事后以离阵擅动不遵军令受军棍，「背上如火烧，眼里却亮」，此后渐有声名传于营内":
    "Winter. Patrolling the line on a night of wind and snow in pursuit of Xi horsemen, the column was ambushed in a gully; the standard-bearer at the front was hit by an arrow, the staff snapped askew and the ranks broke in alarm. Without waiting for orders Lifei went forward with his blade, cut through the neck of the horse of an enemy rider reaching for the standard, snatched up the flag, shook it out and drove the staff into the snow, and behind him the column closed up again into a tight shield wall. Afterwards he was beaten with the army staff for leaving the ranks and acting without orders, “his back as if on fire, but his eyes bright”, and from then on his name began to be talked about in the camp.",
  "曼冉被沃家家长芒沃（女执政官）收为义女——名分而已：曼冉保留本姓 Rangs，不入沃家，不进继承顺位":
    "Mait Rangs was taken as adopted daughter by Mangx Vos, head of the Vos household (the woman who governed): a title only. Mait Rangs kept her own clan name, Rangs, did not enter the Vos household and had no place in its succession.",
  "夏末押粮入关，驿站闻某沟口常有流骑劫掠车队；荔非佯作绕道，诱敌入窄沟，据粮车为障、抄上侧坡故技重施，敌骑几乎尽折，粮米无损；军纪官欲治其擅自改道之罪，吕定仪清点对账时不高不低插一句「数目无损」，军师验其所缴胡骑腰牌（似河北制式），沉吟「罢了」——不治罪，亦不记功":
    "Late summer, escorting grain into the pass. At a post station he heard that mounted raiders often robbed convoys at the mouth of a certain gully. Lifei feigned a detour, lured them into a narrow defile and played his old trick again, the carts as a barricade and a run up the side slope; nearly all the raiders fell, and the grain was untouched. The provost wanted to punish him for changing the route on his own authority; as Lü Dingyi checked the tallies he put in, neither loudly nor softly, “The count is complete.” The strategist examined the waist tokens taken from the Hu riders (apparently of Hebei make), considered, and said, “Let it go”: no punishment, and no merit recorded.",
  "赵盈贞丧满一年祭日，义兄阿辉以屡未能护主为耻，自尽而亡——生平第一次开口说话，乡音唤「小姐…保重」；靖彦抱之允诺「我带你回去，一定带你回去」，葬于长安西郊，唯留其鱼皮柄东瀛短刀":
    "On the first anniversary of Zhao Yingzhen’s death, Ahui, Lanchuan Yun’s adoptive elder brother, ashamed that he had failed time and again to protect the family he served, took his own life; he spoke for the first time in his life, calling in his own tongue, “Miss… take care.” Jingyan held him and promised, “I’ll take you back. I will take you back.” He was buried in the western outskirts of Chang’an; all that was left was his Japanese short blade with its ray-skin (samegawa) hilt.",
  // 738
  "苍云（玄甲军）随王忠嗣出关征奚大胜、吕定仪救荔非右膝骨裂、吕定仪妻移居广武城":
    "The Cangyun Army (the Xuanjia Army) marched out of the pass under Wang Zhongsi against the Xi and won a great victory; Lü Dingyi saved Lifei, whose right knee was cracked; Lü Dingyi’s wife moved to Guangwu Fortress.",
  "圣人命置延恩、怀德、归仁等县，始放回六胡州流散胡户；县治倚河谷夯土为垣，四面设卡、验牒按伍分编，男丁入屯队，昼出垦作、日落归棚更点，离队、越界、聚众皆不容（开元二十六年置宥州及诸县事）":
    "The emperor ordered the counties of Yan’en, Huaide, Guiren and others established, and the scattered Hu households of the Six Prefectures were at last allowed back. The county seats had rammed-earth walls set against the river valleys and checkpoints on all four sides; papers were inspected and people sorted into units of five; the men were put into farming teams, out to till by day and back in their sheds by sunset for the watch count. Leaving the team, crossing the boundary and gathering in groups were all forbidden. (The founding of Youzhou and its counties in the twenty-sixth year of Kaiyuan.)",
  "春夏间，六胡州流散杂胡持旧牒假称奉招抚，劫掠村镇、劫马邑馆驿；玄甲军封锁关卡独留老驿道诱其入网，荔非巡守道口擒之押回；囚前杀心暗起，薛直诫之——「杀得尽吗？……今日你做主动刀，有一次，便有两次、三次、百次。你成了什么人？」翌日荔非亲押杂胡赴三县安置，二十余日往返，城外宿一夜而去；是年秋，晋破阵营第二团旅帅":
    "In spring and summer, scattered Hu from the Six Prefectures, carrying old papers and falsely claiming to have submitted, plundered villages and robbed the post station at Mayi. The Xuanjia Army closed the checkpoints, leaving only the old post road open to draw them into the net, and Lifei, guarding the road mouth, captured them and brought them back. Before the prisoners the urge to kill rose in him; Xue Zhi warned him: “Can you kill them all? … If today you are the one who strikes, once becomes twice, three times, a hundred times. What will you have become?” The next day Lifei himself escorted the Hu to be resettled in the three counties, more than twenty days there and back, and spent one night outside the walls before he left. That autumn he was promoted to Battalion Commander in the Second Regiment of the Rank-Breaker Corps.",
  "曼冉成为祭司":
    "Mait Rangs became a priestess.",
  "手钏被诬：程凯身上一件女人首饰（阿娘遗物）被人发现，程铎首告，诬他偷了夫人之物；程钧知情未言。程凯打出程府，投天策；洛阳来信报到北庭，程钊在父亲身边说「他爱做什么就做什么吧」":
    "The bracelet: a woman’s ornament (his mother’s keepsake) was found on Cheng Kai, and Cheng Duo informed on him, falsely accusing him of stealing it from the principal wife; Cheng Jun knew the truth and said nothing. Cheng Kai fought his way out of the Cheng house and went to the Tiance Command. When the letter from Luoyang reached Beiting, Cheng Zhao, at his father’s side, said, “Let him do whatever he likes.”",
  "叶曙兮随家人西来寻镔铁；北庭兵器遇寒脆折，她与经管甲仗的程钊相识":
    "Ye Shuxi came west with her family in search of fine steel (bintie); the weapons at Beiting were snapping in the cold, and she came to know Cheng Zhao, who had charge of the arms and armour.",
  "闵方城流浪长安西市":
    "Min Fangcheng drifted about Chang’an’s Western Market.",
  "王昱任剑南节度使，奉命「分道经略吐蕃」，毁赤岭碑":
    "Wang Yu became Military Commissioner of Jiannan, ordered to “campaign against Tibet along separate routes”, and destroyed the boundary stele at Chiling.",
  "闵方城至雁门广武城":
    "Min Fangcheng reached Guangwu Fortress at Yanmen.",
  "岚川云丧服满后投天策府——临行靖彦将阿辉随身短刀放在她手中：「让他跟着你，他会愿意」（是年中有几个月闵方城正流浪长安西市及附近诸坊，两人可能碰见过，岚川云给过吃的——参本年三月条）":
    "Her mourning over, Lanchuan Yun went to join the Tiance Command; as she left, Jingyan put Ahui’s short blade in her hand: “Let him go with you. He would want to.” (For several months that year Min Fangcheng was drifting about the Western Market and the wards nearby; the two may have crossed paths, and Lanchuan Yun may have given him something to eat: see the entry for the third month.)",
  "王昱于吐蕃所据安戎城旁筑两城断其粮道，吐蕃大举来救，唐军大败、死者数千，王昱贬死岭南。底色：程铎不在此役——是年他尚在洛阳首告程凯":
    "Wang Yu built two forts beside Tibetan-held Anrong to cut its supply road; the Tibetans came in force to relieve it, the Tang army was badly beaten with thousands dead, and Wang Yu was demoted to Lingnan, where he died. Background: Cheng Duo was not in this battle; that year he was still in Luoyang, informing on Cheng Kai.",
  "册南诏蒙归义（皮逻阁）为云南王；皮逻阁厚赂王昱，求合六诏为一，朝廷从之":
    "Meng Guiyi (Piluoge) of Nanzhao was invested as Prince of Yunnan; Piluoge had richly bribed Wang Yu, seeking to unite the six zhao into one, and the court agreed.",
  "叶曙兮改制的兵器熬过北庭寒冬；她以铸剑人的眼光读出程钊之字「故廉」的本义——刃口磨平，有功不得封赏；程钊生母给她送去冬衣，是程家最先接纳她的人":
    "The weapons Ye Shuxi reworked lasted through the Beiting winter. With a swordsmith’s eye she read Cheng Zhao’s courtesy name, Gulian, in its root sense: a blade’s edge ground flat, merit earned and never rewarded. Cheng Zhao’s mother sent her winter clothes: the first in the Cheng family to accept her.",
  // 739
  "岚川云受训斥候（739–741），其间认识高垣（凌雪阁中人）":
    "Lanchuan Yun trained as a scout (739–741), and in that time came to know Gao Yuan (of the Lingxue Pavilion).",
  "高垣受托至天杀营（739–741间往来）授近身擒搏、侦讯与反讯问之技，以「青山之后」虚刑试炼弟子耐痛；试岚川云——「你有恨。」「原以为一场杀戮，便能荡平，原来没有。」「你年轻，又是有硬芯的人。自己能弄明白这些事，早晚能。」":
    "At the Tiance Command’s request Gao Yuan came to the Heavenly Slayer Corps (back and forth between 739 and 741) to teach close-quarters grappling, interrogation and resistance to interrogation, testing the pupils’ endurance of pain with a mock torture called “Beyond the Blue Hills”. Testing Lanchuan Yun: “You have hatred.” “I thought one round of killing would level it. It didn’t.” “You’re young, and there’s something hard at your core. You’ll work these things out for yourself. Sooner or later, you will.”",
  "皮逻阁迁都太和城，洱海谷地成为南诏心脏":
    "Piluoge moved his capital to Taihe, and the Erhai valley became the heart of Nanzhao.",
  "唐青阳改充长任健儿。开元二十五年诏「于诸色征行人内及客户中招募，取丁壮情愿充健儿长任边军者，每岁加于常例，给田地屋宅」——健儿只从征行人与客户中招，他先当过一回征行人：738年王昱安戎大败后剑南补兵，青神点到他家，他替父亲去了，名册上写的是父亲的名字。739年改充健儿，名册上才第一次是自己的名字；钱粮寄回青神，替家里补庸调的绢":
    "Tang Qingyang re-enlisted as a long-service professional soldier. An edict of the twenty-fifth year of Kaiyuan ordered recruits “from among the campaigners of every kind and the migrant households, taking able-bodied men willing to serve as long-service professional soldiers in the frontier armies, adding to the usual allowance each year and granting fields and houses”. Professional soldiers were drawn only from campaigners and migrant households, and he had already served once as a campaigner: after Wang Yu’s great defeat at Anrong in 738 Jiannan raised replacements, his family in Qingshen was called up, and he went in his father’s place, under his father’s name on the roll. In 739, re-enlisting as a professional soldier, his own name went on the roll for the first time; he sent his pay home to Qingshen to make up the family’s silk for the labour and cloth taxes.",
  "有寨民求医，曼冉以天一教秘法救治男童（天一教正太），男童痊愈后回到父母身边":
    "A villager came for healing, and Mait Rangs treated a boy with the secret arts of the Tianyi Order (the Tianyi Order boy); the boy recovered and went back to his parents.",
  "陆羽鸣赴长安，落脚城西卑路斯旧部后人家":
    "Lu Yuming went to Chang’an and lodged in the west of the city with a household descended from Peroz’s old retainers.",
  "闵方城与苍云军始有来往、结识关山":
    "Min Fangcheng began to have dealings with the Cangyun Army and came to know Guan Shan.",
  "盖嘉运破碎叶，擒突骑施可汗吐火仙（史）；程广、程钊从征":
    "Gai Jiayun took Suyab and captured Tuhuoxian, qaghan of the Türgesh (historical); Cheng Guang and Cheng Zhao went with him.",
  "大光明寺之役，高垣高堑同队（队号「知君青骨」）早往长安布局、为天策府传递机要；高堑有斩敌之功，并于房顶为岚川云解围":
    "In the Great Bright Temple affair Gao Yuan and Gao Qian were in the same squad (the Zhijun Qinggu squad), sent early to Chang’an to lay the ground and to pass secret intelligence to the Tiance Command; Gao Qian had kills to his credit, and on the rooftop he came to Lanchuan Yun’s aid.",
  "秋，大光明寺事件：天策受命，与少林及凌雪阁围剿明教于长安西市义宁坊大光明寺。事前谋划调兵极其隐秘，主动请命赴长安的陆羽鸣仍于一间馆驿周围发现端倪、摸至天策众将集会处，而为时已迟——岚川云穷追，又有凌雪一重保障，使其折戟；陆晚月与岚川云视角皆以为其被高堑当场杀死，实则失踪，此后滞留中原十六年。陆南信因事不在城内，赶回城下时被戒严当夜部署城楼的少年程凯射穿右肘，伤未妥治，筋骨挛缩，无以用双刀":
    "Autumn: the Great Bright Temple Incident. On orders, the Tiance Command, with Shaolin and the Lingxue Pavilion, surrounded and destroyed the Mingjiao at the Great Bright Temple in the Yining Ward by Chang’an’s Western Market. The planning and the movement of troops were kept utterly secret, yet Lu Yuming, who had asked to be sent to Chang’an, still caught the signs around a post house and felt his way to where the Tiance generals were meeting; but by then it was too late. Lanchuan Yun hunted him down, with the Lingxue Pavilion as a second safeguard, and he fell. Both Lu Wanyue and Lanchuan Yun believed Gao Qian had killed him on the spot; in fact he vanished, and stayed in the Central Plains for sixteen years. Lu Nanxin, away from the city at the time, came hurrying back to the walls and was shot through the right elbow by the young Cheng Kai, posted on the gate tower the night the curfew was imposed; the wound was never properly treated, the sinews and bone contracted, and he could no longer use twin blades.",
  "暗线：屋顶一战，陆羽鸣抬头看岚川云，刀线偏开，颈侧下颌重伤失声、昏死，在场者皆以为已死；临昏前念《哈多赫特·纳斯克》2.10 前半句 cišca carāitiš ahi（亡魂过桥之问）":
    "The hidden thread: the fight on the rooftop. Lu Yuming looked up at Lanchuan Yun, the blade’s line veered off, and he was badly wounded at the side of the neck and the jaw, lost his voice and fell senseless; everyone there believed him dead. Before he passed out he spoke the first half of Hadōxt Nask 2.10, cišca carāitiš ahi (the question put to the soul at the bridge).",
  "高堑以刀尖挑下陆羽鸣的萨珊玛瑙印石，交岚川云论功——「剩下的事就是我的了」，拖人离去；岚川云回守军师":
    "With the point of his blade Gao Qian flicked off Lu Yuming’s Sasanian agate seal and gave it to Lanchuan Yun to claim the kill: “The rest is my business.” He dragged the man away; Lanchuan Yun went back to guard the strategist.",
  "暗线：高堑拖人途中发觉陆羽鸣尚有气，不补刀，亦不送机枢府，送回其城西落脚的波斯旧族人家；此后不提（一改口即须剥去岚川云的杀获、交代自己当场让功）。745年高堑死，此事随之入墓林":
    "The hidden thread: dragging him away, Gao Qian found Lu Yuming still breathing. He did not finish him, nor take him to the Jishu Bureau, but carried him back to the old Persian family in the west of the city where he had been lodging, and never spoke of it after (to change his story he would have had to strip Lanchuan Yun of her kill and admit to giving up the credit on the spot). Gao Qian died in 745, and the secret went into the grave with him.",
  "暗线：陆羽鸣困居长安——无籍无过所，恐累收留之家，回教即受疑；教中知情者仅陆危楼（作者定）":
    "The hidden thread: Lu Yuming trapped in Chang’an. He had no household registration and no travel pass, feared bringing trouble on the family that sheltered him, and would fall under suspicion the moment he went back to the order; in the order, only Lu Weilou knew.",
  "岚川云以陆羽鸣的萨珊玛瑙印石论功，得出阵即有「杀获」的嘉奖（时剿杀明教徒甚众，未逐一查验）；印石此后留在她手上":
    "Lanchuan Yun claimed the kill with Lu Yuming’s Sasanian agate seal, and was commended for a kill on her very first sortie (so many Mingjiao followers had been killed that no one checked them one by one); the seal stayed in her hands from then on.",
  "闵方城撞见薛直 修马蹄":
    "Min Fangcheng came upon Xue Zhi trimming a horse’s hooves.",
  "稻谷入仓祭，曼冉带男童主祭，受寨民尊崇，称男童为「圣童」":
    "At the festival for bringing the rice into the granary, Mait Rangs led the rite with the boy, and was revered by the villagers, who called the boy “the Holy Child”.",
  "程钊与藏剑叶曙兮定婚，亲迎须俟长兄先娶；程锋劝他先娶，程钊推辞":
    "Cheng Zhao was betrothed to Ye Shuxi of Cangjian Manor, but the wedding had to wait until his eldest brother married first; Cheng Feng urged him to marry first, and Cheng Zhao declined.",
  "章仇兼琼入奏「安戎城可取」，玄宗大悦，以之为剑南节度使":
    "Zhangchou Jianqiong reported to the throne that “Anrong can be taken”; Xuanzong was delighted and made him Military Commissioner of Jiannan.",
  // 740
  "陆晚月成为「影月」旗下小杀手":
    "Lu Wanyue became a junior assassin under the “Shadow Moon” banner.",
  "冬，高垣代同侪交接情报，误路夜宿巢县破庙，遇幼年宣杨（时庙中老僧新逝）——小孩烤着捡来的饼怡然自得，夜里燎了他的围巾；携归远门沟收养，上报得允，得闲徐徐教些功夫。不知其为恩人黍梁之女":
    "Winter. Handing over intelligence for a colleague, Gao Yuan lost his way and spent the night in a ruined temple in Chao County, where he met the young Xuan Yang (the old monk of the temple had just died): the child was contentedly toasting a cake she had picked up, and in the night she singed his scarf. He took her back to Yuanmen Gully to raise, reported it and was given leave, and taught her some kung fu at his leisure, little by little. He did not know she was the daughter of Shuliang, who had saved him.",
  "叶曙兮撮合程锋与陆灵（739冬—740）：一半出于喜欢陆灵，一半因为那桩婚事成了，自己的才能成":
    "Ye Shuxi brought Cheng Feng and Lu Ling together (winter 739–740): half because she liked Lu Ling, half because once that marriage was made, hers could be.",
  "闵方城入苍云":
    "Min Fangcheng joined the Cangyun Army.",
  "剑南节度使章仇兼琼策反吐蕃安戎城守将翟都局、维州别驾董承晏，开城尽杀吐蕃将卒，以监察御史许远守城；程铎时年二十，随军入城，此为其入剑南后第一份军功（按：738年程铎尚在洛阳首告程凯，故其入剑南系于739年前后，不取738年九月王昱安戎城之败）。唐青阳时年十八，是同在入城队伍里的新健儿：安戎在岷江上游，离祖母讲的蚕丛祖地不远，他第一次看见祖先的山，穿的是官军的衣服":
    "Zhangchou Jianqiong, Military Commissioner of Jiannan, turned Zhai Duju, the Tibetan commander of Anrong Fortress, and Dong Chengyan, Vice Prefect of Weizhou; they opened the gates and killed every Tibetan officer and soldier, and the Investigating Censor Xu Yuan was put in to hold the fortress. Cheng Duo, then twenty, entered it with the army: his first military merit after coming to Jiannan. Tang Qingyang, then eighteen, was a new professional soldier in the same column: Anrong lay on the upper Min River, not far from the land of Cancong his grandmother told of, and he saw his ancestors’ mountains for the first time wearing the uniform of the government army.",
  "长安献俘，立阿史那昕为十姓可汗（史）；程广随盖嘉运入朝受赏，北庭无人主婚":
    "Captives were presented in Chang’an, and Ashina Xin was set up as Qaghan of the Ten Tribes (historical); Cheng Guang went to court with Gai Jiayun to be rewarded, and there was no one at Beiting to preside over a wedding.",
  "莫贺达干怒阿史那昕之立，帅诸部叛（史）；程钊赴俱六守捉，临行叶曙兮越线（由她主动），有了孩子；此后程钊生母常与叶曙兮在城头同望西路":
    "Baga Tarkhan, angered at Ashina Xin’s elevation, led the tribes in revolt (historical); Cheng Zhao was sent to the Juliu Garrison Post. Before he left, Ye Shuxi crossed the line (at her own initiative), and there was a child. From then on Cheng Zhao’s mother often stood with Ye Shuxi on the walls, both watching the western road.",
  "曼冉于蝴蝶泉边收留娜留、佩留并教导；姐妹父母是染织匠人，因「染料中有虫」被逐，迁居山中坠山而亡；姐妹把家传染法带进寨——寨中独有之布由此而来":
    "By Butterfly Spring Mait Rangs took in Nax Liuf and Pet Liuf and taught them. The sisters’ parents were dyers, driven out because “there were insects in the dye”; they moved into the mountains and died in a fall. The sisters brought the family’s dyeing methods into the village, and from them came the cloth found only in this village.",
  "六月至十月，吐蕃两次围攻安戎、维州，关中援兵至而退；安戎城改名平戎城。底色：守城的监察御史许远，757 年与张巡同守睢阳":
    "From the sixth month to the tenth, the Tibetans twice besieged Anrong and Weizhou, and withdrew when relief came from Guanzhong; Anrong was renamed Pingrong. Background: Xu Yuan, the Investigating Censor who held it, would hold Suiyang with Zhang Xun in 757.",
  "吐蕃两次围安戎、维州，唐青阳与程铎同守城头，守城的是监察御史许远。程铎是洛阳来的，不认得这里的山，也听不懂兵说的话；唐青阳替他认路，替他跟兵说话。两人的分工从这里定下：程铎定规矩，唐青阳把规矩讲给兵听":
    "The Tibetans twice besieged Anrong and Weizhou, and Tang Qingyang and Cheng Duo held the walls together under the Investigating Censor Xu Yuan. Cheng Duo came from Luoyang; he did not know these mountains and could not understand what the soldiers said, so Tang Qingyang found the way for him and spoke to the soldiers for him. Their division of labour was settled here: Cheng Duo made the rules, and Tang Qingyang explained the rules to the soldiers.",
  "曼冉主祭，圣童第二年在旁，当场异状，天一教人暗中施术使其恢复，众人未觉；卓沃察觉，暗中收集曼冉勾连天一教、滥用禁术的证据，欲拉她下马":
    "Mait Rangs led the rite, the Holy Child at her side for the second year; something went wrong in front of everyone, and a Tianyi man secretly worked a spell to restore him without anyone noticing. Zhod Vos noticed, and began quietly gathering evidence that Mait Rangs was in league with the Tianyi Order and abusing forbidden arts, meaning to bring her down.",
  "程钊致书程锋交代后事；不愿受抚的部落袭击俱六守捉，程钊战亡——史书只留「叛」与「降」，功劳记在主帅名下；叶曙兮不肯将他的枪头回炉开刃":
    "Cheng Zhao wrote to Cheng Feng setting out his last wishes; tribes unwilling to submit attacked the Juliu Garrison Post, and Cheng Zhao fell in battle. The histories keep only “revolt” and “surrender”, and the merit went to the commander’s name. Ye Shuxi would not let his spearhead be reforged and given an edge.",
  // 741
  "陆晓成为明教正式教众":
    "Lu Xiao became a full member of the Mingjiao.",
  "程广欲接回叶忱，程钊生母劝其放手（她第二次开口），叶曙兮携女回藏剑；同年程广允准程锋与陆灵的婚事（「也罢……总占个心甘情愿」）":
    "Cheng Guang wanted to take Ye Chen in; Cheng Zhao’s mother urged him to let go (the second time she spoke up), and Ye Shuxi took her daughter back to Cangjian Manor. The same year Cheng Guang consented to Cheng Feng’s marriage to Lu Ling (“Very well… at least it’s willing on both sides”).",
  "高堑外任成都（约 741–742）：安戎城刚靠内应拿下，吐蕃反复反扑。章仇兼琼的打法本就是情报战——策反守将、收买别驾——凌雪阁小队的标的，即这条线上的内应或反间；745 年玄鹤别院的「吐蕃翻译」，可以是他在成都结下的人":
    "Gao Qian posted to Chengdu (about 741–742): Anrong had only just been taken with help from inside, and the Tibetans kept counter-attacking. Zhangchou Jianqiong’s way of fighting was a war of intelligence from the start, turning the garrison commander and buying the vice prefect, and the Lingxue squad’s targets were the agents and double agents along this line; the “Tibetan interpreter” at the Xuanhe Lodge in 745 could be someone he got to know in Chengdu.",
  "许秋生之父染疫身亡，沈含英随师走方救其母子，引许秋生入谷——「怕么？」「自己双亲，怕什么。可你有法子么？」":
    "Xu Qiusheng’s father died in an epidemic; Shen Hanying, travelling with his master to treat the sick, saved the mother and son and brought Xu Qiusheng into the Valley: “Are you afraid?” “They’re my own parents. What is there to be afraid of? But do you have a way?”",
  "沈含英、许秋生、江蓠同场入门三选一：沈含英选刀（医者之勇），许秋生选木锨（医者之勤），江蓠选桃（医者之智）":
    "Shen Hanying, Xu Qiusheng and Jiang Li entered the Valley together and each chose one of three: Shen Hanying chose the knife (a physician’s courage), Xu Qiusheng the wooden shovel (a physician’s diligence), Jiang Li the peach (a physician’s wisdom).",
  "男童病情反复，父母求医，曼冉借口将男童留下；天一教人趁虚而入，提供药方或术法（具体待定）":
    "The boy relapsed and his parents sought help; Mait Rangs found an excuse to keep him with her. The Tianyi Order seized its chance, offering prescriptions or spells (details undecided).",
  "叶忱生于北庭，从母姓；名取程钊遗书中的一个「忱」字——信末寻常一语，并非为她而起":
    "Ye Chen was born at Beiting and took her mother’s surname; her name came from the word chen, “sincere”, in Cheng Zhao’s last letter: an ordinary phrase at the end of the letter, not chosen for her.",
  "岚川云一去西域援边（741–742），随杨宁往救一孤城，初会陆晚月（城内有陆晚月亲眷，岚川云不知）；程凯同行，经庭州（北庭一别），碎叶道遇伏":
    "Lanchuan Yun’s first tour to reinforce the Western Regions frontier (741–742): with Yang Ning she went to relieve an isolated town and first met Lu Wanyue (Lu Wanyue had kin inside the town, which Lanchuan Yun did not know). Cheng Kai went too; they passed through Tingzhou (the parting at Beiting) and were ambushed on the Suyab road.",
  "曼冉第三年主祭":
    "Mait Rangs led the rite for the third year.",
  "程广以伊西北庭节度副使出北庭西路，讨不肯受抚的突骑施余部，在程钊殁身的那条路上被围；程凯随杨宁援边，率百骑解围，父子阵前相见——程凯问阿玉葬在哪里，程广答不上来":
    "Cheng Guang, as Vice Military Commissioner of Yixi and Beiting, took the western road out of Beiting against the Türgesh remnants who would not submit, and was surrounded on the very road where Cheng Zhao had died; Cheng Kai, reinforcing the frontier with Yang Ning, broke the encirclement at the head of a hundred horsemen, and father and son met before the lines. Cheng Kai asked where A-Yu was buried; Cheng Guang could not answer.",
  // 742
  "靳沉白（约十五岁）随父北上，避敌袭临时入雁塔，助治伤患、书记誊录，因与楼氏结识楼谊、楼谯姐弟；楼准始有以婿之心，欲留塔纳编，靳沉白辞归乡尽孝进学，此后偶通书信":
    "Jin Chenbai (about fifteen) went north with his father; sheltering from an enemy raid in Yanta Tower, he helped tend the wounded and kept the records, and so came to know the Lou family and the sister and brother Lou Yi and Lou Qiao. Lou Zhun began to think of him as a son-in-law and wanted to keep him on the tower’s rolls; Jin Chenbai declined, going home to serve his parents and pursue his studies, and afterwards they exchanged the occasional letter.",
  "龙门再遇：陆晚月见师父的萨珊玛瑙印石在岚川云身上，二人大打出手；交谈中岚川云复述陆羽鸣临终音节（印石是否交还待定），陆晚月携音节回西域，陆南信认出为亡魂过桥之问；同年，陆隐遇天宝改元大赦获释，回归杀手小队":
    "Meeting again at Longmen: Lu Wanyue saw her master’s Sasanian agate seal on Lanchuan Yun, and the two fought fiercely. As they talked, Lanchuan Yun repeated the syllables Lu Yuming had spoken as he died (whether the seal was given back: undecided); Lu Wanyue carried the syllables back to the Western Regions, and Lu Nanxin recognised them as the question put to the soul at the bridge. The same year Lu Yin was released in the amnesty for the new Tianbao era and went back to the assassin squad.",
  "夫人到北庭；程锋娶陆灵（在程钊期丧满后）":
    "The principal wife came to Beiting; Cheng Feng married Lu Ling (after the year of mourning for Cheng Zhao was over).",
  "吕定仪女生病，妻子抱去营中诊治；苍云上一代人物一同宴饮场景；开春女儿病势复发，夭折，吕定仪妻返乡":
    "Lü Dingyi’s daughter fell ill and his wife carried her to the camp to be treated; a scene of the older generation of the Cangyun Army feasting together. In early spring the girl’s illness returned and she died; Lü Dingyi’s wife went back to her home.",
  "天宝改元大赦，陆隐获释，回影月旗":
    "In the amnesty for the new Tianbao era Lu Yin was released and went back to the Shadow Moon banner.",
  "正式设剑南节度使，治益州，兵三万九百人，职在「西抗吐蕃，南抚蛮獠」":
    "The Military Commission of Jiannan was formally established, seated at Yizhou, with 30,900 troops, charged “to resist Tibet in the west and pacify the Man and Lao in the south”.",
  "芦笙节，卓沃发难，揭露曼冉滥用禁术，治男童之事公开，村民各执一词；诺朗当众讲述母亲以禁术救命之事，大祭司由此得到支持":
    "At the Lusheng festival Zhod Vos made her move, exposing Mait Rangs’s abuse of forbidden arts; the boy’s treatment became public and the villagers were divided. Nof Langb told everyone how Nof Langb’s mother had once saved a life with forbidden arts, and the high priestess won support.",
  "曼冉与卓沃冲突，借力尼亚得胜，将卓沃控制起来，政教又合一":
    "Mait Rangs clashed with Zhod Vos and, with Nyax Vos’s help, won, putting Zhod Vos under control; rule and rite were one again.",
  "男童死亡、化为毒尸，适逢父母探望，曼冉灭口":
    "The boy died and became a poison corpse just as his parents came to visit; Mait Rangs silenced them.",
  "天一教掌握曼冉灭口一事，要挟她相助，始渗透村寨；曼冉意图摆脱压制，转而改造、控制男童以自强":
    "The Tianyi Order, knowing about the silencing, blackmailed Mait Rangs into helping it and began to infiltrate the village; Mait Rangs, wanting to throw off its grip, turned to remaking and controlling the boy to strengthen herself.",
  // 743
  "太原冬日，闵方城路遇犯错被打、跌坐道边不能动的少年伶工杜徵，拉他起来——二人初见":
    "Winter in Taiyuan: Min Fangcheng came upon Du Zheng, a boy musician who had been beaten for a mistake and sat collapsed by the road, unable to move, and pulled him up: their first meeting.",
  "龙飞大营换防，程凯以攒了数年的饷钱欲赎姗娘（昔年爱护过他的歌伎），岚川云代他进歌楼寻人，未果——「好心是他的事，走与不走，走得走不得，却是我的事」；程凯又自往城郊寻阿玉的坟，未得":
    "When the Longfei Camp changed garrison, Cheng Kai wanted to use the pay he had saved for years to buy out Shanniang (a singing girl who had been kind to him long ago); Lanchuan Yun went into the house of song to see her on his behalf, but it came to nothing; Shanniang said, “Being kind is his affair. Whether I leave, and whether I can leave, is mine.” Cheng Kai then went alone to look for A-Yu’s grave outside the city, and did not find it.",
  "秋，天杀营斥候数人奉冷天锋之意访凌雪阁，互通软甲丸药诸物；岚川云与高堑切磋，败于青苔湿石之滑——「有人看石头，有人看青苔吧」；湖畔高垣论青苔与硬芯：「一年到头啊，从不见消萎，比人心人命都坚久。」后岚川云见其腰牌篆字：怀青":
    "Autumn. Several scouts of the Heavenly Slayer Corps visited the Lingxue Pavilion at Leng Tianfeng’s wish, to exchange soft armour, pills and the like; Lanchuan Yun sparred with Gao Qian and lost, slipping on a wet, mossy stone: “Some people look at the stone; some look at the moss.” By the lake Gao Yuan talked of moss and a hard core: “All year round it never withers. It outlasts people’s hearts and people’s lives.” Afterwards Lanchuan Yun saw the seal characters on his waist token: Huaiqing.",
  "天一教叛乱，控制村寨":
    "The Tianyi Order rose and took control of the village.",
  // 744
  "曼冉试图完全控制男童；娜留或已唤醒男童意识（待定）":
    "Mait Rangs tried to take complete control of the boy; Nax Liuf may already have woken his consciousness (undecided).",
  // 745
  "春，两公主和亲奚、契丹，自雁门出关，吕定仪协理各项文书；同年秋两蕃各杀公主举兵南下，吕定仪谏军师闭锁关城、候平卢节度先动以免正面接敌——“可是圣人想听的？”不用，遂有雁门关之役之痛":
    "Spring: two princesses went out through Yanmen in marriage alliances with the Xi and the Khitan, and Lü Dingyi helped with all the paperwork. That autumn both peoples killed their princesses and marched south. Lü Dingyi urged the strategist to seal the pass and wait for the Pinglu Military Commission to move first rather than meet the enemy head-on (the strategist: “But is that what the emperor wants to hear?”). He was not heeded, and so came the grief of the Battle of Yanmen Pass.",
  "夏，楼准因狼牙偷袭坠塔身亡，楼谊十五岁临危受命，升灯、报讯、点兵、值守如常，塔没有乱；靳氏父子念旧缘北上赴塔协助，靳沉白析文书为死伤、器械、粮秣、值守、传讯五类复核册，事后留塔为书手；与楼谊合写殉塔报文并器械损耗申领，文书落到关内吕定仪手中，拨料不曾拖沓":
    "Summer: Lou Zhun fell from the tower to his death in a Langya surprise attack, and Lou Yi, fifteen, took up the charge in the crisis; the lamps were raised, the signals sent, the men mustered and the watches kept as usual, and the tower did not fall into disorder. Remembering the old connection, Jin Chenbai and his father came north to help at the tower; Jin Chenbai sorted the documents into five verification ledgers (dead and wounded, equipment, grain and fodder, watches, signals), and stayed on afterwards as the tower’s scribe. With Lou Yi he wrote the report on those who died at the tower and the requisition for lost equipment; the papers reached Lü Dingyi inside the pass, and the materials were issued without delay.",
  "狄元恪（十五岁）与同窗自城外别院谈书论道归，太原城门见守卒欺侮一半大流民孩童；同窗劝「何必费口舌」「你是要考进士的，不是当武夫」，他说「哀民多艰，也在于看没看见。谁让他现在我眼前呢」，翻身下马喝止，以「怠惰公务」折服守卒；孩童抱着两个硬馒头不哭不瑟缩，他以糕点相易不成——「你的东西我不抢」——带回府中。父兄不喜，谓结交野童污了门风，他说「逐出这孩子便是逐我」，终得收留。孩童樊璋，云州流民：村寨为边骑冲突所焚，阿爷死于乱兵，阿娘病死岚州道旁葬于浅丘，随逃民车队入太原，籍券俱佚；一直留着阿娘的犬牙吊坠——「娘说是玉做的，看着却像石头」「玉就是石头，切磋琢磨，人才知道好」":
    "Di Yuanke (fifteen) was riding back with his classmates from a retreat outside the city, where they had been discussing books and the Way, when at the gate of Taiyuan he saw the guards bullying a half-grown vagrant child. His classmates urged him to let it be (“Why waste your breath?” “You’re meant to sit the jinshi examinations, not be a soldier”); he said, “Grieving at the hardships of the people also depends on whether you see them. And he happens to be right in front of my eyes,” swung down from his horse, shouted the guards off and cowed them with a charge of neglecting their duty. The child, clutching two hard buns, neither cried nor cowered; Di offered cakes in exchange and was refused (“I won’t take what’s yours”), and took the child home. His father and brothers disapproved, saying that befriending a stray disgraced the family; he said, “Throw this child out and you throw me out,” and in the end the child was taken in. The child was Fan Zhang, a refugee from Yunzhou: his village burned in a frontier skirmish, his father killed by marauding soldiers, his mother dead of illness by the road in Lanzhou and buried in a shallow mound, he had come into Taiyuan with a train of refugee carts, all papers lost, and still kept his mother’s dog-tooth pendant: “Mother said it was jade, but it looks like stone.” “Jade is stone. It takes cutting and polishing before people see it is good.”",
  "岚川云再至西域，处置红衣教之乱；陆晚月探查龙门红衣教魔鬼城，两人再遇；岚川云以弓弦扼杀陆隐":
    "Lanchuan Yun went to the Western Regions again to deal with the Hongyi Order’s uprising; Lu Wanyue, investigating the Hongyi Order’s Devil’s City at Longmen, met her again; Lanchuan Yun strangled Lu Yin with a bowstring.",
  "凌雪阁内乱 高堑身亡 高垣冤狱 宣杨入门":
    "Strife within the Lingxue Pavilion; Gao Qian died; Gao Yuan was wrongly imprisoned; Xuan Yang entered the Pavilion.",
  "天宝四载，李俶任外阁主，李林甫卸任、退控凌雪楼，朝堂宰相与太子之争在阁中一样上演；高堑受凌雪楼策动窃机枢府密卷，兄弟山坡缠斗，高垣重伤夺卷；外阁清剿宰相势力、收厌兵院，高堑转战玄鹤别院被捕，臼齿藏毒自尽，死前诬告兄长；高垣冤狱严刑，唯答「没有，不是我」——后宰相隐匿之弟子自首、证据确凿，冤白获释":
    "In the fourth year of Tianbao Li Chu became Master of the Outer Pavilion, and Li Linfu stepped down and withdrew to control the Lingxue Tower; the court’s struggle between the chancellor and the crown prince played out inside the Pavilion as well. Incited by the Lingxue Tower, Gao Qian stole secret scrolls from the Jishu Bureau; the brothers fought it out on a hillside, and Gao Yuan, badly hurt, took the scrolls back. As the Outer Pavilion purged the chancellor’s faction and took over the Yanbing Court, Gao Qian fought his way to the Xuanhe Lodge and was caught; he killed himself with poison hidden in a molar, and before he died falsely accused his brother. Gao Yuan was wrongly imprisoned and harshly tortured, and answered only, “No. It wasn’t me.” Later a hidden disciple of the chancellor’s gave himself up, the evidence was conclusive, and Gao Yuan was cleared and released.",
  "章仇兼琼开步头路（云南通交州），筑安宁城；东爨诸部起兵杀筑城者，朝廷令蒙归义（皮逻阁）弹压，南诏借爨氏内斗吞并其地。底色：蒙萍换蛊即为此局；安宁盐路由此断绝，卓沃的盐成了筹码":
    "Zhangchou Jianqiong opened the Butou road (linking Yunnan with Jiaozhou) and built Anning; the Eastern Cuan tribes rose and killed the builders, the court ordered Meng Guiyi (Piluoge) to put them down, and Nanzhao used the Cuan’s internal strife to swallow their lands. Background: Meng Ping’s exchange of gu belongs to this situation; the Anning salt road was cut from this point, and Zhod Vos’s salt became a bargaining chip.",
  "成都一夜：佩留交割特殊药材后灭口南诏商人蒙萍；央馨为截换天一教药材冒充商人入仓库，死于唐哲小组伏击，尸身随仓库焚毁，唐哲私藏其驱蚊小球；杨钊扣下布料与药材，照单全收。监视唐哲者为谁，暂未定":
    "A night in Chengdu: after handing over special medicinal herbs, Pet Liuf silenced the Nanzhao merchant Meng Ping; Vangb Xenb, posing as a merchant to get into the warehouse and switch the Tianyi Order’s herbs, died in an ambush by Tang Zhe’s team, and her body burned with the warehouse; Tang Zhe secretly kept her little mosquito-repelling ball. Yang Zhao impounded the cloth and the herbs and took the lot. Who was watching Tang Zhe is not yet settled.",
  "成都一夜：副队头唐青阳带一火人从平戎城到成都领军器，那一夜宿在城里。仓库起火，他赶到时火场干净得不像火场；他在城里报了所见，最后鲜于仲通结了案，写的是失火。回平戎城后跟程铎说起，程铎说：上面说是失火，就是失火。他记住了那种干净，九年后在唐哲队里又见了一次，才知道是谁收拾的":
    "The night in Chengdu: Tang Qingyang, a deputy squad leader, brought a squad from Pingrong to Chengdu to draw weapons, and that night they stayed in the city. The warehouse caught fire; by the time he got there the scene was too clean to be the scene of a fire. He reported what he had seen in the city, and in the end Xianyu Zhongtong closed the case, writing it down as an accidental fire. Back at Pingrong he told Cheng Duo about it, and Cheng Duo said: if those above say it was a fire, it was a fire. He remembered that cleanness, saw it once more nine years later in Tang Zhe’s team, and only then knew who had cleaned up.",
  "大决战：成都一夜后天一教缺药、毒尸狂暴；曼冉放出卓沃共抗天一教，圣童出手终结毒尸；大祭司一方损失惨重，娜留或死于此役；卓沃趁虚而入":
    "The decisive battle: after the night in Chengdu the Tianyi Order ran short of medicine and its poison corpses ran wild; Mait Rangs let Zhod Vos out to fight the Cult together, and the Holy Child struck the blow that ended the poison corpses. The high priestess’s side suffered heavy losses, and Nax Liuf may have died in the fighting; Zhod Vos took her chance.",
  "秋，杨钊携春彩入京，另携郫地蜀货「可直万缗」，分赠诸姊并称「此章仇公所赠也」；得出入禁中，改金吾兵曹参军。杨钊时为章仇兼琼推官，由采访支使鲜于仲通引荐。底色：春彩即成都一夜被扣之布（入京月份不详，系于仲秋）":
    "Autumn: Yang Zhao came to the capital with spring silks, and with goods of Shu from Pi “worth ten thousand strings of cash”, which he gave out among the Yang sisters, his cousins, saying “these are gifts from Lord Zhangchou”; he gained entry to the palace and was made Administrator of the Military Service Section of the Imperial Insignia Guard. Yang Zhao was then a judge under Zhangchou Jianqiong, recommended by Xianyu Zhongtong, assistant to the surveillance commissioner. Background: the spring silks were the cloth impounded on the night in Chengdu.",
  "雁门关之役":
    "The Battle of Yanmen Pass.",
  "雁门关之役中，荔非承烈于薛直身侧力战不敌，重伤倒地眼看统帅战亡，敌以为其已死未挨补刀；后闵方城出关寻回统帅遗体，将他一同拉回，捡得一命。745年后荔非始有「无功」之字，自谓不能护卫统帅、原该殉死却又得活，无功愧悔":
    "In the Battle of Yanmen Pass Lifei Chenglie fought hard at Xue Zhi’s side and was overwhelmed; badly wounded and down, he watched the Commander fall. The enemy took him for dead and did not finish him off. When Min Fangcheng went out beyond the pass to bring back the Commander’s body, he dragged Lifei back too, and his life was saved. It was after 745 that Lifei took the courtesy name Wugong, “no merit”: having failed to protect the Commander, he said, he ought to have died with him and yet had lived; no merit, only shame.",
  "皇甫惟明攻石堡城，败（史）；程凯压阵断后，押尾射杀蕃兵，指尖崩裂，由此成名":
    "Huangfu Weiming attacked Shibao Fortress and was defeated (historical); Cheng Kai held the line and covered the retreat, shooting down Tibetan soldiers from the rear until his fingertips split, and made his name by it.",
  "闵方城成名之战（薛直大丧见次年暮春）":
    "Min Fangcheng’s battle of renown (for Xue Zhi’s great funeral, see late spring of the following year).",
  "雁门关之役后军队重组间，吕定仪擢为团级长官之一（破阵营三团）——薛直时代始有所成就，而后来为中流砥柱，跨越苍云军两个阶段":
    "In the reorganisation after the Battle of Yanmen Pass, Lü Dingyi was raised to be one of the regimental commanders (Third Regiment, Rank-Breaker Corps). He had first made his mark in Xue Zhi’s day and later became a pillar of the army, spanning both of the Cangyun Army’s eras.",
  "军队重组间，荔非承烈与吕定仪、闵方城同列擢为破阵营团级长官（二团），后有「旧三柱」之说；薛褚擢为二团副官——为尊者讳，营中单以字行，隐去薛姓，称季韬将军":
    "In the reorganisation Lifei Chenglie was raised to regimental commander in the Rank-Breaker Corps (Second Regiment) alongside Lü Dingyi and Min Fangcheng; later people spoke of them as “the Old Three Pillars”. Xue Chu was raised to deputy of the Second Regiment; out of reverence for the dead, the camp called him only by his courtesy name and left out the Xue: General Jitao.",
  "关山阵亡后，闵方城关外一战成名，悍勇近乎不要命；景惠时新寡，初次试以静坐陪伴之法近他，他只许她处置伤口（只许她医，不许她说话）":
    "After Guan Shan fell in battle, Min Fangcheng made his name in a fight beyond the pass, fearless almost to the point of wanting to die; Jing Huishi, newly widowed, first tried to come near him by simply sitting with him in silence, and he would let her do nothing but tend his wounds (she might treat him, but not talk).",
  "薛褚南下绛州（薛氏族地），携信与遗物回族、交割薛直身后事，并在族宅正堂廊下听见「名声之论」；遂未久留，翌年1月即回雁门":
    "Xue Chu went south to Jiangzhou, the Xue clan’s seat, carrying letters and relics back to the clan and settling Xue Zhi’s affairs, and under the eaves of the main hall of the clan house he overheard “the talk about reputation”. He did not stay long, and was back at Yanmen in the first month of the next year.",
  // 746
  "岚川云回长安顺路见了高垣一面，而后返洛；程凯与岚川云遍寻城郊坟岗，仍认不出阿玉葬处，遂以西北军功所得赏赐为她立衣冠冢，二人同访，互相讲述旧事（741年程凯曾问程广，程广亦不知）":
    "On her way back to Chang’an Lanchuan Yun saw Gao Yuan once, then returned to Luoyang. Cheng Kai and Lanchuan Yun searched every grave mound outside the city and still could not tell where A-Yu was buried, so with the rewards from his merit in the north-west he raised a cenotaph for her; they visited it together and told each other about the past (in 741 Cheng Kai had asked Cheng Guang, and Cheng Guang did not know either).",
  "天宝五载，道永入少林为沙弥——年少家中变故，雨夜独自摸爬拜山门，到了却不敲门，只站着，一夜风雨；掌事师兄出来问「小小年纪，一个人上来的？」答「不是，同我一道还有风雨，和竹声」。几年劳作后，经首座请度牒为僧":
    "In the fifth year of Tianbao Daoyong entered Shaolin as a novice. After a misfortune in his family as a boy he had crawled and climbed alone up to the monastery gate on a rainy night, and when he got there did not knock but only stood, all night in the wind and rain. The senior brother in charge came out and asked, “So young, and you came up alone?” He answered, “No. The wind and the rain came with me, and the sound of the bamboo.” After some years of labour the head monk obtained an ordination certificate for him and he became a monk.",
  "高垣冤白后年余，身体心力渐复，遣守千秋楼、处理迎来送往；此后回机枢府主理文书、讲授后辈——腿伤永在，而人永远立得笔直":
    "In the year or so after he was cleared, Gao Yuan slowly recovered in body and spirit and was sent to keep the Qianqiu Tower, receiving and seeing off visitors; afterwards he went back to the Jishu Bureau to run its records and teach the younger ones. His leg injury never left him, but he always stood perfectly straight.",
  "五毒线收尾：佩留任大祭司并统领村寨，政教又合一；曼冉与尼亚远走；诺朗带佩留回蝴蝶泉；卓沃再次远走，带商队另开盐路（盐路已断、男子只能代掌，佩留握圣童与染法）":
    "The Wudu thread closes: Pet Liuf became high priestess and ruled the village, rule and rite one again; Mait Rangs and Nyax Vos went far away; Nof Langb took Pet Liuf back to Butterfly Spring; Zhod Vos left again, taking a caravan to open a new salt road (the salt road was cut and a man could only rule in her stead, while Pet Liuf held the Holy Child and the dyeing methods).",
  "陆晚月在成都遇见唐哲":
    "Lu Wanyue met Tang Zhe in Chengdu.",
  "程钧弱冠，离家出游":
    "Cheng Jun came of age and left home to travel.",
  "暮春，残军回城、整理一切；薛直大丧，较战亡迟了几个月：三军衣缟，从冰室请出匆匆掩藏的遗骨装裹停放；送殡路上跑上来一只白狮子——丧毕，统帅方携闵方城、吕定仪、薛褚等往霸刀山庄":
    "Late spring: the battered army came back to the fortress and set everything in order. Xue Zhi’s great funeral came some months after his death in battle: all three armies wore mourning white, and his remains, hastily hidden in the ice cellar, were brought out, dressed and laid out; on the road of the funeral procession a white lion came running up (two little girls from a players’ troupe dressed as a white lion). When the funeral was over the Commander took Min Fangcheng, Lü Dingyi, Xue Chu and others to Badao Manor.",
  "程宇生于庭州":
    "Cheng Yu was born at Tingzhou.",
  "苍云访霸刀，宴席狼牙刺客使毒针，吕定仪替闵方城挡下，残毒损伤心脉；后闵方城与统帅先返雁门固防，吕定仪、薛褚留霸刀":
    "The Cangyun Army visited Badao Manor; at the banquet a Langya assassin used a poisoned needle, and Lü Dingyi took it in Min Fangcheng’s place; the residual poison damaged his heart. Min Fangcheng and the Commander went back first to strengthen Yanmen’s defences; Lü Dingyi and Xue Chu stayed at Badao Manor.",
  "霸刀山庄切磋：苍云选残军强将展示武功阵法，闵方城露功夫，薛褚亦出手而风头为其所盖；擂台向外，以名换粮（吕定仪：统帅带你来，为让人瞧着苍云不是没了人，这事在你身上，不在我）":
    "Sparring at Badao Manor: the Cangyun Army chose strong officers from its battered ranks to show its martial arts and formations; Min Fangcheng showed his skill, and Xue Chu fought too but was outshone. The challenge bouts were for outside eyes, reputation traded for grain (Lü Dingyi: the Commander brought you to show people the Cangyun Army isn’t out of men; this rests on you, not on me).",
  "陆晚月去西南":
    "Lu Wanyue went to the south-west.",
  "吕定仪、薛褚等从霸刀押车（霸刀援助苍云粮资）回雁门，于灵丘岔道口击败劫车胡人":
    "Lü Dingyi, Xue Chu and others escorted the carts from Badao Manor (Badao’s aid to the Cangyun Army in grain and supplies) back to Yanmen, defeating Hu raiders who tried to seize them at the Lingqiu fork.",
  "章仇兼琼入朝为户部尚书，「诸杨引之也」":
    "Zhangchou Jianqiong went to court as Minister of Revenue: “it was the Yangs who brought him in”.",
  "夏末，雁门关之役后残营乏治文事者，吕定仪毒伤劳顿常常躺倒；荔非承烈换防前营亲巡雁塔，见靳沉白所理关外地形与敌袭路线复盘，带回其名——“看着倒像又一个状元”；靳沉白传入关城，入吕定仪帐下为借调书手。“文书过手，便有过手之责。”":
    "Late summer. After the Battle of Yanmen Pass the battered garrison was short of anyone to handle its paperwork, and Lü Dingyi, worn down by his poison wound, was often laid up. Lifei Chenglie, rotating to the forward camp, inspected Yanta Tower in person, saw Jin Chenbai’s reconstruction of the terrain beyond the pass and the routes of the enemy raids, and brought back his name: “He looks like another zhuangyuan to me.” Jin Chenbai was summoned into the pass fortress and joined Lü Dingyi’s staff as a seconded scribe. “A document that passes through your hands is your responsibility.”",
  // 747
  "夏，靳沉白随军中人事整编，同伤退兵士、裁撤杂役、补入新卒一一谈话、核发赏赐银饷，无声无息，没有一处闹到帐前；补入名册，正式纳入破阵营。楼谊雁塔箱笼相送——“到底塔上已经不缺写字的人。缺的那些，也不是你留下便能补得了的。”":
    "Summer. In a reorganisation of the army’s personnel, Jin Chenbai talked one by one with soldiers retiring wounded, with dismissed odd-job men and with new recruits, and checked and paid out their rewards and pay, without a sound: not one case was carried to headquarters. Entered on the rolls, he formally joined the Rank-Breaker Corps. Lou Yi sent his trunks over from Yanta Tower: “The tower is not short of people who can write any more. And what it is short of isn’t something you could make up by staying.”",
  "深秋，苍云北上出援，行军至云中永宁寺遇敌袭；寺内民丁召集授甲，荔非承烈亲取敌酋。邱鸿（时年十五六，寺中俗家弟子）先不受刀、只以盾缘引卸来势护住大殿，后为护后院药棚于西廊出刀杀敌——生平第一刀；薛褚率士接防西门——「我早知多留一把刀有用」。战后老僧授沉香珠串：「非常之世，有非常之法。持戒并非不杀，是从此而止。」自出刀杀贼后，邱鸿再未抬头看佛面":
    "Late autumn. Marching north to bring relief, the Cangyun Army was attacked at Yongning Monastery in Yunzhong. The monastery’s lay men were mustered and issued armour, and Lifei Chenglie took the enemy chief himself. Qiu Hong (fifteen or sixteen, a lay disciple of the monastery) at first would not take a blade and only turned the enemy’s blows aside with the rim of a shield to protect the main hall; later, to protect the medicine shed in the rear court, he drew a blade in the west cloister and killed: the first of his life. Xue Chu led men to take over the west gate: “I always knew a spare blade would come in handy.” After the fighting an old monk gave him a string of agarwood beads: “Extraordinary times have their extraordinary ways. Keeping the precepts is not never killing; it is stopping, from here on.” After he drew his blade on the bandits, Qiu Hong never again raised his eyes to the Buddha’s face.",
  "敌袭数日后，荔非欲带邱鸿入军，与薛褚帐中之争——「燕帅是叫你我物色，没叫咱们拉壮丁」「就是说我拉壮丁我也干……那是个铁骨衣的苗子，带回去，你收他当弟子」；邱鸿布衣至帐前请从，「面目莹净，像玉柱覆粗麻」，随军入苍云，拜薛褚门下修铁骨衣":
    "Some days after the attack Lifei wanted to take Qiu Hong into the army, and argued it out with Xue Chu in the tent: “The Commander told you and me to look out for likely men, not to press-gang them.” “Call it press-ganging if you like, I’ll still do it … the boy is made for the Iron-Bone Mantle. Bring him back and take him as your disciple.” Qiu Hong came to the tent in plain cloth to ask to follow, “his face clean and clear, like a jade pillar wrapped in coarse hemp”, went with the army into the Cangyun Army, and became Xue Chu’s disciple in the Iron-Bone Mantle.",
  "岚川靖彦多年忧思苦劳，病重；程凯同岚川云回长安探望——靖彦见那青年将军，心中了然，眼带欣慰，临终问女儿「当年你说逝者不安，如今可以想想，他们安了没有，你又安了没有」，又言「东归渡海之事，要在于你了」；身故后程凯协助处置丧仪，陪伴宽解（同年，程凯生父程广殁于小勃律之役——安西与长安，同一年）":
    "Years of worry and toil left Lanchuan Jingyan gravely ill; Cheng Kai went back to Chang’an with Lanchuan Yun to see him. Seeing the young general, Jingyan understood, and there was gladness in his eyes; dying, he asked his daughter, “You said back then that the dead were not at peace. Now you can think about it: are they at peace? And are you?” and said, “Crossing the sea back east is up to you now.” After his death Cheng Kai helped with the funeral and stayed by her to comfort her. (That same year Cheng Kai’s own father Cheng Guang died in the Little Balur campaign: Anxi and Chang’an, the same year.)",
  "程广殁于小勃律之役（随高仙芝；史：是年高仙芝讨小勃律）":
    "Cheng Guang died in the Little Balur campaign (under Gao Xianzhi; historically, Gao Xianzhi campaigned against Little Balur that year).",
  "伽罕巴尔节，玛奈丽随村人往圣山途中被吐蕃游骑掳走":
    "At the Gahambar festival, on the way to the Holy Mountain with the villagers, Māneli was carried off by Tibetan raiders.",
  "雁门关之役后首次恢复考课：闵方城于擂台坐实团主官之位（是年正授团主官，称将军；745.11 重组时已署理一团）；营中无人能敌，擂台实为确认之仪式，苍云着意以之为榜样；「原来这就是先统帅看中过的人」之闲话自此每年一回（与757年恢复考课成对：一立柱，一倒柱；薛褚或为其对手之一，输作寻常比试，赛后无人提起）（月份推定）":
    "The first merit review since the Battle of Yanmen Pass: in challenge bouts Min Fangcheng made his place as regimental commander certain (that year he was formally appointed regimental commander and called General; since the reorganisation of 745.11 he had been acting head of the First Regiment). No one in the camp could match him, so the bouts were really a ceremony of confirmation, and the Cangyun Army deliberately held him up as an example; from then on, every year, there was talk of “so this is the man the late Commander had his eye on”. (It pairs with the restored review of 757: one raises a pillar, the other brings one down. Xue Chu may have been one of his opponents, losing as in an ordinary bout; no one mentioned it afterwards.)",
  "天宝六载十月，玄宗幸骊山温泉宫，改名华清宫；宫在会昌县——天宝二年析新丰、万年置，七载省新丰入之、更名昭应。许秋生乡里新丰即此县（王维《少年行》首句「新丰美酒斗十千」）（注：是月沈含英随师赴天策府，皇帝正在许秋生家乡）":
    "In the tenth month of the sixth year of Tianbao, Xuanzong went to the hot-spring palace on Mount Li and renamed it the Huaqing Palace. The palace lay in Huichang County, formed in the second year of Tianbao from parts of Xinfeng and Wannian; in the seventh year Xinfeng was merged into it and the county renamed Zhaoying. Xu Qiusheng’s home of Xinfeng was this county (the first line of Wang Wei’s “Song of Youth”: “The fine wine of Xinfeng, ten thousand cash a measure”). (In this month Shen Hanying went with his master to the Tiance Command, while the emperor was in Xu Qiusheng’s home county.)",
  "沈含英随师至天策府为侍医（竞猎前夕；注：是月玄宗幸华清宫，校猎观军容之使当自骊山东来）；初到即遇天弓营吐泻、被疑下药，程凯挡箭护之，岚川云暗访搜证为其洗冤":
    "Shen Hanying went with his master to the Tiance Command as attending physician (on the eve of the hunt; note: that month Xuanzong was at the Huaqing Palace, so the envoy sent to watch the hunt and review the troops would have come east from Mount Li). On arrival he ran straight into an outbreak of vomiting and diarrhoea in the Heavenly Bow Corps and was suspected of poisoning; Cheng Kai took an arrow to shield him, and Lanchuan Yun quietly gathered evidence and cleared his name.",
  // 748
  "冬夜，吕定仪膝痛难忍，靳沉白以家传药油为其按治——“将军授业，我理当趋奉。”“我授不了你的业。”“将军不逐我，我见一分，便是一分。”":
    "A winter night. Lü Dingyi’s knee pain was past bearing, and Jin Chenbai treated it with his family’s medicinal oil: “The General is teaching me; it is only right that I wait on him.” “I can’t teach you what you need.” “So long as the General doesn’t send me away, whatever I see is that much gained.”",
  "薛褚带邱鸿在帐下一二年，武功已成而永宁寺中所见天赋不复现——武学天生带一层「知止」，越发将自己锁住；对练分明可以翻势，只把人推出去不补那一下，老兵骂「这么打，上阵害死自己」；薛褚问「怎不出刀」，答「他退了，我想便已够了，再下去怕是重手」，薛褚无法逼迫":
    "Xue Chu kept Qiu Hong on his staff for a year or two; his skill was formed, but the gift seen at Yongning Monastery did not appear again. His fighting had an inborn sense of “knowing when to stop” that locked him in more and more: in sparring, when he plainly could turn the bout, he only pushed his man away and never struck the follow-up, and the veterans cursed: “Fight like that in battle and you’ll get yourself killed.” Xue Chu asked, “Why didn’t you strike?” He answered, “He fell back. I thought that was enough. Any more and it would have been too heavy a hand.” Xue Chu could not force him.",
  "约此年，灵隐寺一度被神策围、天竺僧袭扰，叶添灯送信函纸有毒，中毒昏厥，藏剑山庄遣弟子相助，僧护他至山庄解毒疗伤；避居期间见弟子练剑，看得路都走不动，僧携之投帖诉其向往之心——藏剑先纳他入庄内书院，做洒扫整理，庄内寺院两头跑；僧为其改名「叶添灯」，取字「照」":
    "Around this year Lingyin Monastery was for a time surrounded by the Shence Army and harried by monks from India; Ye Tiandeng, carrying a letter on poisoned paper, was poisoned and fainted. Cangjian Manor sent disciples to help, and a monk took him to the manor to have the poison drawn and his injuries treated. While sheltering there he watched the disciples at sword practice so raptly he could hardly walk on, and the monk took him to present a letter setting out his longing; Cangjian first took him into the manor’s academy to sweep and keep things in order, running back and forth between manor and monastery. The monk renamed him Ye Tiandeng, “adding a lamp”, with the courtesy name Zhao, “to shine”.",
  "高垣受命整理名籍抚恤，档案中惊见恩人黍梁即宣康——宣杨生父；再赴江南至巢县芜皋村，知其妻儿早死于课税酷吏；淮扬据点查旧抚恤，任上之人早作宰相钉子被拔、记档无存；临河酒肆有人掷来沾污的老妪木簪相胁——「该知道的人，我自会让她知道。那时你若乱动，也别怪我」":
    "Ordered to put the rolls and death benefits in order, Gao Yuan found to his shock in the files that his rescuer Shuliang was Xuan Kang, Xuan Yang’s father. He went south again to Wugao Village in Chao County and learned that the wife and son had long since died under the taxes and the harsh officials. At the Huaiyang station he looked into the old death benefits: the man who had held the post had long ago been pulled out as the chancellor’s plant, and no record was left. In a riverside tavern someone tossed him an old woman’s soiled wooden hairpin as a threat: “The one who ought to know, I’ll see that she knows. If you make a wrong move before then, don’t blame me.”",
  "冷天锋致信荐医，沈含英赴凌雪阁为高垣诊治髋伤腿疾——燃香推拿，累年瘀结逼出无源之泪，「水流冲过积石，石上又生苔藓。藓老且厚，流水不过，春草不生」；宣杨窗纸戳洞窥见。后沈含英返府断言：负伤致残兼神思郁结，纵然用药只恐难久，「兴许…就这几年了」":
    "On a letter of recommendation from Leng Tianfeng, Shen Hanying went to the Lingxue Pavilion to treat Gao Yuan’s hip injury and leg ailment. With burning incense and massage he forced out years of knotted stasis and with it tears that came from nowhere: “Water runs over piled stones, and moss grows on the stones. When the moss is old and thick, the water cannot pass, and no spring grass grows.” Xuan Yang poked a hole in the window paper and watched. Back at the Command Shen Hanying gave his verdict: injuries that had left him crippled, with a mind weighed down and knotted; even with medicine he was unlikely to last long: “Maybe… only these few years.”",
  "夫人病亡于北庭（程钊生母侍疾），归葬洛阳":
    "The principal wife died of illness at Beiting (Cheng Zhao’s mother nursed her), and was taken back to Luoyang for burial.",
  "皮逻阁卒，子阁罗凤嗣，以其子凤伽异为阳瓜州刺史":
    "Piluoge died and his son Geluofeng succeeded him, making his own son Fengjiayi Prefect of Yangguazhou.",
  "首个天长节（是年千秋节改名，八月初五），齐晟与玛奈丽同台献演":
    "The first Tianchang Festival (the Qianqiu Festival was renamed that year; the fifth day of the eighth month): Qi Sheng and Māneli performed on the same stage.",
  // 749
  "草场少年木苏（mosur，族语约「威风」之意）随游奕队伍追逃骑，控马认路快过老兵，被带回帐前；报名而族音含混，左右暗笑「倒像将军那条猎犬的名儿」；狼牙将领捏其下巴细看，如相一匹新得的马——「你该有汉姓」，随行青毡汉人（军师）接口取「朔」字——「便像……像这风」。有了大名连朔，收为义子（「假子」，与所谓八千曳落河差不多一回事）；将领言并安置其父母亲眷，起初确也迁居，然奚众惯于游牧，徒有居所无以生活，仍时时出入边境":
    "A boy of the grasslands, Musu (mosur, roughly “imposing” in his people’s tongue), rode with a patrol in pursuit of fleeing horsemen, handling his horse and finding the way faster than the veterans, and was brought back before the tent. When he gave his name the sounds of his tongue came out blurred, and those around snickered that it sounded “like the name of the general’s hound”. The Langya general took him by the chin and looked him over, as if appraising a newly acquired horse: “You should have a Han surname.” A Han man in a green felt cloak at his side (the strategist) took up the word and chose the character shuo, the north wind: “Like… like this wind.” Given the formal name Lian Shuo, he was taken in as an adopted son (a “false son”, much the same thing as the so-called eight thousand yeluohe, the “stalwarts”, surrendered Tongluo, Xi and Khitan warriors whom An Lushan kept as adopted sons). The general said he would settle the boy’s parents and kin too; at first they did move, but the Xi were used to herding on the move and a dwelling alone gave them no living, so they still crossed back and forth over the border.",
  "沈含英侍医期满，离天策府返谷；程凯套车送行——「这东西两京之隔能有多远，往后要见，不难」":
    "Shen Hanying’s term as attending physician ended, and he left the Tiance Command for the Valley; Cheng Kai harnessed a cart to see him off: “How far apart can the two capitals be? If we want to meet again, it won’t be hard.”",
  "程钧带酒赴天策探程凯，劝他不要过于执着家族认同":
    "Cheng Jun brought wine to the Tiance Command to visit Cheng Kai, and urged him not to hold on so hard to the family’s acknowledgement.",
  "上元夜，老人一席话，齐晟不复去寻玛奈丽，随戏班回乡":
    "On the night of the Lantern Festival, after a few words from an old man, Qi Sheng stopped looking for Māneli and went home with the troupe.",
  "天策府公开招兵，纳人不拘出身，齐晟入府（是年五月停折冲府鱼书，六月哥舒翰拔石堡城，史）":
    "The Tiance Command recruited openly, taking men whatever their background, and Qi Sheng joined (historically, that year the fish tallies of the garrison militia were suspended in the fifth month, and Geshu Han took Shibao Fortress in the sixth).",
  "许秋生之母重症风寒，未能撑过这一冬（沈含英自天策府侍医期满返谷后那一冬）；新年夜沈含英留下相陪——「我们说的一心赴救，其实…常常并不落在那个『救』字上」":
    "Xu Qiusheng’s mother, gravely ill with a chill, did not live through the winter (the winter after Shen Hanying’s term as physician at the Tiance Command ended and he went back to the Valley); on New Year’s Eve Shen Hanying stayed to keep him company: “What we call giving ourselves wholly to saving others… often doesn’t land on the word ‘saving’ at all.”",
  // 750
  "连朔（十七八岁）派驻雁门关外与苍云前营对峙的狼牙营垒，在一游骑队伍中；所部一面防御苍云，一面监管附近牧场奚人；牧人受迫不敢与关内过分亲近，苍云仍不时以医药、盐糖稍稍援助，景惠时作为医官不顾危险一再来往，还给连朔治过伤——「他心里都知道，所以宁把手松一松，从不过酷」":
    "Lian Shuo (seventeen or eighteen) was posted with a patrol troop to the Langya stockade beyond Yanmen Pass that faced the Cangyun Army’s forward camp; the unit both guarded against the Cangyun Army and kept watch over the Xi herders on the nearby pastures. Under pressure, the herders dared not be too friendly with the men inside the pass, but the Cangyun Army still sent them a little medicine, salt and sugar from time to time, and Jing Huishi, as army physician, went back and forth again and again in spite of the danger, and once treated Lian Shuo’s wounds: “He knew all of it, so he would rather loosen his grip a little; he was never cruel.”",
  "狄元恪入太原守军历练，樊璋随行照料护卫——背甲、递箭、磨刀。狄府延请的多年在安西劲旅中的武官授其骑战，惯使马槊、步下环首刀；那槊要轻、韧、结实，能悬平，直握冲阵不折，从选材起总要三年才得":
    "Di Yuanke went into the Taiyuan garrison for experience, and Fan Zhang went with him to look after and guard him: carrying his armour, handing him arrows, sharpening his blades. An officer who had served for years in the crack troops of Anxi, engaged by the Di household, taught him mounted fighting: he favoured the cavalry lance on horseback and the ring-pommel blade on foot. The lance had to be light, supple and strong, able to hang level and to be held straight into a charge without breaking; from the choosing of the wood it always took three years.",
  "岚川云三去西域（750–752），随杨宁会明教求和解（杨宁明教受掌），程凯同行；程凯见陆南信（互动待定）；而后征南诏、天一教等":
    "Lanchuan Yun’s third tour to the Western Regions (750–752): she went with Yang Ning to meet the Mingjiao and seek a reconciliation (Yang Ning’s audience with the Mingjiao), and Cheng Kai went too; Cheng Kai met Lu Nanxin (what passed between them: undecided); then came the campaigns against Nanzhao, the Tianyi Order and others.",
  "约此年，朱鹭（十五六岁）随坊中前辈至藏剑；晚秋湖畔落雪，叶添灯罩伞与她讲神光立雪、断臂求法、雪为之红的公案——「天降红雪，可神光断臂求法，似乎并非天降…是人为」；同至灵隐寺饭堂吃素面。此后二人也有些往来":
    "Around this year Zhu Lu (fifteen or sixteen) came to Cangjian with seniors of the Qixiu House. Snow fell by the lake in late autumn, and Ye Tiandeng, holding an umbrella over her, told her the story of Shenguang standing in the snow, cutting off his arm to seek the Dharma, and the snow turning red for it: “Red snow fell from heaven, but Shenguang cutting off his arm to seek the Dharma doesn’t seem to have fallen from heaven… people did it.” They went together to the refectory at Lingyin Monastery and ate plain noodles. After that the two saw something of each other.",
  "玛奈丽随猛兽被长安城外一处神策军营接收，几沦为军妓":
    "Māneli was taken in, along with her wild beasts, by a Shence Army camp outside Chang’an, and was almost made an army prostitute.",
  "杨国忠荐鲜于仲通为剑南节度使，史称其「性褊急，失蛮夷心」。底色：745 年成都一夜扣货、结案经他之手，是他失蛮夷心的最早一例":
    "Yang Guozhong recommended Xianyu Zhongtong as Military Commissioner of Jiannan; the histories say he was “narrow and hasty by nature, and lost the hearts of the Man and Yi”. Background: the impounding of goods on the night in Chengdu in 745, and the closing of that case, went through his hands: the earliest instance of his losing the hearts of the Man and Yi.",
  "考课擂台：邱鸿（二团，荔非麾下，薛褚所带）对力大分山老兵，于铁骨中沉扛，始终不还手，判负（或平）；闵方城于台下见其「没有想」之静，将其要到身边为弟子，此后私下传授（记录作败而实为天赋，与757年擂台成镜像；系年约750，月份推定）。薛褚自身铁骨衣是一面平实硬盾而身无芒刺，带兵立阵极好，个体武学成就不及闵方城；理想铁骨衣是闵方城那样——金身不破，罡劲化于周身，形似黑火，触之即伤":
    "A challenge bout at the merit review: Qiu Hong (Second Regiment, under Lifei, trained by Xue Chu) faced a powerful Mountain-Splitting veteran, took it all in the Iron-Bone, never struck back, and was judged the loser (or it was a draw); watching from below, Min Fangcheng saw the stillness of “not thinking” in him, asked to have him at his side as his disciple, and from then on taught him privately (recorded as a loss though it was really a gift; it mirrors the challenge bout of 757). Xue Chu’s own Iron-Bone Mantle was a plain, hard shield with no thorns on it: superb for drawing up and holding troops, while his own achievement in the martial arts fell short of Min Fangcheng’s. The ideal Iron-Bone Mantle was Min Fangcheng’s: a golden body that cannot be broken, its force spread through the whole frame, like black fire, wounding whoever touches it.",
  "是年冬，云南太守张虔陀对阁罗凤多所征求，不应则辱骂、密奏其罪；阁罗凤发兵陷云南（姚州），杀虔陀，取夷州三十二（月份不详，系于孟冬）":
    "That winter Zhang Qiantuo, governor of Yunnan, made many demands on Geluofeng, cursing him when he did not comply and secretly memorialising his crimes; Geluofeng raised troops, took Yunnan (Yaozhou), killed Qiantuo and seized thirty-two Yi prefectures.",
  // 751
  "骆父（约天宝初年明经出身，历浙东县尉、州曹参军）调赴太原府任中层州县职事，家眷随任北迁，落脚太原城中；骆文璧时在天台山南坡、台州海边一带，未随父北上。太原狄氏为坐地望族，骆父公事上与之往来，两家逐渐知根知底":
    "Luo’s father (who had passed the mingjing examination early in Tianbao and served as a county sheriff in eastern Zhejiang and as a prefectural administrator) was transferred to a middle-ranking post in Taiyuan, and the family moved north with him and settled inside the city; Luo Wenbi, then on the southern slopes of Mount Tiantai and along the coast of Taizhou, did not go north with her father. The Di of Taiyuan were the great local family, Luo’s father had official dealings with them, and the two families gradually came to know each other well.",
  "玛奈丽逃出军营投红衣教，时已有身孕":
    "Māneli escaped from the army camp and joined the Hongyi Order; she was already with child.",
  "安禄山兼河东节度使（治太原，辖天兵、大同、岢岚、横野军与云中守捉），代州雁门在其辖内；苍云自此为河东境内唯一不听命于安禄山之兵":
    "An Lushan took on the Hedong Military Commission as well (seated at Taiyuan, with the Tianbing, Datong, Kelan and Hengye Armies and the Yunzhong Garrison Post under it), and Yanmen in Daizhou came under him; from then on the Cangyun Army was the only force in Hedong that did not take his orders.",
  "陈瑞和由庐州乡贡解送入京，应进士举屡试不第；许秋生赴岑菡家府雅集，与之相谈，荐其入万花":
    "Chen Ruihe was sent up to the capital as a provincial candidate from Luzhou and sat the jinshi examination again and again without passing; at a gathering at Cen Han’s family house Xu Qiusheng talked with him and recommended him to Wanhua.",
  "鲜于仲通率兵八万分两道征南诏，战于西洱河，士卒死者六万，仲通仅以身免，杨国忠掩败叙功；程铎所部即护仲通突围撤回的那支人。唐青阳为队头，带弩队断后；队里十几个青神同乡，回来的连他只有三个。尸首带不回来，他把名字写在母亲织的素绢上交程铎报阵亡；报上去的阵亡数随后被改小，程铎照上面给的数报了——两人第一次分歧，没有吵，唐青阳从此自己留一份名单":
    "Xianyu Zhongtong led eighty thousand men in two columns against Nanzhao and fought at the Xi’er River; sixty thousand of the soldiers died and Zhongtong barely escaped with his life, while Yang Guozhong covered up the defeat and reported merit. Cheng Duo’s unit was the one that protected Zhongtong in breaking out and falling back. Tang Qingyang, as squad leader, took the crossbow squad to cover the rear; of the dozen or more men from Qingshan in the squad, only three came back, himself included. The bodies could not be brought back, so he wrote their names on plain silk his mother had woven and gave it to Cheng Duo to report them killed; the number of dead reported was then made smaller, and Cheng Duo reported the number he was given from above: the first time the two disagreed. They did not quarrel; from then on Tang Qingyang kept a list of his own.",
  "西洱河之役，南诏大军将段俭魏破鲜于仲通八万众，战场在下关一带；段韶为段俭魏子侄，在南诏一方——程铎、天策在南诏一侧的镜像":
    "In the battle of the Xi’er River the Nanzhao grand general Duan Jianwei defeated Xianyu Zhongtong’s eighty thousand, the battlefield lying around Xiaguan; Duan Shao, a younger kinsman of Duan Jianwei’s, was on the Nanzhao side: the mirror image of Cheng Duo and the Tiance Command on the Tang side.",
  "西洱河之后，阁罗凤收唐兵尸筑京观，北臣吐蕃；吐蕃封为「赞普钟」，号「东帝」，赐金印。又刻碑国门，称叛唐「非本心」（月份不详，系于战后；德化碑以 752 年为赞普钟元年）":
    "After the Xi’er River, Geluofeng gathered the bodies of the Tang soldiers into a jingguan, a mound of the dead, and turned north to submit to Tibet; Tibet named him Zanpuzhong, the Tsenpo’s younger brother, with the title Emperor of the East and a gold seal. He also carved a stele at the gate of his kingdom saying that his break with the Tang was “not of his own heart” (the Dehua Stele counts 752 as the first year of Zanpuzhong).",
  "八九月，安禄山发所节度三道兵马出击契丹，以奚二千骑为向导；过平卢千余里至土护真河遇大雨，昼夜兼行三百余里至契丹牙帐；弓弩筋胶皆湿松弛，大将何思德请按甲息兵，禄山怒欲杀之，何请免死为前锋，因形貌与禄山相像，契丹争击杀之而士气大振；奚兵见契丹得势复叛，与之合击，唐军大败，禄山马中箭、折冠失履，仅以二十余骑遁入师州，归罪于突厥与河东兵马使":
    "In the eighth and ninth months An Lushan sent out the troops of the three commands under him against the Khitan, with two thousand Xi horsemen as guides. More than a thousand li past Pinglu, at the Tuhuzhen River, they met heavy rain, and marched day and night another three hundred li to the Khitan royal camp; the bows and crossbows were wet, their sinew and glue gone slack. His general He Side asked him to halt and rest the troops; An Lushan in a rage wanted to kill him, and He begged to be spared and to lead the vanguard instead. Because he looked like An Lushan, the Khitan fought one another to kill him, and their spirits soared; the Xi, seeing the Khitan gaining, turned against the Tang again and attacked with them. The Tang army was routed; An Lushan’s horse was hit by an arrow, he lost his hat and his shoes, and fled into Shizhou with barely twenty riders, laying the blame on the Türks and the Commander of Troops from Hedong.",
  "连朔所在游骑被点为向导入列讨契丹；见奚兵复叛、局面翻覆，不欲卷入出尔反尔之事，趁乱引麾下十数骑奔回平卢上报；平卢守将史定方从别处并得其情，认连朔虽则逃遁、实是不与狡竖翻覆之辈为伍，授一骑尉；旋随狼牙将领同平卢精兵二千往救，契丹兵退，禄山得免":
    "Lian Shuo’s patrol troop was picked to serve as guides in the campaign against the Khitan; when he saw the Xi turn again and everything overturned, he wanted no part in such double-dealing, and in the confusion led his dozen or so riders back to Pinglu to report. Shi Dingfang, the general holding Pinglu, had the same news from elsewhere and judged that though Lian Shuo had fled, he was really one who would not throw in with turncoats, and gave him the merit title of Commandant of Cavalry; soon after he went with the Langya generals and two thousand picked Pinglu troops to the rescue, the Khitan withdrew, and An Lushan escaped.",
  "征南诏无人应募，杨国忠遣御史分道捕人、枷送军所；强征之兵逃入唐门，程铎不追，由此识得唐百翮——五个月前他刚从西洱河活着回来。夜里给押来的眉州人指路往唐门去的是唐青阳——青神的丝卖到那里，那里收人。这批人尚未交割，名字没进军籍，不算「征名已定」，程铎知道是谁指的路，什么也没说；在唐门地界接人、天亮前把人藏干净的，是二十五岁的唐哲带的小组，两人那夜没说话":
    "No one answered the call to arms against Nanzhao, and Yang Guozhong sent censors out on every road to seize men and send them to the army in cangues; the press-ganged men fled into the Tang Clan’s lands, and Cheng Duo did not pursue them, and so came to know Tang Baihe, who five months before had come back alive from the Xi’er River. The one who showed the way to the Tang Clan that night to the men brought in from Meizhou was Tang Qingyang: the silk of Qingshan was sold there, and they took people in there. These men had not yet been handed over and their names were not on the military register, so they were not yet “conscripts whose names are entered”; Cheng Duo knew who had shown the way and said nothing. The team that met the men on Tang Clan ground and hid them all before daybreak was led by Tang Zhe, then twenty-five; the two did not speak that night.",
  "冬，岚川云随天策征南诏入蜀；次年仲夏班师，秋归府，与程凯成婚（成婚事详752年秋条）（按：年纪文本作「752年夏赴蜀中」，作者已定从 Notion：751年十一月入蜀、752年五月班师）":
    "Winter: Lanchuan Yun went into Shu with the Tiance Command’s campaign against Nanzhao; the army came back in midsummer of the next year, and in autumn she returned to the Command and married Cheng Kai (for the marriage, see the entry for autumn 752).",
  "杨国忠遥领剑南节度使，人在长安":
    "Yang Guozhong held the Military Commission of Jiannan in absentia, staying in Chang’an.",
  // 752
  "三月，安禄山又发蕃、汉步骑二十万击契丹，欲雪去秋之耻；会朔方节度副使李献忠（突厥阿布思）惧为禄山所害，帅所部大掠仓库、叛归漠北；禄山遂顿兵不前，气怒不平，为免失颜面，命杀手中奚、契丹俘虏，纳为边功":
    "In the third month An Lushan again sent two hundred thousand foot and horse, Han and non-Han, against the Khitan, to wipe out the shame of the autumn before; just then Li Xianzhong (the Türk Abusi), Vice Military Commissioner of Shuofang, fearing An Lushan meant him harm, plundered the granaries with his men and went back over to the northern steppe. An Lushan halted his army, seething, and to save face had his Xi and Khitan prisoners killed and counted as frontier merit.",
  "春夏间，所谓俘虏中多有乱中被掳的平民牧户，连朔父亲叔伯并不少族亲皆枉死其中；连朔仍派驻雁门外狼牙营，起先不知，一两个月后族亲失去联络，到关外毡帐一看，已空空如也——从此幻灭；碍于母家亲眷尚在营中被掌握，不能即刻「降敌」":
    "In spring and summer many of these so-called prisoners were herding families seized in the confusion, and Lian Shuo’s father, his uncles and many of his kin died wrongly among them. Lian Shuo was still posted to the Langya camp outside Yanmen and at first did not know; after a month or two he lost touch with his kin, went to the felt tents beyond the pass, and found them empty. From then on he was disillusioned; but his mother’s family were still in the camp, in the Langya Army’s hands, and he could not “go over to the enemy” at once.",
  "夏，连朔渐与关岳有联络（也许通过景惠时），暗中向苍云守军传递信息；关岳见其才能与心思，私下相见劝降，知其顾虑，提出援救其母、镇上寻差事定居，如能策反从骑，家人皆无后顾之忧——连朔经过一次这种事已不大相信，「但关岳似乎全然信任他」，连同家人安排都一一想好":
    "Summer: Lian Shuo gradually got in touch with Guan Yue (perhaps through Jing Huishi) and secretly passed information to the Cangyun garrison. Guan Yue, seeing his ability and how his mind worked, met him privately and urged him to surrender; knowing his worries, he offered to rescue his mother and find the family work and a home in the town, so that if he could bring his riders over, his family would have nothing to fear. Lian Shuo, having been through this once, hardly believed it any more, “but Guan Yue seemed to trust him completely”, and had thought out every arrangement for the family too.",
  "九月初，连朔与关岳暗谈事为军师耳目所见；军师帐中对质——「你只管跑罢」「倘我报知将军，你要如何」「要紧的是，我要让上头这些狗东西出出血，最好偿命。……你一个写字的，不跑能干什么？」连朔打定主意纳投名状，策反游骑小队一部，不从欲声张者帐中手刃，纵火生乱脱身；关岳在外接应，更借势杀入敌营，生擒其义父狼牙将领，营地狼牙折损相当——策反加擒敌，关岳得首功；连朔入关城后方知连义父都叫人活着拿下了，一时念头复杂":
    "Early in the ninth month the strategist’s eyes and ears saw Lian Shuo’s secret talk with Guan Yue, and he was confronted in the strategist’s tent: “Just run, then.” “And if I report you to the general, what will you do?” “What matters is that I make these dogs above us bleed, and pay with their lives if I can. … You’re a man who writes. What can you do but run?” Lian Shuo made up his mind to bring a proof of allegiance: he turned part of his patrol troop, killed with his own hand in the tent those who would not follow and meant to raise the alarm, and set fires to make chaos and get away. Guan Yue, waiting outside to meet him, used the moment to strike into the enemy camp, took Lian Shuo’s adoptive father, the Langya general, alive, and the Langya losses at the camp were heavy; for the turning of the riders and the capture, Guan Yue had the first merit. Only after he was inside the pass fortress did Lian Shuo learn that even his adoptive father had been taken alive, and for a while his thoughts were tangled.",
  "冬，柳戎与闵方城战阵初见——闵方城叫她捧雪止血、重伤犹能暴起杀敌，柳戎由此生了好感":
    "Winter: Liu Rong first met Min Fangcheng on the battlefield. He told her to pack snow on the wound to stop the bleeding, and badly hurt as he was, he could still rise up suddenly and kill; from then on Liu Rong had a soft spot for him.",
  "狄元恪到天策府参与军演，与秦徽（天策府秦颐岩侄女）相识，彼此看见，有情，就在一样的弓马骑战里；到底相处未久，二人心思又都在从军建功上，仍旧两地，只书信传于北都、东都之间。樊璋随行":
    "Di Yuanke went to the Tiance Command for the military exercises and came to know Qin Hui (niece of Qin Yiyan of the Tiance Command). They saw each other and there was feeling between them, in the very same archery, riding and mounted combat; but they had not known each other long, and both had their minds set on soldiering and earning merit, so they stayed apart, with only letters passing between the Northern Capital and the Eastern Capital. Fan Zhang went with him.",
  "约此年（天宝最后的太平年月），骆文璧从台州沿海某渔港出海——或随出海方士船队，或于外海中转岛遇蓬莱门人被引入，细节留白，给人物保留一段不可追溯的空白。此后数年在岛上度过她最自由的岁月，学了一身与天台山完全不同的功夫，并有一只海雕相随，自蓬莱起便默契配合":
    "Around this year (the last peaceful years of Tianbao), Luo Wenbi put to sea from a fishing harbour on the Taizhou coast, perhaps with a fleet of magicians setting out on the ocean, perhaps meeting Penglai disciples on an island where ships put in far out at sea and being brought in by them; the details are left blank, keeping for the character a stretch of time that cannot be traced. She spent the next few years on the island, the freest of her life, learned a whole body of martial arts quite unlike Mount Tiantai’s, and was followed by a sea eagle that worked with her in close understanding from Penglai on.",
  "歌莉生于长安郊外灾民营地——玛奈丽随红衣教施援染疾，产后血不止，母女终得活":
    "Golī was born in a refugee camp outside Chang’an: Māneli had caught a fever giving aid with the Hongyi Order and bled without stopping after the birth, but mother and daughter both lived in the end.",
  "天策在蜀征南诏间（751.11–752.5），马翊与五毒女子彩瑶相识生情。马翊是伏波将军马援之后——马援当年征武陵五溪蛮，病死军中，「马革裹尸」语出其口：祖先的死地与情人的故土，同在西南群山":
    "During the Tiance Command’s campaign against Nanzhao in Shu (751.11–752.5), Ma Yi met Ncaik Ya, a woman of the Wudu Order, and they fell in love. Ma Yi was a descendant of Ma Yuan, General Who Calms the Waves; Ma Yuan had campaigned against the Man of the Five Streams of Wuling and died of illness with the army, and the saying “to be wrapped in a horse’s hide” comes from his mouth: the place where his ancestor died and the homeland of the woman he loved lay in the same south-western mountains.",
  "程凯中天一教刀，五毒以蛊解毒；岚川云护送伤员遇伏，陆晚月解围；程凯至成都养伤，与兄程铎重逢；魏谦查实通敌案，牵连程铎部下：被叫去问话的部下里有唐青阳，他不是内鬼，却说不清751年那一夜去了哪里；程铎具状担保，没问他那夜去了哪里":
    "Cheng Kai was cut by a Tianyi Order blade, and the Wudu Order cured the poison with gu; Lanchuan Yun was ambushed escorting the wounded, and Lu Wanyue came to her aid. Cheng Kai went to Chengdu to recover and met his brother Cheng Duo again. Wei Qian uncovered a case of collusion with the enemy that implicated Cheng Duo’s men: among the men called in for questioning was Tang Qingyang, who was not the traitor but could not account for where he had been that night in 751; Cheng Duo put his name to a guarantee for him, and never asked where he had been that night.",
  "剑南兵破吐蕃、南诏联军（即本年六月杨国忠奏捷之役）":
    "The Jiannan troops defeated the combined armies of Tibet and Nanzhao (the battle behind Yang Guozhong’s report of victory in the sixth month of this year).",
  "天平胜宝四年闰三月，藤原清河遣唐使团拜朝受节刀，旋即出航；四月九日东大寺大佛开眼供养":
    "In the intercalary third month of the fourth year of Tenpyō-shōhō, Fujiwara no Kiyokawa’s embassy to the Tang had its audience, received the sword of authority and soon set sail; on the ninth day of the fourth month came the eye-opening ceremony of the Great Buddha of Tōdai-ji.",
  "林叶矢之父（造像工匠）随藤原清河使团入唐，习佛教造像技艺，此后留唐未归（时叶矢约两岁）":
    "Hayashi Kyōya’s father (a sculptor of images) went to the Tang with Fujiwara no Kiyokawa’s embassy to learn the craft of Buddhist image-making, and stayed in the Tang and never went home (Kyōya was then about two).",
  "蜀中定情（岚川云、程凯）":
    "Love declared in Shu (Lanchuan Yun and Cheng Kai).",
  "仲夏，天策自成都班师；离蜀前正值炎夏，岚川云与程凯在路边糕坊吃冰酥酪（《思停》序章）":
    "Midsummer: the Tiance Command’s army set out home from Chengdu. Before they left Shu, in the height of summer, Lanchuan Yun and Cheng Kai ate iced junket at a cake shop by the road (the prologue of “A Halting Thought”).",
  "六月甲子，杨国忠奏：吐蕃以六十万众救南诏，剑南兵击破之于云南，拔隰州等三城，俘六千三百人——天宝间剑南对南诏唯一一次报捷，「六十万」或有虚报，意在遮掩前年西洱河六万人之败。底色：752.3 剑南兵破吐蕃南诏联军即此奏背后的真仗，魏谦在其中；他日后得知自己打赢的仗被拿去遮掩西洱河六万人之败——与「天宝四年那场捷报是假的」是同一根刺，第二次扎进去":
    "On the jiazi day of the sixth month Yang Guozhong reported that Tibet had sent six hundred thousand men to rescue Nanzhao, that the Jiannan troops had beaten them in Yunnan, taken three towns including Xizhou, and captured six thousand three hundred men: the only report of victory over Nanzhao from Jiannan in all the Tianbao years. The “six hundred thousand” was perhaps inflated, meant to cover up the defeat of sixty thousand at the Xi’er River two years before. Background: the battle of 752.3, in which the Jiannan troops beat the Tibetan and Nanzhao allies, was the real fighting behind this report, and Wei Qian was in it; when he learned later that a battle he had won had been used to cover up the defeat of sixty thousand at the Xi’er River, it was the same thorn as “the victory report of the fourth year of Tianbao was false”, driven in a second time.",
  "程凯、岚川云成礼前休假同往洛阳——先拜祭程凯生母衣冠冢，再入南市：程凯塞与她枣泥糕，岚川云三镖赢得鸠车；遇才别师门学磨镜的叶添灯，择无铭菱花镜——「我看这最好，没那些聒噪」，叶添灯以镜相赠为贺，并为新赐角弓取名「藏器」——君子藏器于身，待时而动；程凯弓弦裂瓜，「弓嘛，怎么用、怎么爱惜它都是弓」（按：作者已定752年五月仲夏自蜀班师，七月同往洛阳，九月成婚）":
    "On leave before their wedding, Cheng Kai and Lanchuan Yun went to Luoyang together: first to pay their respects at the cenotaph of Cheng Kai’s mother, then into the Southern Market. Cheng Kai pressed date-paste cakes on her, and Lanchuan Yun won a toy dove cart with three darts. They met Ye Tiandeng, newly out of his master’s school to learn mirror polishing, and chose an unsigned mirror with a water-chestnut-flower rim: “I think this is the best; none of that noise.” Ye Tiandeng gave the mirror as a wedding gift and named the newly bestowed horn bow Cangqi, “keeping the tool hidden”: the gentleman keeps his tool on his person and waits for the moment to act. Cheng Kai split a melon with the bowstring: “A bow’s a bow, however you use it, however you look after it.”",
  "秋，连朔以狼牙降将入苍云":
    "Autumn: Lian Shuo joined the Cangyun Army as a surrendered Langya officer.",
  "秋，程凯与岚川云成婚——二人少年相识，许多坎坷，互相欣赏，至此终成。后岚川云曾有一次怀孕，但在激烈打斗中流产":
    "Autumn: Cheng Kai and Lanchuan Yun were married. They had known each other since they were young and been through many hardships, admiring each other all the while; now at last it came about. Later Lanchuan Yun was once with child, but miscarried in a fierce fight.",
  "南诏屡寇边，蜀人请杨国忠赴镇；国忠入蜀途中，因李林甫病危召回；以崔圆为剑南留后":
    "Nanzhao raided the frontier again and again, and the people of Shu asked Yang Guozhong to come and take charge; on his way into Shu he was recalled because Li Linfu was gravely ill, and Cui Yuan was made acting Military Commissioner of Jiannan.",
  "连朔旧部八九游骑被打散自新兵营受训，两三人不惯苍云军规、屡屡迟误，留字条与连朔琢磨出逃（「过去的长官也还在被审，兴许审完了连咱们一块杀了都未可知」），连朔未直言制止，只说「尚看不明，暂且不要再提」；字条先一步被营中士兵截下，压在闵方城手里未发作——有爱惜其心性天分之意。后三人夤夜缒城出逃，被守城士兵擒下，以逃兵论处，闵方城下令斩之；营中传出「不该纳降」的话，连朔自危以为将被驱逐，闵方城只说一句：「各人论各人的。」而字条从此成为把柄，通敌叛逃随时可以编排在他头上":
    "Eight or nine of Lian Shuo’s old riders were broken up and put through the recruits’ camp; two or three of them, unused to the Cangyun Army’s discipline and often late, left a note for Lian Shuo working out a way to desert (“The old commander is still being questioned; when they’re done they may kill us along with him, who knows”), and Lian Shuo did not forbid it outright, saying only, “It’s too early to tell. Don’t speak of it again for now.” The note was intercepted first by soldiers in the camp and ended up in Min Fangcheng’s hands, where he let it lie: he valued Lian Shuo’s character and gifts. Later the three let themselves down the wall at night to desert, were caught by the wall guards and dealt with as deserters, and Min Fangcheng ordered them beheaded. Talk went round the camp that “we should never have taken their surrender”, and Lian Shuo, fearing for himself, thought he would be driven out; Min Fangcheng said only, “Each man answers for himself.” And from then on the note was a hold on him: collusion with the enemy and desertion could be pinned on him at any time.",
  "狼牙将领堡内审讫，推出斩首；连朔与其从骑听令到场看着，见一同被擒的还有几个副将，军师不在其中，暗暗从鼻子里笑了一声。死前军将大笑——「好小子，我养的狗倒来啃我身上的肉，好。就怕你不知道，贰姓的叛徒是什么下场。」声音在雪地上久久不散，鬼魂似地":
    "When the questioning of the Langya general inside the fort was done, he was led out to be beheaded; Lian Shuo and his riders were ordered to stand and watch. Among those captured with him were several of his deputies, but the strategist was not among them, and Lian Shuo gave a quiet snort through his nose. Before he died the general laughed aloud: “Good lad. The dog I raised comes to gnaw the meat off my bones. Good. Only you may not know yet what becomes of a traitor who serves two masters.” The voice hung over the snow a long time, like a ghost.",
  "高垣病亡 宣杨承其衣钵——冬，伤病复发呕血而亡，时身畔无人，房中炭火燃尽；临终留信，具言宣杨身世与「我等人物又究竟为何定要存续下去」之问；民女转交围巾，宣杨抱之往墓林，树下红花覆雪，雪又覆红花":
    "Gao Yuan died of illness and Xuan Yang took up his mantle. In winter his old injuries flared up again and he died coughing blood, alone, the charcoal in his room burned out; he left a letter setting out Xuan Yang’s origins and the question “why must people like us go on surviving at all?”. A village woman passed on his scarf, and Xuan Yang carried it to the burial grove: red flowers under the trees covered the snow, and the snow covered the red flowers.",
  // 753
  "年初，关岳安排连朔母亲与姑母安置广武城（族中男丁大都因禄山掳掠奚地换边功而枉死）；二人汉话一般，仍以畜牧为生，时入山中射猎，毛皮野味卖与汉人。移居之初，广武百姓与巡防士兵敌意甚大，轻则泼水、倾倒垃圾于门前，重则有人闯入侵扰；连朔怒寻巡逻士兵理论，士兵只说从未听说，搪塞过去，无处说理":
    "Early in the year Guan Yue settled Lian Shuo’s mother and aunt at Guangwu Fortress (most of the men of the clan had died wrongly when An Lushan seized people in the Xi lands to trade for frontier merit). The two women spoke only passable Chinese and still lived by herding, sometimes going into the hills to hunt and selling the furs and game to the Han. When they first moved in, the people of Guangwu and the patrolling soldiers were bitterly hostile: at the least, water splashed and rubbish tipped at their gate; at worst, people breaking in to harass them. Lian Shuo angrily sought out the patrol soldiers to have it out with them; they only said they had never heard of it and fobbed him off, and there was nowhere to take his case.",
  "荔非最先提醒闵方城：连朔此人是祸，「留着他，对你不好」；吕定仪问理由，荔非几乎笑出——「这看一眼就知道，还用一二三？」吕定仪摇头：「野狗而已，阿城迟早镇得住，只看想不想。」荔非两手一摊":
    "Lifei was the first to warn Min Fangcheng that Lian Shuo was trouble: “Keep him, and it won’t go well for you.” When Lü Dingyi asked why, Lifei almost laughed: “You can see it at a glance. Does it need one, two, three?” Lü Dingyi shook his head: “He’s just a wild dog. A-Cheng can bring him to heel sooner or later; it’s only whether he wants to.” Lifei spread his hands.",
  "程骞生于北庭":
    "Cheng Qian was born at Beiting.",
  "安南都护府何履光自南线出兵击南诏":
    "He Lüguang of the Annan Protectorate attacked Nanzhao from the southern route.",
  "入冬，闵方城便装上广武城巡视（隔段时间自去城上百姓处转转，他知道原先薛直也这样），见连朔家院内木柴散落一地、所剩不多；问哨上士兵，闻「那不过两个牧马儿的女人，何必劳神」——「牧马儿？我也是牧马儿。」士兵汗出如浆跪下请罪。闵方城命此间凡来过城上驻哨而无所作为者尽领军杖，又从自己那拨了炭火木柴过去，此后住处再无人骚扰，而未与连朔主动说一个字；连朔从母亲口中听来人模样方知，过后不久寻机夜谒帐前求见，最后两人以搏斗般相抱倒在风屏后床榻而告终——隐秘私情自此始（按：文档一处作754入冬，然同段又言「那时连朔入营小一年」，兹从关系库私情边753之起点）":
    "As winter came on, Min Fangcheng went up to Guangwu Fortress in plain clothes on his rounds (every so often he went himself to walk among the townsfolk, as he knew Xue Zhi used to); he saw firewood scattered over the ground of Lian Shuo’s family yard, little of it left. When he asked the soldiers at the post, he was told, “They’re only two herding women, why trouble yourself?” “Herders? I’m a herder too.” The soldier broke into a sweat and knelt to beg forgiveness. Min Fangcheng ordered the army staff for every man who had stood watch there and done nothing, and sent charcoal and firewood over from his own share; after that no one troubled the household again, and he never said a word to Lian Shuo himself. Lian Shuo learned of it only from his mother’s description of the visitor, and not long after found a chance to come to the tent at night and ask to see him; in the end the two of them, locked together as if fighting, fell onto the bed behind the screen: the start of their secret affair.",
  // 754
  "秋，父母、岳家并妻子安置蒲州；吕定仪赴蒲州拜谢吕諲，不久归返，又因奔波劳顿伤风咳嗽。荔非问他怎么想起和人连宗去——“九原不啻极边。我念头不住。”":
    "Autumn: having settled his parents, his wife’s family and his wife at Puzhou, Lü Dingyi went to Puzhou to thank Lü Yin (an official of a Puzhou family, later a chancellor); he came back soon after, and the travelling gave him a chill and a cough. Lifei asked him what had possessed him to join his line to another man’s clan: “Jiuyuan is nothing short of the farthest frontier. My mind won’t rest.”",
  "蚕月，再征南诏，兵源仍靠强征（具体方式待核）。程铎留守成都发兵：州县押来的人到军所由他点验入册，名字一进册即「征名已定」。他派押官唐青阳去眉州押人，额子里有青神一里的人——唐青阳的从弟、邻家的儿子、当年教他认蚕的老人的孙子，时值蚕户一年里最离不得人的时候。唐青阳在押回成都的路上、点验入册之前把人放了（751年那一夜，他学会了那道门槛在哪里），自己没有回营：他把十几个人从名册上抹掉，把自己的名字留在了上面。他的拒绝是乡土的拒绝，程铎的服从是军人的服从（月份不详，系于蚕月）":
    "In the silkworm month there was another campaign against Nanzhao, and the troops still had to be pressed. Cheng Duo stayed to hold Chengdu and send out the troops: the men brought in by the prefectures and counties were checked and entered on the rolls by him at the army post, and once a name was on the roll the man was a “conscript whose name is entered”. He sent Tang Qingyang as escort officer to bring men from Meizhou, and the quota included men from one ward of Qingshan: Tang Qingyang’s cousin, the neighbour’s son, the grandson of the old man who had taught him to know silkworms, at the very time of year a silkworm household could least spare anyone. On the road back to Chengdu, before they were checked and entered, Tang Qingyang let them go (that night in 751 he had learned where that threshold lay), and did not go back to the camp himself: he wiped a dozen or so men from the roll and left his own name on it. His refusal was a countryman’s refusal; Cheng Duo’s obedience was a soldier’s obedience.",
  "程铎追唐青阳十五天。《唐律疏议·捕亡》：「诸征名已定及从军征讨而亡者，一日徒一年，一日加一等，十五日绞……主司故纵，与同罪。」751年不追，是因为那些人还不是兵；这一次是兵，而且是他的兵——放了唐青阳，他就没资格点下一个名字。没说出口的一层：抓得越早罪越轻，第八日已是流三千里，他追得急，是在跟十五天赛跑。第三夜，追兵的弩射穿唐青阳右肩，那张弩是唐门造的。唐青阳带着箭伤进了唐门地界，唐哲出面挡下追兵：751年他藏的是程铎不追的人，这一次藏的是程铎非追不可的人。唐门不交人，留后崔圆不会为一个逃兵开罪唐门，唐遐夹在中间。第十五天程铎亲自来了，等到天黑才走，只对唐遐说：「过了今天，他在册上就是死人。」唐遐知道那一层，唐青阳不知道（月份不详，系于蚕月）":
    "Cheng Duo pursued Tang Qingyang for fifteen days. The Tang Code with Commentary, “Arrest and Flight”: “Anyone whose name has been entered for conscription, or who is on campaign with the army, and absconds: one day, a year’s penal servitude, each further day one degree more, fifteen days, strangulation … An official in charge who deliberately lets him go is guilty of the same.” In 751 he had not pursued, because those men were not yet soldiers; this time they were soldiers, and his soldiers: if he let Tang Qingyang go, he would have no right to call the next name. What went unsaid: the sooner a man was caught, the lighter his crime, and by the eighth day it was exile to three thousand li; he pursued hard because he was racing the fifteen days. On the third night a crossbow bolt from the pursuers went through Tang Qingyang’s right shoulder; the crossbow was of Tang Clan make. Tang Qingyang, with the bolt wound, got onto Tang Clan ground, and Tang Zhe came out and stopped the pursuers: in 751 he had hidden men Cheng Duo did not pursue; this time he was hiding a man Cheng Duo had to pursue. The Tang Clan would not give him up, Cui Yuan, the acting Military Commissioner, would not offend the Tang Clan over one deserter, and Tang Xia was caught in between. On the fifteenth day Cheng Duo came himself, waited until dark and left, saying only to Tang Xia: “After today, on the roll he is a dead man.” Tang Xia understood what lay under it; Tang Qingyang did not.",
  "剑南留后李宓率七万击南诏，阁罗凤闭城不战，唐军粮尽、瘴疫与饥饿死者大半，引还时为南诏、吐蕃联军追击，全军覆没；程铎奉命留守成都、负责发兵——他亲手点的名册，没有一个人回来。青神空出来的额子，程铎另点了人补上，那些人也没有回来：唐青阳救下的是他认识的人，替他们去死的是他不认识的人——程铎从没对他说过这句话，这才是两人嫌隙的底":
    "Li Mi, acting Military Commissioner of Jiannan, led seventy thousand men against Nanzhao; Geluofeng shut his gates and would not fight, the Tang army ran out of grain, more than half died of miasmal fevers and hunger, and on the retreat it was pursued by the Nanzhao and Tibetan allies and wiped out. Cheng Duo had been ordered to stay in Chengdu to send out the troops: of the rolls he had called with his own hand, not one man came back. Cheng Duo filled the places Qingshan had left empty by calling other men, and they did not come back either. Tang Qingyang had saved men he knew; men he did not know had died in their place. Cheng Duo never said this to him, and it was the true root of the rift between them.",
  "乱前最后一次考课：连朔在士兵中比试无败，几次三番，吕定仪方下场应之；缠斗三十合，连朔几被锁住，低身斜切欲撞吕定仪右膝旧患；闵方城要拦，荔非先掷皮革手靶，骂「小畜生」；连朔收手，吕定仪不语皱眉。擂台无结果，此后再无重打（三柱与连朔同场之唯一一次；闵方城时已与连朔有私，「要拦」一下不点破）（月份推定）":
    "The last merit review before the rising: Lian Shuo was unbeaten in bout after bout among the soldiers, again and again, until Lü Dingyi stepped down into the ring to meet him. They grappled for thirty rounds; Lian Shuo, nearly locked up, dropped low and cut in at an angle, meaning to crash into the old injury in Lü Dingyi’s right knee. Min Fangcheng moved to stop it, but Lifei got there first, flinging a leather hand target and cursing him for a “little beast”; Lian Shuo held back, and Lü Dingyi frowned and said nothing. The bout had no result and was never fought again (the only time the Three Pillars and Lian Shuo were in the ring together; Min Fangcheng was already involved with Lian Shuo, and his move to stop it is left unexplained).",
  "李宓败后，南诏控制盐源盐池，与吐蕃结盟（至 794 年；月份不详，系于年末）":
    "After Li Mi’s defeat Nanzhao took control of the Yanyuan salt lakes and allied with Tibet (until 794).",
  // 755
  "春，吕希纯生于蒲州，得吕氏庇护教养；吕定仪率军游击雁北，概未得知":
    "Spring: Lü Xichun was born at Puzhou and brought up under the protection of the Lü family; Lü Dingyi, leading his men raiding north of Yanmen, never learned of it.",
  "苍云诈败离雁门（755年初，安史乱前）：留旧部伏于关城，全师西转入朔方天德军—九原一线，归郭子仪麾下，在北境游击狼牙——雁门在河东节度辖内，援、粮、奏报皆在安禄山之手，死守必重蹈745，告发不被信，不战而撤为弃关；唯诈败可留下「败走」之凭而保全全军；南东北皆安禄山之地，唯西入朔方（倾向：军师事先与郭子仪略有暗通，以收拢败军为名）。吕定仪久患风湿心疾，不耐辗转":
    "The Cangyun Army’s feigned defeat and departure from Yanmen (early 755, before the An Lushan Rebellion): it left its old hands hidden in the pass fortress and the whole army turned west into Shuofang, along the Tiande Army–Jiuyuan line, under Guo Ziyi, harrying the Langya Army along the northern frontier. Yanmen lay within the Hedong Military Commission, and reinforcements, grain and reports were all in An Lushan’s hands: to hold it to the death would be to repeat 745; denouncing him would not be believed; to withdraw without a fight would be to abandon the pass. Only a feigned defeat left the record of “a defeat and retreat” and kept the whole army intact. South, east and north were all An Lushan’s ground; only west, into Shuofang, was open (tentatively: the strategist had quietly been in touch with Guo Ziyi beforehand, under cover of gathering in a defeated army). Lü Dingyi, long ill with rheumatism and a weak heart, was ill-suited to the moving about.",
  "春，安史乱前雁门先受袭扰，一时退走关城以图，情况危急一如十年前；闵方城遣连朔为先锋诱敌，连朔领命去，闵方城看着他走，好一会，转头翻出当年逃兵字条，投进炭火烧了——无人看见":
    "Spring: before the An Lushan Rebellion Yanmen was harried first, and the army fell back for a time on the pass fortress to make its plans; the danger was as great as ten years before. Min Fangcheng sent Lian Shuo ahead as the vanguard to draw the enemy out; Lian Shuo took the order and went, and Min Fangcheng watched him go a good while, then turned, dug out the deserters’ note of years before, and threw it into the charcoal fire. No one saw.",
  "二月何千年入奏，请以蕃将三十二人代汉将；天策府闻河北情形暗中整备医药，沈含英携药出谷东来，四月入潼关":
    "In the second month He Qiannian came to court with a memorial asking that thirty-two non-Han generals replace Han generals; hearing how things stood in Hebei, the Tiance Command quietly laid in medicine, and Shen Hanying brought medicine east out of the Valley and reached Tongguan in the fourth month.",
  "薛褚领留守旧部（不足一旅）伏于苍云堡地下武库、冰室与回廊；袭击时狼牙打两蕃旗号，官方记作「两蕃寇雁门，苍云败走」；事后河东节度（安禄山）以「收复雁门」为名，遣大同军所部驻守，纸面上为唐军（安禄山借此又立边功），伏兵所避者名义上是自己人；留守者名簿记作「失散」；九个月不见烟火，武库炉冷，以油石养械，粮食均冷":
    "Xue Chu led the old hands left behind (fewer than a battalion) to hide in the underground armoury, ice cellar and passages of the Cangyun stronghold. In the attack the Langya Army flew the banners of the Two Fan (the Xi and the Khitan), and the official record had it that “the Two Fan raided Yanmen and the Cangyun Army fled”. Afterwards the Hedong Military Commission (An Lushan), in the name of “recovering Yanmen”, sent part of the Datong Army to garrison it: on paper, Tang troops (and another piece of frontier merit for An Lushan), so that those the hidden men were hiding from were, in name, their own side. The names of those left behind were entered on the rolls as “missing”. For nine months no smoke was seen; the armoury forges were cold, the weapons kept with oilstones, and all their food eaten cold.",
  "苍云密报：吕定仪起草、统帅署名，经吕諲递河西节度哥舒翰（避开中书、杨国忠一路，以免卷入杨、安之争）；哥舒翰是年在京中风，家居不出，书遂无下文；吕諲静慎，不肯以一判官之身越级上奏，书压箱箧（无人拒绝、无人出卖；吕定仪至死不知此书可曾被读；书之下落倾向就此沉没）":
    "The Cangyun Army’s secret report: drafted by Lü Dingyi and signed by the Commander, it went through Lü Yin to Geshu Han, Military Commissioner of Hexi (avoiding the Secretariat and Yang Guozhong’s line, so as not to be drawn into the struggle between Yang and An). That year Geshu Han suffered a stroke in the capital and stayed at home, and the letter came to nothing; Lü Yin, quiet and cautious, would not go over his superiors’ heads as a mere administrative assistant, and the letter lay in a chest (no one refused it, no one betrayed it; Lü Dingyi never knew to his dying day whether it had been read; tentatively, the letter simply sank from sight there).",
  "岚川云潼关失子，时沈含英在潼关大营为其诊治，程凯事后赶到":
    "Lanchuan Yun lost a child at Tongguan; Shen Hanying, then in the Tongguan camp, treated her, and Cheng Kai arrived afterwards.",
  "占据期间，连朔母亲与姑母为广武城邻人（昔日泼水偷柴者）藏匿（正文不交代，只在758年广武家宴中见邻人态度之变）":
    "During the occupation Lian Shuo’s mother and aunt were hidden by their neighbours at Guangwu Fortress (the very people who had once splashed water and stolen their firewood) (the story does not say so; it shows only in the neighbours’ changed manner at the Guangwu family dinner of 758).",
  "夏，道永在潼关度化岚川云与程凯未出世之子（文本作「755年夏」，当稍后于四月失子之事）":
    "Summer: at Tongguan Daoyong performed the rites of deliverance for the unborn child of Lanchuan Yun and Cheng Kai.",
  "七月，安禄山表请献马三千匹，每马控夫二人，遣蕃将二十二人部送；河南尹达奚珣疑其有变（按：可接岚川云四月潼关所察马匹网络）":
    "In the seventh month An Lushan memorialised offering three thousand horses, with two grooms to each horse, sent under escort of twenty-two non-Han generals; Daxi Xun, Governor of Henan, suspected a coup.",
  "伏兵地下病亡二人：入秋一人死于疫，初冬一人死于寒病（皆无名，非战死）":
    "Two of the men hidden underground died of illness: one of the plague as autumn came on, one of a sickness of the cold early in winter (both nameless, and not killed in battle).",
  "安禄山起兵后，河东唐军闭东陉关，以拒叛军南下；关城下苍云伏兵未动":
    "After An Lushan rose, the Tang troops of Hedong closed the Eastern Pass to stop the rebels coming south; the Cangyun men hidden beneath the pass fortress did not move.",
  "安禄山反后，杨国忠以身领剑南，令剑南留后崔圆暗中储备，以备幸蜀（月份不详，系于起兵之后）":
    "After An Lushan rebelled, Yang Guozhong took the Jiannan command himself and had Cui Yuan, the acting Military Commissioner, quietly lay in stores against the emperor’s flight to Shu.",
  "高秀岩入寇振武军。吕定仪遭暗害再受毒伤，气力大损，不能负甲兼持盾刀；命靳沉白拟檄书送入敌营，遣人搦战激敌将出阵斗将。孤身持盾立于阵前，身势一斜，肘下寸勾，盾面圆钉吃住辔革，掀翻敌骑；铁盾下沿砸透颈侧甲缝，带血嵌进冻土。靳沉白阵中暗记其招，事后作图记录":
    "Gao Xiuyan raided the Zhenwu Army. Lü Dingyi, struck down by treachery, was poisoned again and his strength badly failed; he could no longer bear armour and wield shield-and-blade together. He had Jin Chenbai draft a challenge to be sent into the enemy camp, and sent men to provoke the enemy general into coming out for single combat. He stood alone before the lines with his shield, his body tilted, a short hook under the elbow, the round studs of the shield face caught the bridle leather and overturned the enemy rider; the lower edge of the iron shield smashed through the gap in the armour at the side of the neck and bit, bloody, into the frozen earth. Jin Chenbai, in the ranks, memorised the moves and drew them up afterwards as a record.",
  "吕定仪身故。收兵后授意靳沉白暂领调度，三日亲巡行营各帐，行走如常；夜归，卧帐不起，数日后逝。遗言唯命靳沉白：战未已，切莫发丧，令胡儿得意。闵方城至营——“你去。”“我不敢。”“别装假。”靳沉白对榻叩首，捧印而走；三团交靳沉白，将旗名号未改":
    "Lü Dingyi died. After the troops were withdrawn he had Jin Chenbai take charge of operations for the time being, and for three days went round every tent of the field headquarters in person, walking as usual; coming back at night, he lay down in his tent and did not rise again, and died some days later. His only last order was to Jin Chenbai: the fighting is not over; on no account announce my death and let the Hu brats gloat. Min Fangcheng came to the camp: “You go.” “I don’t dare.” “Don’t pretend.” Jin Chenbai bowed his head to the ground before the bed, took up the seal and went; the Third Regiment passed to Jin Chenbai, its banner and name unchanged.",
  "天策府被围，府城固守与血战（至次年二月城破）":
    "The Tiance Command was besieged: the Command held fast and fought bloodily (until it fell in the second month of the next year).",
  "封常清赴东京募兵，斫断河阳桥；十二月十二日洛阳陷落":
    "Feng Changqing went to the Eastern Capital to raise troops and cut the Heyang Bridge; on the twelfth day of the twelfth month Luoyang fell.",
  "苍云随郭子仪于振武军败高秀岩、收静边军；吕定仪战后数日身故，遗命秘不发丧，闵方城命靳沉白接掌三团":
    "With Guo Ziyi the Cangyun Army beat Gao Xiuyan at the Zhenwu Army and took the Jingbian Army; Lü Dingyi died some days after the battle, leaving orders that his death be kept secret, and Min Fangcheng had Jin Chenbai take over the Third Regiment.",
  "封常清东京兵败，西奔陕郡，与屯陕之高仙芝弃陕退保潼关，焚太原仓而去，陕郡遂陷；旋为监军边令诚所奏，二将并斩于潼关":
    "Defeated at the Eastern Capital, Feng Changqing fled west to Shan Commandery, and with Gao Xianzhi, camped at Shan, abandoned it and fell back to hold Tongguan, burning the Taiyuan Granary as they left; Shan Commandery fell. Soon after, on the memorial of the Army Monitor Bian Lingcheng, both generals were beheaded at Tongguan.",
  "齐晟自崤山工事随高仙芝、封常清弃陕西撤，退入潼关，亲见二将就戮于关下；天策府自此被留在敌后（注：齐晟755夏接程凯守崤山，见《潼关失子》）":
    "Qi Sheng left the Mount Xiao works with Gao Xianzhi and Feng Changqing, abandoning Shan and withdrawing west into Tongguan, and saw the two generals executed below the pass with his own eyes; from then on the Tiance Command was left behind enemy lines (Qi Sheng had taken over Mount Xiao from Cheng Kai in the summer of 755; see “Losing a Child at Tongguan”).",
  "十二月，郭子仪既于振武军败高秀岩、拔静边军，进围云中；使别将公孙琼岩将二千骑击马邑，拔之，开东陉关（《通鉴》卷217，作者核；站内755.12B「闵方城复马邑、再开东陉」即寄于此）。其时云中随河东入叛军之手（见751.2：云中守捉隶河东节度）":
    "In the twelfth month, having beaten Gao Xiuyan at the Zhenwu Army and taken the Jingbian Army, Guo Ziyi advanced to besiege Yunzhong, and sent his subordinate general Gongsun Qiongyan with two thousand horsemen against Mayi, which he took, opening the Eastern Pass (Zizhi tongjian, juan 217; the site’s 755.12B, “Min Fangcheng took back Mayi and reopened the Eastern Pass”, hangs on this). By then Yunzhong had passed into rebel hands along with Hedong (see 751.2: the Yunzhong Garrison Post came under the Hedong Military Commission).",
  "围云中期间，邱鸿随二团（荔非麾下）在围城军中——747年苍云北上，是来救他的永宁寺；这一回他站在城外，攻的是自己的家乡。正月罢围，随大军回撤（草人所掩护者即此，见756.1D），家乡留与叛军；撤至朔州前后调往东陉，与闵方城会合，二月随赴常山（正文一句话即可：他又一次离开了家；不写入城，不交代家人下落）":
    "During the siege of Yunzhong Qiu Hong was with the Second Regiment (under Lifei) in the besieging army: in 747 the Cangyun Army had come north to save his Yongning Monastery; this time he stood outside the walls, attacking his own home. When the siege was lifted in the first month he fell back with the main army (this was what the straw men covered, see 756.1D), leaving his home to the rebels; around the time they reached Shuozhou he was sent to the Eastern Pass to join Min Fangcheng, and in the second month went with him to Changshan.",
  "奇兵合雁门关城内旧部里应外合，收复雁门（所对者为大同军驻军，起兵后已成叛军）；闵方城复马邑，再开东陉；此役连朔有先登之功":
    "A surprise force, working with the old hands inside the Yanmen pass fortress from within and without, recovered Yanmen (against the Datong Army garrison, which had joined the rising and become rebels); Min Fangcheng took back Mayi and reopened the Eastern Pass; in this battle Lian Shuo had the merit of being first up the wall.",
  "马邑先登之役，连朔自狼牙手中救下马邑民女贺兰（后入女卫营，为景惠时弟子，承静息医帐）":
    "In the battle at Mayi where he was first up the wall, Lian Shuo saved a village girl of Mayi, He Lan, from the Langya Army (she later joined the Women’s Guard Corps, became Jing Huishi’s pupil and inherited her Quiet Breath medical tent).",
  "收复之夜，薛褚所部开门接应，再折数人；武库炉火九月后重燃；薛褚将地下病亡二人报作是夜阵亡（763年验骨之先例，正文不点破）":
    "On the night of the recovery Xue Chu’s men opened the gates to let the attackers in, and lost a few more; the armoury forges were lit again after nine months. Xue Chu reported the two who had died of illness underground as killed in action that night (a precedent for the examination of bones in 763; the story leaves it unstated).",
  // 756
  "安史乱起，太原守御日急；狄元恪最初隶于北都留守，出入军府文移与守城杂务之间——太原调遣兵将、又常纳流民，细小政事总有不到之处，他凡门禁、传驿、军资转输诸务皆肯亲自过问，写成文书，法度整肃，危乱不惧":
    "With the An Lushan Rebellion begun, the defence of Taiyuan grew daily more urgent. Di Yuanke at first served under the Regent of the Northern Capital, moving between the paperwork of the military office and the odd jobs of holding the city. Taiyuan was deploying troops and constantly taking in refugees, and the small business of government always had its gaps; he was willing to see to everything himself, gates, the post service, the transport of military supplies, and to put it in writing, orderly and strict, unafraid in danger and disorder.",
  "中原大乱的消息传到东南沿海，骆文璧自海上归，回到天台山暂住，等待消息——从浙东到太原须经整个淮南、河南，全是两军反复拉锯之地，家人亦宁愿她留在海上或越州老家；浙东在安史之乱中基本未受兵火。她没有经历757年的太原围城":
    "News of the great disorder in the Central Plains reached the south-east coast, and Luo Wenbi came back from the sea and stayed for a time on Mount Tiantai, waiting for news. From eastern Zhejiang to Taiyuan meant crossing the whole of Huainan and Henan, all ground fought over again and again by the two armies, and her family would rather she stayed at sea or at the old home in Yuezhou; eastern Zhejiang was largely spared the fighting of the rebellion. She did not live through the siege of Taiyuan in 757.",
  "程钧游走各地，为程凯捎送消息":
    "Cheng Jun travelled about from place to place, carrying messages for Cheng Kai.",
  "南诏陷越巂（巂州），俘西泸县令郑回；郑回后为南诏王室三代之师，终至清平官（宰相）":
    "Nanzhao took Yuexi (Xizhou) and captured Zheng Hui, magistrate of Xilu; Zheng Hui later became tutor to three generations of the Nanzhao royal house and rose at last to qingpingguan (chancellor).",
  "沈含英、许秋生自师门东出，困于燕都洛阳——正月初一安禄山称帝，颜杲卿被缚天津桥柱遇害；二月府城破后两日内赶至药师观残营":
    "Shen Hanying and Xu Qiusheng came east from their master’s school and were trapped in Luoyang, the capital of Yan: on the first day of the first month An Lushan proclaimed himself emperor, and Yan Gaoqing was tied to a pillar of the Tianjin Bridge and killed. In the second month, within two days of the Command’s fall, they reached the remnant camp at the Yaoshi Abbey.",
  "天宝十五载正月初一，安禄山于洛阳称大燕皇帝":
    "On the first day of the first month of the fifteenth year of Tianbao, An Lushan proclaimed himself emperor of Great Yan at Luoyang.",
  "颜杲卿、袁履谦等先行押抵洛阳，缚天津桥柱支解（李庭泽未同批，见三月条）":
    "Yan Gaoqing, Yuan Lüqian and others, sent ahead under escort, reached Luoyang and were tied to the pillars of the Tianjin Bridge and dismembered (Li Tingze was not in the same group; see the entry for the third month).",
  "常山被围到陷落，众人行动（从755年12月开始）；李庭泽入营营救颜杲卿，为变节旅帅指认、中箭被执；伤重滞营，未随颜杲卿首批（正月中旬）起解；正月下旬随第二批起解":
    "From the siege of Changshan to its fall, everyone’s movements (from the twelfth month of 755): Li Tingze went into the enemy camp to rescue Yan Gaoqing, was pointed out by a turncoat battalion commander, hit by an arrow and taken; too badly wounded to move, he stayed in the camp and was not sent off with Yan Gaoqing in the first group (mid first month), but in the second, late in the first month.",
  "常山城破，赵廷之（早年天策府兵，伤退后经营铁器，晚年归乡）翻出旧日甲胄——亮银札甲、枣红罩袍、「天策府」赵字腰牌——披挂以保乡民，卒阵；这套天策旧甲后为长歌门岑菡、杜徵等人收得，托付闵方城，756年六月下旬随苍云军离常山，七月初抵雁门寄放":
    "When Changshan fell, Zhao Tingzhi (a Tiance soldier in his early years who, retired by his wounds, had dealt in ironware and come home in old age) dug out his old armour, the bright silver lamellar armour, the jujube-red surcoat and the Tiance Command waist token with the character Zhao, put it on to protect the villagers and died fighting. This old Tiance armour was later gathered up by Cen Han, Du Zheng and others of the Changge School and entrusted to Min Fangcheng; late in the sixth month of 756 it left Changshan with the Cangyun Army, and early in the seventh month it reached Yanmen to be kept there.",
  "正月，诏郭子仪罢云中之围，还朔方，益发兵进取东京；选良将一人分兵先出井陉，定河北——子仪荐李光弼（《通鉴》卷217，作者核；罢围回撤之掩护见756.1D草人；下接756.2李光弼出井陉，闵方城携邱鸿随赴常山）":
    "In the first month Guo Ziyi was ordered by edict to lift the siege of Yunzhong, return to Shuofang and raise more troops to take the Eastern Capital, choosing one good general to go out first through Jingxing with a detached force and settle Hebei; Ziyi recommended Li Guangbi (Zizhi tongjian, juan 217; for the cover of the withdrawal from the siege, see the straw men of 756.1D; it leads on to 756.2, Li Guangbi coming out through Jingxing and Min Fangcheng taking Qiu Hong to Changshan).",
  "正月，吕定仪秘不发丧期间，三团受命与朔方军协同，作偏军诱敌：布残旗、扎数百草人、于风口设发声器械，呜咽如筚篥，如同吕定仪仍率部行军；雾夜燃草放烟诱敌入谷，靳沉白执盾侧倾、膝盖压下、右腿微晃，全然吕定仪身势，翻将破阵，伏兵火攻——兵员无一伤损，只消耗残旗旧甲而已——所掩护者，即奉诏罢云中之围（756.1C）后回撤整备之大军：拖慢追兵，为大军争取时间（作者定；邱鸿亦随此撤，见755.12A1；吕定仪灵柩随后自朔州扶归雁门）":
    "First month: while Lü Dingyi’s death was being kept secret, the Third Regiment was ordered to work with the Shuofang Army as a flanking force to lure the enemy: they spread out tattered banners, set up several hundred straw men and placed sounding devices in the windy gaps that moaned like the bili, as though Lü Dingyi were still leading his men on the march. On a foggy night they burned grass to make smoke and lured the enemy into a valley; Jin Chenbai, shield tilted to one side, knee pressed down, right leg swaying slightly, in every way Lü Dingyi’s stance, overturned the enemy general and broke their ranks, and the troops in ambush attacked with fire. Not one man was hurt; all it cost was tattered banners and old armour. What it covered was the main army falling back to regroup after it was ordered by edict to lift the siege of Yunzhong (756.1C): delaying the pursuit to buy the main army time (Qiu Hong withdrew with it too, see 755.12A1; Lü Dingyi’s coffin was later escorted back from Shuozhou to Yanmen).",
  "荔非承烈与靳沉白扶榇，大军返雁门；景惠时才为靳沉白缝制新旗幡":
    "Lifei Chenglie and Jin Chenbai escorted the coffin, and the main army returned to Yanmen; Jing Huishi only now sewed new banners for Jin Chenbai.",
  "755年冬安史乱起，天策府在围攻下撑到次年初春。府城危殆时程凯负伤强守伤兵营，被一刀当胸穿透（落下肺疾），传言战死，实为医者全力救回；府中残兵不得不撤离，岚川云随曹雪阳西撤潼关，757年九月北上，当时决定终生不再返回洛阳。都统李承恩与军师等随圣上入蜀，李庭深负伤不能跟随，临危受命统军，收拢伤兵残队与敌周旋——程凯及兵士三百之众，天策府火种，得他庇护；项旌以入府未满一年的新兵为其录事，草纸炭笔，事无巨细到处记录（按：府城被围始自755年十二月、二月城破，分见各条；「随圣上入蜀」在六月潼关失守之后）":
    "In the winter of 755 the An Lushan Rebellion broke out, and the Tiance Command held out under siege until early spring. When the Command was in peril Cheng Kai, wounded, held the wounded soldiers’ camp by force and was run clean through the chest by a blade (leaving him with a lung ailment); rumour said he had died in battle, but physicians brought him back with all their skill. The remnants in the Command had to withdraw; Lanchuan Yun withdrew west to Tongguan with Cao Xueyang, went north in the ninth month of 757, and decided then never to go back to Luoyang as long as she lived. Li Cheng’en, Commander-in-Chief of the Tiance Command, the strategist and others went with the emperor into Shu; Li Tingshen, wounded and unable to follow, was given command in the crisis and gathered the wounded and the scattered companies to play cat and mouse with the enemy: Cheng Kai and three hundred soldiers, the Tiance Command’s last embers, were under his protection. Xiang Jing, a recruit not yet a year in the Command, served as his recorder, writing everything down wherever he went with charcoal on rough paper. (The siege of the Command began in the twelfth month of 755 and it fell in the second month, see the separate entries; “went with the emperor into Shu” came after Tongguan fell in the sixth month.)",
  "闵方城携邱鸿随李光弼出井陉赴常山，守城至六月（边赛远传信、柳戎联络补给、关岳留守东陉、邱鸿展现能力）；岑菡等人劝服常山团练兵反正，擒安思义出降唐军；史思明自饶阳回争，退屯九门、断粮道，相持四十余日；闵方城协防常山数月":
    "Min Fangcheng took Qiu Hong with Li Guangbi out through Jingxing to Changshan and held the city until the sixth month (Bian Saiyuan carried messages, Liu Rong arranged supplies, Guan Yue stayed to hold the Eastern Pass, Qiu Hong showed what he could do). Cen Han and the others persuaded the Changshan militia to come back over to the Tang, and they seized An Siyi and surrendered to the Tang army; Shi Siming came back from Raoyang to contest it, fell back to camp at Jiumen and cut the supply road, and the two sides faced each other for more than forty days. Min Fangcheng helped defend Changshan for several months.",
  "北境战功嘉奖：闵方城、关岳策勋；连朔马邑先登记功（擢旅帅在757年秋，人在河西时）；女卫营主将受嘉奖":
    "Rewards for merit on the northern frontier: Min Fangcheng and Guan Yue were recorded for merit titles; Lian Shuo had merit recorded for being first up the wall at Mayi (his promotion to Battalion Commander came in the autumn of 757, while he was in Hexi); the commander of the Women’s Guard Corps was rewarded.",
  "薛褚于关城门口接吕定仪灵柩（荔非承烈、靳沉白扶榇）":
    "Xue Chu met Lü Dingyi’s coffin at the gate of the pass fortress (Lifei Chenglie and Jin Chenbai escorting it).",
  "苍云大军返雁门，薛坚（时年二十二）未随归，留郭子仪帐下，自此入朔方军（755.3随苍云西入朔方、归郭子仪麾下；即《闵方城763到765》所谓「出去到军中历练，屡有功勋」）；薛褚、闵方城此后只能远远关注":
    "When the main Cangyun army went back to Yanmen, Xue Jian (then twenty-two) did not return with it but stayed on Guo Ziyi’s staff, and from then on was in the Shuofang Army (in 755.3 he had gone west into Shuofang with the Cangyun Army and come under Guo Ziyi: this is the “going out into the army for experience and winning merit again and again” spoken of later); from then on Xue Chu and Min Fangcheng could only watch over him from afar.",
  "伤兵营被袭夜程凯中刀（疑似）战亡，府城破，天策府生力西撤；两日内沈含英、许秋生、江蓠等万花弟子来援——只有沈含英执意再验看一遍遗体，从中发现程凯回天有望；运回卸甲，才见其右前臂伤疤，知是昔日小巷中救过自己的幼童。许秋生劝阻，而李庭深求，两难之间下了决心，不惜内力耗竭为其封伤、疏通气脉（按：与本年二月「府城危殆」综述条互见；江蓠一行随后携药至）":
    "On the night the wounded soldiers’ camp was attacked, Cheng Kai was cut down and (it seemed) killed; the Command fell and its main force withdrew west. Within two days Shen Hanying, Xu Qiusheng, Jiang Li and other Wanhua disciples came to help; only Shen Hanying insisted on examining the body once more, and found that Cheng Kai might yet be brought back. When they carried him in and took off his armour, he saw the scar on Cheng Kai’s right forearm and knew him for the man who had once saved him as a child in the alley. Xu Qiusheng tried to stop him, while Li Tingshen pleaded; between the two he made up his mind, and spent his inner strength to the last to close the wound and clear the meridians (see also the summary entry for the second month of this year; Jiang Li’s party arrived later with medicine).",
  "程凯昏迷、炎症，情况未卜（二至六月）；沈含英以内力吊命，渐至虚耗":
    "Cheng Kai unconscious and inflamed, his chances uncertain (second to sixth month); Shen Hanying kept him alive with his inner strength and was slowly drained.",
  "曹雪阳率生力西撤，取道已陷之崤函敌后，经程凯旧年所修崤山工事突围入潼关；岚川云随行（注：上承756.2A「西撤（潼关方向）」，下启五月起潼关对峙）":
    "Cao Xueyang led the main force west, through enemy-held country behind the fallen Xiao and Hangu passes, and broke through into Tongguan by way of the Mount Xiao works Cheng Kai had built in earlier years; Lanchuan Yun went with them (following on from 756.2A, “withdrawing west (towards Tongguan)”, and leading into the stand-off at Tongguan from the fifth month).",
  "府城破后，魏谦、马翊随李庭深留天策残营：魏谦以斥候联络内外；马翊亦在残营（因果待定）":
    "After the Command fell, Wei Qian and Ma Yi stayed with Li Tingshen in the Tiance remnant camp: Wei Qian, as a scout, kept up contact inside and out; Ma Yi was in the remnant camp too (how it came about: undecided).",
  "陆晚月得知天策府城破，想起大光明寺——同样是师门的灭顶之灾":
    "When Lu Wanyue learned that the Tiance Command had fallen, she thought of the Great Bright Temple: the same ruin overwhelming one’s order.",
  "吕定仪下葬，身覆荔非承烈当年送他的整张虎皮毯":
    "Lü Dingyi was buried, covered with the whole tiger-skin rug Lifei Chenglie had given him years before.",
  "李庭泽随第二批俘押抵洛阳系狱":
    "Li Tingze reached Luoyang with the second group of prisoners and was put in prison.",
  "三月，哥舒翰素与安思顺不协，使人伪为安禄山致思顺书，于关门擒使献之，并疏思顺七罪；思顺（禄山从兄，前朔方节度，曾先奏禄山反状而不见信）与弟元贞坐诛，家属徙岭南，杨国忠救之不得。底色：苍云755年西入朔方时，朔方节度正是安思顺（郭子仪为其属下天德军使兼九原太守，755.11方代为节度）；苍云密报所投之哥舒翰（755.3C），次年以一封伪书杀之（正文不必用；若用，止于靳沉白756春闻一句传闻，不加评论）":
    "In the third month Geshu Han, long at odds with An Sishun, had someone forge a letter from An Lushan to An Sishun, seized the messenger at the pass gate and presented the letter, and laid out seven crimes of An Sishun’s; An Sishun (An Lushan’s elder cousin, formerly Military Commissioner of Shuofang, who had reported An Lushan’s treasonous designs early on and not been believed) and his brother Yuanzhen were put to death and their families exiled to Lingnan, and Yang Guozhong could not save them. Background: when the Cangyun Army went west into Shuofang in 755, the Military Commissioner of Shuofang was An Sishun himself (Guo Ziyi was his subordinate, commissioner of the Tiande Army and governor of Jiuyuan, and only replaced him as Military Commissioner in 755.11); Geshu Han, to whom the Cangyun Army’s secret report had been sent (755.3C), killed him the next year with a forged letter.",
  "四月，平卢游奕使刘正臣举事杀伪节度吕知诲，孟雪萦之父随之，与安东都护王玄志遥相援助、驰告朝廷；后刘正臣以功拜平卢节度，率军攻范阳，半途败于史思明，回奔平卢，被王玄志设计毒杀，局势成谜——变乱之中孟父将孟雪萦托付夏明沧，二人离城避祸，北上白河村安顿，引入药宗师门修习":
    "In the fourth month Liu Zhengchen, Patrol Commissioner of Pinglu, rose and killed Lü Zhihui, the false Military Commissioner; Meng Xueying’s father joined him, and they gave each other help from afar with Wang Xuanzhi, Protector of Andong, and sent word to the court. Later Liu Zhengchen, rewarded with the post of Military Commissioner of Pinglu, led an army against Fanyang, was beaten by Shi Siming halfway, fled back to Pinglu and was poisoned by a plot of Wang Xuanzhi’s, and the situation became a riddle. In the turmoil Meng’s father entrusted Meng Xueying to Xia Mingcang, and the two left the city to escape the trouble, went north to settle in Baihe Village and were brought into the Beitian School of Medicine to study.",
  "常山围解（四月郭子仪出井陉来会，九门城南大败史思明）；岑杜南下洛阳寻骨，约五月初抵洛":
    "The siege of Changshan was lifted (in the fourth month Guo Ziyi came out through Jingxing to join forces, and Shi Siming was heavily defeated south of Jiumen); Cen Han and Du Zheng went south to Luoyang to look for his bones, arriving about the beginning of the fifth month.",
  "李庭泽斩于洛阳城外；岑杜凭桃花簪认尸，暂厝镇上小庙，择日葬于洛阳，周全丧仪；岑菡去信长安、太原、天策府":
    "Li Tingze was beheaded outside Luoyang; Cen Han and Du Zheng identified the body by the peach-blossom hairpin, laid it for the time being in a small temple in the town, and on a chosen day buried him at Luoyang with full funeral rites; Cen Han wrote to Chang’an, to Taiyuan and to the Tiance Command.",
  "沈含英封伤救人后内力虚亏，狼牙突袭牧场时被围，护卫伤兵而亡；李庭深被迫斗将，率残兵收回沈含英遗骨。许秋生一度因此对程凯怨怼":
    "After closing the wound and saving the man, Shen Hanying’s inner strength was depleted; when the Langya Army made a surprise attack on the pasture he was surrounded, and died guarding the wounded soldiers. Li Tingshen was forced into single combat and led the remnants to bring back Shen Hanying’s remains. For a time Xu Qiusheng resented Cheng Kai for it.",
  "嘉山之战（五月壬午，常山郡东）：郭子仪、李光弼大破史思明，河北十余郡杀贼守将而降；闵方城留守常山，遣邱鸿领一队随唐军部署出战，邱鸿阵前有功，武艺为人所见（757年考课擂台之张本）":
    "The Battle of Jiashan (on the renwu day of the fifth month, east of Changshan Commandery): Guo Ziyi and Li Guangbi routed Shi Siming, and more than ten commanderies of Hebei killed the rebel garrison commanders and surrendered. Min Fangcheng stayed to hold Changshan and sent Qiu Hong with a squad to fight as the Tang army deployed them; Qiu Hong won merit in the field, and people saw his skill (groundwork for the merit-review bout of 757).",
  "潼关城破，六月十三日玄宗离京；闵方城六月下旬离常山，边赛远马前下拜、拜入苍云（七月初抵雁门，见七月条）":
    "Tongguan fell, and on the thirteenth day of the sixth month Xuanzong left the capital; Min Fangcheng left Changshan late in the sixth month, and Bian Saiyuan bowed before his horse and joined the Cangyun Army (reaching Yanmen early in the seventh month, see the seventh-month entry).",
  "长安陷落，李庭深家人蒙京中旧友相助，北迁太原郡望旧宅（家信伏线）":
    "Chang’an fell; with the help of old friends in the capital, Li Tingshen’s family moved north to the old family house in Taiyuan (groundwork for the family letter).",
  "枫华谷红衣教事：五月起岚川云、齐晟率残军与狼牙对峙潼关，擒操兽女玛奈丽；岚川云以陆晚月之药致其假死脱身，玛奈丽于谷间索道解绞索时中箭坠谷——六月潼关、枫华谷失陷，岚川云重伤":
    "The Hongyi Order affair at Fenghua Valley: from the fifth month Lanchuan Yun and Qi Sheng, leading the remnants of the army, faced the Langya Army at Tongguan and captured the beast-tamer Māneli; Lanchuan Yun used Lu Wanyue’s drug to make her seem dead so she could get away, but as Māneli was untying the noose on the rope way across the valley she was hit by an arrow and fell into the gorge. In the sixth month Tongguan and Fenghua Valley fell, and Lanchuan Yun was badly wounded.",
  "李家抵太原，洛中来书已候；李母闻李庭泽死讯，心疾离世（家信缘起）":
    "The Li family reached Taiyuan, where a letter from Luoyang was already waiting; on hearing of Li Tingze’s death, his mother died of heart failure (the origin of the family letter).",
  "闵方城自常山返雁门，初至吕定仪墓前；景惠时又一次试图近他，仍只得处置其身":
    "Min Fangcheng came back from Changshan to Yanmen and went for the first time to Lü Dingyi’s grave; once again Jing Huishi tried to come near him, and once again could only tend his body.",
  "崔圆遣使于河池迎驾，奉「剑南备具」；七月玄宗至成都，八月闻肃宗灵武即位，自称太上皇，留蜀至次年。底色：天策都统李承恩、军师随驾在蜀":
    "Cui Yuan sent envoys to meet the emperor at Hechi with “the Jiannan provisions”; in the seventh month Xuanzong reached Chengdu, and in the eighth, hearing that Suzong had taken the throne at Lingwu, he styled himself Retired Emperor and stayed in Shu until the next year. Background: Li Cheng’en, Commander-in-Chief of the Tiance Command, and the strategist were with the emperor in Shu.",
  "六七月间，陆晚月自潼关谷地救岚川云至长安城郊，置宅其地——宅中重逢滞留中原十六年的师父陆羽鸣；岚川云大体康复之际，并遇晁衡一行（按：作者编年一处作「756年秋」，当指康复遇晁衡之时；兹从 Notion 系于六七月）":
    "In the sixth or seventh month Lu Wanyue rescued Lanchuan Yun from the Tongguan valleys and brought her to the outskirts of Chang’an, where she found a house; in the house she met again her master Lu Yuming, who had stayed on in the Central Plains for sixteen years. When Lanchuan Yun had largely recovered, they also met Chao Heng and his party.",
  "卢秉毓协守九门，七月城破被俘，叛军认出卢氏子，灌药压制经脉擒送范阳家府门前；挣缚杀敌中箭，卢氏献情报、献铁换其性命；此后闭门养伤至757年":
    "Lu Bingyu helped hold Jiumen and was captured when it fell in the seventh month; the rebels recognised him as a son of the Lu family, drugged him to suppress his meridians and delivered him, bound, to the gate of the family house at Fanyang. He fought free of his bonds and killed, and was hit by an arrow; the Lu family bought his life with intelligence and iron. After that he stayed shut away recovering from his wounds until 757.",
  "暗线：陆晚月循胡商之线所得安全屋，即陆羽鸣藏身处；陆羽鸣照料重伤的岚川云，其嗓音露出旧事（岚川云认否未定）":
    "The hidden thread: the safe house Lu Wanyue found by following the Hu merchants’ network was where Lu Yuming was hiding; Lu Yuming nursed the badly wounded Lanchuan Yun, and his voice gave away the past (whether Lanchuan Yun recognised it: undecided).",
  "程凯苏醒及初步康复，许秋生照护——发急症昏迷时被他直性灌药救回":
    "Cheng Kai came round and began to recover, with Xu Qiusheng nursing him: when Cheng Kai fell into a sudden fit and lost consciousness, Xu Qiusheng brought him back by bluntly pouring medicine down his throat.",
  "岑杜前往长安，岑菡援救、安顿长姐":
    "Cen Han and Du Zheng went to Chang’an, where Cen Han rescued her eldest sister and saw her settled.",
  "程锋随边兵东归勤王（经朔方入河东），陆灵携二子随行；程钊生母独留北庭":
    "Cheng Feng went east with the frontier troops to come to the aid of the throne (through Shuofang into Hedong), and Lu Ling went with him, taking their two sons; Cheng Zhao’s mother stayed alone at Beiting.",
  "肃宗灵武即位大赦，《即位大赦文》：「大辟罪已下，常赦所不免者，咸赦除之。」绞是大辟，唐青阳册上的绞罪就此勾销，门主手里的把柄也没了——他可以走了。同一道赦文写明杨国忠近亲「不在免限」：强征南诏兵的那家人不赦，从强征里逃出来的人赦了（赦文七月甲子下于灵武，八月闻于蜀）":
    "Suzong’s amnesty on taking the throne at Lingwu, the Amnesty on Accession: “Crimes up to and including the death penalty, and those not covered by ordinary amnesties, are all pardoned.” Strangulation was the death penalty: the strangulation charge against Tang Qingyang’s name on the roll was struck off, and the hold the head of the clan had over him was gone too; he could leave. The same amnesty laid down that Yang Guozhong’s close kin were “not within the pardon”: the family that had pressed the men for Nanzhao was not pardoned, and the men who had escaped the press were (the amnesty was issued at Lingwu on the jiazi day of the seventh month and known in Shu in the eighth).",
  "常山再陷：六月郭子仪、李光弼西撤后河北复失，九月常山又陷；书院生徒或走或留（757年正月颜真卿告知岑杜，为二人折返常山之缘由）":
    "Changshan fell again: after Guo Ziyi and Li Guangbi withdrew west in the sixth month Hebei was lost once more, and in the ninth month Changshan fell again; of the academy’s students, some fled and some stayed (in the first month of 757 Yan Zhenqing told Cen Han and Du Zheng of it, which is why the two went back to Changshan).",
  "李庭深得太原家信，知李庭泽身故、母亲心疾离世，带伤闭门，心疾初发，程凯相劝；江蓠补衣":
    "Li Tingshen received the family letter from Taiyuan and learned that Li Tingze was dead and that his mother had died of heart failure; wounded as he was, he shut himself away, and his own heart trouble first showed itself. Cheng Kai tried to talk him round; Jiang Li mended his clothes.",
  "九月阿史那从礼诱河曲九姓府、六胡州诸胡聚经略军北，将寇朔方，郭子仪诣天德军发兵讨之；十一月与回纥会师，破同罗及叛胡于榆林河北，河曲平":
    "In the ninth month Ashina Congli enticed the Hu of the Nine Surnames commands of the Hequ and of the Six Hu Prefectures to gather north of the Jinglüe Army, meaning to raid Shuofang; Guo Ziyi went to the Tiande Army, raised troops and moved against them, and in the eleventh month joined forces with the Uighurs, defeated the Tongluo and the rebel Hu north of the Yulin River, and the Hequ was pacified.",
  "十月，岚川云护送晁衡奔彭原（宁州）皇帝行在，得嘉赏、册飞骑尉；后闻太原备战，转赴太原，见齐晟，始与苍云接触——次年正二月叛军大举攻城，齐晟惨烈战亡（详757年二月条）（按：作者编年作「757年初奔灵武」，然肃宗是年九月已离灵武南下，十月驻彭原，次年二月方幸凤翔；且太原之围起于757年正月，岚川云须先期抵太原，故从 Notion 系于756年十月、行在作彭原）":
    "In the tenth month Lanchuan Yun escorted Chao Heng to the emperor’s travelling court at Pengyuan (Ningzhou), was rewarded and invested as Commandant of Flying Cavalry; then, hearing that Taiyuan was preparing for war, she went on to Taiyuan, found Qi Sheng, and first had dealings with the Cangyun Army. In the first and second months of the next year the rebels attacked the city in force, and Qi Sheng died terribly in battle (see the entry for the second month of 757).",
  "固防；李庭深居丧养伤，江蓠陪伴，二人知晓互有心意；程凯康复训练、带训士兵、打听岚川云去向（未果）":
    "Strengthening the defences; Li Tingshen in mourning and recovering from his wounds, with Jiang Li at his side, the two aware of each other’s feelings; Cheng Kai in rehabilitation, drilling soldiers and asking after where Lanchuan Yun had gone (without success).",
  "项旌得家信回河阳奔父丧（时河阳在燕军治下），在家数月，程凯寄钱慰问":
    "Xiang Jing received a letter from home and went back to Heyang to mourn his father (Heyang was then under the Yan army’s rule), staying at home several months; Cheng Kai sent money and his condolences.",
  "苍云偏师随郭子仪征河曲（闵方城、荔非承烈、薛褚等），经天德军（九原，仅作地名带过）；榆林河一战荔非前军突阵，胸肋为同罗精骑骨朵所击，内伤不显于外；当夜薛褚为之裹肋，应其所请瞒下不报，伤延至757年（即757年擂台「体如鼓面」之由）；战后闵方城引破阵营百人留驻朔方（故757年正月得以就近出援河西）":
    "A detached Cangyun force went with Guo Ziyi on the Hequ campaign (Min Fangcheng, Lifei Chenglie, Xue Chu and others), passing the Tiande Army (Jiuyuan). In the battle of the Yulin River Lifei led the van through the enemy line and was struck on the ribs by the mace of a picked Tongluo horseman, an internal injury that did not show; that night Xue Chu bound his ribs and, at his request, hid it from the reports, and the injury dragged on into 757 (the source of “a body like a drumskin” at the challenge bout of 757). After the battle Min Fangcheng left a hundred men of the Rank-Breaker Corps stationed in Shuofang (which is why they could go to Hexi’s aid from close by in the first month of 757).",
  "榆林河战后，荔非受命点验、押送俘虏：一册名簿，逐一点名分押，不言一语；六胡州再叛，荔非底里消沉（俘虏去处不交代；不认出任何面孔，不提738年，薛直不出名）":
    "After the battle of the Yulin River Lifei was ordered to count and escort the prisoners: one roll of names, called one by one and sent off in groups, without a word. The Six Hu Prefectures had rebelled again, and Lifei was sunk deep in gloom (where the prisoners went is not told; he recognises no faces; 738 is not mentioned; Xue Zhi is not named).",
  "河曲庆功宴后雪夜，荔非拖刀出帐舞刀，闵方城上前对打，尽兴后荔非立刀雪中：「阿城，你说我是不是傻子」，随即跪地痛哭；士兵尴尬，乐照奏；闵方城不言而去（文档原无系年，暂系于此；荔非带内伤对打，无人察觉；「傻子」之意正文不解释）":
    "On a snowy night after the victory feast for the Hequ, Lifei dragged his blade out of the tent and danced with it; Min Fangcheng stepped up to fight him, and when they had fought their fill Lifei stood his blade in the snow: “A-Cheng, tell me, am I a fool?”, and dropped to his knees weeping bitterly. The soldiers were embarrassed, and the music played on; Min Fangcheng left without a word (Lifei fought with his internal injury and no one noticed; what “fool” means is not explained in the story).",
  "年末项旌及冠。魏谦说既然李将军为长官，不如请他取字，于是李庭深忝做一回长辈，取「扬节」二字——时项旌居父丧于河阳（见十一月条），丧中而冠（《礼记·杂记下》「以丧冠者，虽三年之丧可也」），字由书信往还取定":
    "At the end of the year Xiang Jing came of age. Wei Qian said that since General Li was his superior, they might as well ask him to choose a courtesy name, and so Li Tingshen played the elder for once and chose the two characters Yangjie, “to raise one’s integrity”. Xiang Jing was then at Heyang in mourning for his father (see the entry for the eleventh month), and was capped while in mourning (the Book of Rites, “Miscellaneous Records II”: “To be capped while in mourning is permissible, even in the three-year mourning”); the name was settled by letters back and forth.",
  // 757
  "正月，河西兵马使盖庭伦谋割据，与武威九姓商胡安门物等杀节度使周泌，聚兵六万；武威七城，胡人已据其五，惟二城坚守，支度判官崔称与中使刘日新以二城兵攻之，月余乱平":
    "First month: Gai Tinglun, Commander of Troops in Hexi, plotting to set himself up independently, killed the Military Commissioner Zhou Bi together with An Menwu and other Hu merchants of the Nine Surnames at Wuwei, and gathered sixty thousand men. Of the seven walled towns of Wuwei the Hu already held five, and only two held out; the supply officer Cui Cheng and the palace envoy Liu Rixin attacked with the troops of the two towns, and after a month and more the rising was put down.",
  "尹子奇围睢阳，张巡自宁陵入城与许远合守。底色：许远即 740 年以监察御史守安戎城（后改名平戎城）者；陈瑞和入城后，可留一句许远说起平戎城的闲话":
    "Yin Ziqi besieged Suiyang, and Zhang Xun came into the city from Ningling to hold it with Xu Yuan. Background: Xu Yuan was the Investigating Censor who had held Anrong (later renamed Pingrong) in 740.",
  "闵方城、连朔将兵往河西协助平乱（连朔可能留在河西一年算是历练＋方便联络，直到758春方归）":
    "Min Fangcheng and Lian Shuo took troops to Hexi to help put down the rising (Lian Shuo perhaps stayed on in Hexi a year, for the experience and to keep up communications, not coming back until the spring of 758).",
  "岑杜见颜真卿，得知卢秉毓之事以及书院事情未了":
    "Cen Han and Du Zheng saw Yan Zhenqing and learned what had happened to Lu Bingyu, and that the academy’s affairs were still unsettled.",
  "天策残营新岁，许秋生与李庭深夜饮":
    "New Year in the Tiance remnant camp: Xu Qiusheng and Li Tingshen drank together at night.",
  "太原守城 齐晟战亡":
    "The defence of Taiyuan; Qi Sheng fell in battle.",
  "叛军攻围太原，狄元恪充守城兵马使一员，主一段城防，兼机动应援与转输护送诸务，麾下二三百人：除樊璋随侍，请昔日授艺的安西武官为副以稳部伍，一书手主文书、一传讯头目司外哨接应，居中总其纲纪，其部虽小而诸务有序，军中多不以寻常斗将视之；樊璋数度持盾护卫，密不透风。苍云一度遣关岳赴太原暂管苍云军太原行营，并考察其人——战况激烈之际连日不下城垣，一场战事后队伍满面尘灰血污、疲敝非常，仍然面貌整肃":
    "The rebels besieged Taiyuan, and Di Yuanke served as one of the commanders of troops for the city’s defence, with charge of a stretch of the walls as well as mobile relief and the escort of supplies, two or three hundred men under him. Besides Fan Zhang at his side, he asked the Anxi officer who had once taught him to serve as his deputy to steady the ranks, with a copyist for the paperwork and a messenger chief for the outposts and liaison, while he himself held the whole together; his unit was small but everything in it was in order, and in the army few took him for an ordinary fighting general. Several times Fan Zhang covered him with his shield, leaving not a gap. The Cangyun Army for a time sent Guan Yue to Taiyuan to take temporary charge of the Cangyun field headquarters there, and to size him up: in the heaviest fighting he stayed on the walls for days on end, and after one battle, his men grimy with dust and blood and utterly spent, they were still in good order.",
  "暮春，乱平后中使见闵方城履历，知其必熟甘、凉地形风物，命巡视凉州长城沿线，与连朔西行至甘、凉州境；黄昏横风大雪无从扎营，山背避风处遇牧人，累于兵戈不肯相让；闵方城不提借地，只问羊群走失方位，自与青年牧人上马奔袭数时辰，半夜带回牧羊五十余头，脸鼻僵冷、眉睫生霜；牧人感激，请入毡帐饮乳酒，单辟小帐留宿。是夜连朔复命后与之同榻抵足——「那要是咱们寻不着路回去呢」「想我报你脱队逃逸？」连朔看他一会，摇头而笑，手上仍然拥住；闵方城阖眼睡去，「他的脸锋棱起伏，像城外山峦」":
    "Late spring. After the rising had been put down, the palace envoy saw Min Fangcheng’s record and, knowing he must know the land and ways of Ganzhou and Liangzhou, ordered him to inspect the line of the Great Wall at Liangzhou, and he went west with Lian Shuo into Ganzhou and Liangzhou. At dusk a heavy snow on a crosswind left them nowhere to make camp; in a sheltered spot behind a hill they met herdsmen, worn down by the fighting and unwilling to make room. Min Fangcheng said nothing about borrowing ground and asked only where their sheep had strayed; he mounted and rode out with a young herdsman for hours, and in the middle of the night brought back fifty-odd sheep, his face and nose frozen stiff and frost on his brows and lashes. The grateful herdsmen invited them into the felt tent to drink fermented milk and gave them a small tent of their own for the night. That night, after reporting back, Lian Shuo lay down beside him, feet to feet: “And what if we can’t find the way back?” “Want me to report you for leaving your unit and deserting?” Lian Shuo looked at him a while, shook his head and laughed, his arms still round him; Min Fangcheng closed his eyes and slept, “his face all ridges and folds, like the hills outside the city”.",
  "雪霁归凉州，时汉、蕃僧西来，欲携经卷佛宝赴洛阳冲觉寺，闵方城所部受命协助点验；正殿香客中间闵方城燃香俯拜，连朔越人群看他——「忽觉他根本不是军人，也非牧人。河西汉子而已」。起行点验时连朔察一阔面僧头上青皮生硬，闵方城以「弱水／黑河」地名试出其未历甘州，扣人细搜：安息香漆匣夹层得半枚穿系牦牛毛的骨契，香饼中卷蕃字木牒，旁以汉字记姑臧、广武、金城地名与马、仓、卒数——「城，人马，粮，还能是什么。押下去。」交凉州驻军，译语人验为蕃军探报；沙弥失踪的师兄于城郊沙棘丛中拖出，几乎干渴而死":
    "When the snow cleared they went back to Liangzhou, where Han and Tibetan monks had come from the west meaning to take sutras and Buddhist treasures to Chongjue Monastery in Luoyang, and Min Fangcheng’s men were ordered to help check them. Among the pilgrims in the main hall Min Fangcheng lit incense and bowed low, and Lian Shuo looked at him across the crowd: “It struck me suddenly that he wasn’t a soldier at all, nor a herdsman either. Just a man of Hexi.” When they set out and the checking began, Lian Shuo noticed that the shaven scalp of a broad-faced monk looked stiff and raw, and Min Fangcheng caught him out with the place names Ruo Shui and Black River, proving he had never been through Ganzhou; they held him and searched him closely. In the false bottom of a lacquered box of benzoin they found half a bone tally strung on yak hair, and rolled into an incense cake a wooden slip in Tibetan script, with the place names Guzang, Guangwu and Jincheng noted in Chinese beside numbers of horses, granaries and soldiers: “Towns, men and horses, grain, what else could it be. Take him away.” He was handed to the Liangzhou garrison, and the interpreter confirmed it as a Tibetan army scout’s report; the missing elder brother of the novice was dragged out of a sea-buckthorn thicket outside the city, nearly dead of thirst.",
  "春夏之交，天策残营与河东官军（李光弼系统南面偏师）接上关系；程锋时为行军司马；鱼朝恩为偏师监军（至德中常令监军事）":
    "At the turn of spring and summer the Tiance remnant camp made contact with the Hedong government army (the southern detached force of Li Guangbi’s command); Cheng Feng was then its Adjutant, and Yu Chao’en its Army Monitor (in the Zhide years the court regularly appointed Army Monitors).",
  "岑菡、杜徵返回常山，安排书院徒生下江南投师门（卢秉毓夜访送桃、协办里坊文书，边赛远自苍云来助）；杜徵刺杀狼牙将官":
    "Cen Han and Du Zheng went back to Changshan and arranged for the academy’s students to go south to the school’s masters in Jiangnan (Lu Bingyu came at night bringing peaches and helped with the ward papers, and Bian Saiyuan came from the Cangyun Army to help); Du Zheng assassinated a Langya officer.",
  "闵方城奉命返雁门；城外河边喂马刷马，沿河杏花簌簌摇落，连朔站在他跟前一片片拈他身上沾的落花，拈下来便松手让它落下；闵方城留下一条久用的套马索，命连朔带兵士七八十人驻留凉州，以便朔方、河西二节度联络、看视边情——「听见了没，你警醒着」。连朔驻留约一年，收拾行装那几天把河边落杏花收了些晒在帐外，临走抓两把半干花瓣塞进一只束口布袋":
    "Min Fangcheng was ordered back to Yanmen. By the river outside the city he fed and groomed his horse while apricot blossom drifted down all along the river; Lian Shuo stood before him picking the fallen petals off him one by one, letting each go as he picked it. Min Fangcheng left him an old lasso he had long used, and ordered Lian Shuo to stay at Liangzhou with seventy or eighty men, to keep up communications between the Shuofang and Hexi commissions and watch the frontier: “Do you hear? Keep your wits about you.” Lian Shuo stayed about a year; in the days he was packing he gathered some of the fallen apricot blossom from the riverbank and dried it outside his tent, and when he left stuffed two handfuls of half-dry petals into a drawstring cloth bag.",
  "闵方城返回雁门":
    "Min Fangcheng went back to Yanmen.",
  "兄弟重逢：程凯夜袭狼牙营，救出程宇":
    "Brothers reunited: Cheng Kai raided the Langya camp by night and rescued Cheng Yu.",
  "常山书院生徒（擅琴者）持杜徵向雁门求得之文书，以军中乐人身份经雁门、太原南下，往投长歌师门":
    "Students of the Changshan academy (good at the qin), carrying papers Du Zheng had obtained from Yanmen, went south through Yanmen and Taiyuan as army musicians to join their Changge masters.",
  "夏，天策残营斥候风波，魏谦的奚族发小阿会朗撞魏谦弯刀而死":
    "Summer: the scouts’ affair in the Tiance remnant camp; Wei Qian’s Xi childhood friend Ahui Lang ran onto Wei Qian’s curved blade and died.",
  "程凯北原（青骓牧场一带）两箭退狼骑：一箭破大旗，一箭射杀主将战狼":
    "On the northern plain (around the Qingzhui pastures) Cheng Kai drove off the wolf riders with two arrows: one split the great banner, one killed the commander’s war wolf.",
  "卢秉毓救杜徵至范阳休养，岑菡、边赛远等随后而至":
    "Lu Bingyu rescued Du Zheng and brought him to Fanyang to recover, and Cen Han, Bian Saiyuan and the others followed.",
  "苍云谋召狄元恪：吕定仪身亡后军政谋略一线缺人，需可维护雁门与关内重镇、主流士族联系的人物；更深一层——破阵营之心系于闵方城一人人格之上，「早晚全营认人不认制，其实极度危险」，统帅期待狄元恪进来「校正」、补全制度骨架，此意不与狄氏说（当年玄甲军初立及雁门关之役后困苦时，狄氏父辈曾暗中相助，此召亦是续旧缘）。狄父原欲送他往灵武行在，苍云递文书——「此任虽在边陲，然非轻遣……俟其历练既深，建树既著，必为请功」；狄氏终不好回绝，狄元恪念及秦徽，愈发自励，不可畏难避险":
    "The Cangyun Army planned to send for Di Yuanke. Since Lü Dingyi’s death the army was short of anyone for military government and strategy, someone who could keep up Yanmen’s ties with the great garrisons inside the passes and the leading gentry families. And, at a deeper level: the Rank-Breaker Corps’ heart hung on one man, Min Fangcheng, and his character; “sooner or later the whole corps will follow the man and not the system, and that is extremely dangerous”. The Commander hoped Di Yuanke would come in to “correct” this and fill out the framework of the system; this was not said to the Di family (in the days when the Xuanjia Army was first raised, and in the hard times after the Battle of Yanmen Pass, the elder generation of the Di family had quietly helped it, so this summons also renewed an old bond). Di’s father had meant to send him to the emperor’s travelling court at Lingwu, but the Cangyun Army sent a letter: “Though this post lies on the frontier, it is no light posting … once he has gained deep experience and made his mark, we will surely ask that his merit be rewarded”; in the end the Di family could not well refuse, and Di Yuanke, thinking of Qin Hui, drove himself all the harder, unwilling to shrink from difficulty or danger.",
  "残营营啸，师兄闯院斥程凯「龟缩深院」，许秋生以医针制之；江蓠结阵为众兵安神":
    "A camp panic in the remnant camp: a senior brother burst into the courtyard and berated Cheng Kai for “cowering in the back courtyard”, and Xu Qiusheng subdued him with acupuncture needles; Jiang Li formed a ring to calm the soldiers.",
  "程凯决战（杀死沈含英的）狼牙将官，夺回沈含英玉佩，险不能全身而退；少林道永危难之际一记金钟相救，此后驻留营中一段时日，树下安坐绳床，点檀香诵《金光明经》以度苦护国；许秋生见程凯真心，方才敬服。道永临别留字纸：「吾存一心，愿永空囹圄，长息烽烟。经年不道干戈字，满耳唯闻丝竹声；将比嵩山无动转，万年常镇洛阳城」——李庭深与程凯同听其讲道，其去后奉一卷《金刚经》于案前":
    "Cheng Kai fought it out with the Langya officer (who had killed Shen Hanying) and took back Shen Hanying’s jade pendant, barely getting away alive; in his peril Daoyong of Shaolin saved him with a stroke of the Golden Bell, and afterwards stayed in the camp for a time, sitting peacefully on a rope seat under a tree, burning sandalwood and chanting the Golden Light Sutra to deliver the suffering and protect the realm. Xu Qiusheng, seeing Cheng Kai’s sincerity, came to respect him. When Daoyong left he left a slip of writing: “I keep one mind, and wish the prisons ever empty and the beacons long at rest. Years without a word of shield and spear, the ears full only of strings and flutes; unmoving as Mount Song, may it guard Luoyang ten thousand years.” Li Tingshen had listened to his teaching with Cheng Kai, and after he left placed a scroll of the Diamond Sutra on his desk.",
  "程凯不欲长久苟安，谋求起复，与李庭深有所争驰；后攻拔半山狼牙营垒而建功（受李光弼南面偏师节制，李光弼本人仍在太原）；李庭深联络程锋暗中相助，陆灵援手；复职，得三百人营":
    "Cheng Kai, unwilling to live in safety for long, sought to be reinstated, and was at odds with Li Tingshen over it; later he won merit by storming the Langya stockade halfway up the hill (under the command of Li Guangbi’s southern detached force; Li Guangbi himself was still at Taiyuan); Li Tingshen got in touch with Cheng Feng to help in secret, and Lu Ling lent a hand; he was reinstated and given a camp of three hundred men.",
  "狄元恪太原守备有功 应召入苍云为将官预备":
    "Di Yuanke, having won merit in the defence of Taiyuan, answered the summons to join the Cangyun Army as an officer in waiting.",
  "狄元恪辞谢安西武官，守城两名副手也不带，随行只樊璋，两人两骑，从关城南大门纳名帖而入。黄昏，酗酒的何姓老兽医从马厩晃出，醉眼见为首年轻军将人马俱甲、又执长槊，高大端严，惊跑而涕泪纵横；当晚营中风传老兽医「见着了故统帅」「银枪烈马，好像真瞧见昔年薛帅一般」。荔非承烈斥了士兵，又去问，老兽医醒了酒竟都忘了。闵方城看荔非拎着那兽医——「怎么？」「你没听见？」「有新人。」「知道来了个姓狄的小子，但我说的哪是这个啊。你——」闵方城再不说话，半晌，摇摇头":
    "Di Yuanke thanked the Anxi officer and took his leave, and did not bring his two deputies from the city defence either; only Fan Zhang went with him, two men on two horses, and they presented their name cards at the south gate of the pass fortress and went in. At dusk an old horse doctor named He, a drunkard, came weaving out of the stables, saw through his drunken eyes the young officer at the front, horse and rider both armoured and a cavalry lance in his hand, tall and grave, and ran off in fright with tears streaming down his face; that evening word went round the camp that the old horse doctor had “seen the late Commander”, “silver spear and fiery horse, just as if he’d really seen Commander Xue in the old days”. Lifei Chenglie scolded the soldiers, then went to ask, but the old horse doctor, sober again, had forgotten all of it. Min Fangcheng watched Lifei hauling the horse doctor along: “Well?” “Didn’t you hear?” “There’s someone new.” “I know some lad called Di has turned up, but that’s not what I mean at all. You—” Min Fangcheng said nothing more, and after a long while shook his head.",
  "校场初见：一通鼓罢，狄元恪上前拱手自报名字来历，闵方城看着他，点了一下头，没有话。「往后军中事务，还望将军多加指点。」「指点？」——不含讥讽，只像品咂了一遍这个问题——「做你会的事。」又问「你多大了」，答「开元十八」；闵方城静了一刻，仿佛在虚空中摆了片刻算筹，朝关城北门方向望了一眼：「多活十年。」拎起盾刀转身走了，把狄元恪晾在原地。狄元恪把这几句想了一遍，几乎可笑，旋即火气直顶上来——若当真想羞辱，也太不像，那人神情太过平静和认真。恰关岳快步赶来接引，言语晓畅、知分寸礼节——「闵将军是开元八年的人，半生都在苍云」——狄元恪方觉偌大边城到底还算有人通达世情":
    "First meeting on the drill ground. When the drum roll ended, Di Yuanke stepped forward, saluted and gave his name and background; Min Fangcheng looked at him, nodded once, and said nothing. “I hope the General will guide me in the army’s affairs from now on.” “Guide?” (no mockery in it; he seemed only to turn the question over) “Do what you know how to do.” Then he asked, “How old are you?”, and was told, “Born in the eighteenth year of Kaiyuan.” Min Fangcheng was quiet a moment, as if laying out counting rods in the air, glanced towards the north gate of the pass fortress, said, “Ten years longer,” picked up his shield-and-blade, turned and walked away, leaving Di Yuanke standing there. Di Yuanke went over the few words; it was almost laughable, and then anger rushed up into his head: if it was meant as an insult, it was very unlike one, the man’s face too calm and serious. Just then Guan Yue hurried over to receive him, fluent, with a sense of what was fitting and of manners (“General Min was born in the eighth year of Kaiyuan; he has spent half his life in the Cangyun Army”), and only then did Di Yuanke feel that this great frontier town had, after all, someone who understood the ways of the world.",
  "过午拜会同级的三团长官靳沉白：靳沉白容易说话，撤了案上加盐椒香料的民间茶，另烹清茶待客——雅士做派，若非狄元恪门第见识，怕还要嫌它无味；狄元恪留意其背后大幅毡布挂图久用垂顺、四下补了小图，「这军帐里，连你我并物什都算上，怕是这图更有资历些」——「致威好眼力。故吕将军刀笔，鞠躬尽瘁。」是晚寝帐，狄元恪问樊璋：「现成两座山在前头。你怎么想的？谁好？」樊璋抿着嘴，想着闵方城对他点一下头的模样——「我可不敢说，说了二郎可要生气。……若说二郎看不出，我也不信。山就只那一座。」":
    "After noon he called on his equal, Jin Chenbai, commander of the Third Regiment. Jin Chenbai was easy to deal with: he took away the country tea, made with salt, pepper and spices, from his table and brewed plain tea for his guest, a cultivated man’s way; without Di Yuanke’s family background and breadth of experience it might even have seemed tasteless. Di Yuanke noticed the large felt map hanging behind him, soft and limp with long use and patched all round with small maps: “In this tent, counting you and me and everything in it, I suspect the map has the longest service.” “Zhiwei has a good eye. The late General Lü’s pen and blade; he gave himself to it to the last.” That night in their sleeping tent Di Yuanke asked Fan Zhang: “There are two mountains right in front of us. What do you think? Which is better?” Fan Zhang pressed his lips together, thinking of the way Min Fangcheng had nodded once at him: “I wouldn’t dare say; if I did, Erlang would be angry. … But if Erlang says he can’t see it, I won’t believe him either. There’s only the one mountain.”",
  "狄元恪携樊璋两人两骑自关城南门入雁门：老兽医醉中误认作故统帅；校场初见闵方城，问年岁后答以「多活十年」；关岳引入营安顿；过午拜靳沉白，帐中清茶，见吕定仪旧图":
    "Di Yuanke and Fan Zhang, two men on two horses, entered Yanmen by the south gate of the pass fortress: the old horse doctor, drunk, took him for the late Commander; at his first meeting with Min Fangcheng on the drill ground, asked his age, Min answered, “Ten years longer”; Guan Yue took him into the camp and saw him settled; after noon he called on Jin Chenbai, and in the tent, over plain tea, saw Lü Dingyi’s old map.",
  "蜀郡健儿郭千仞等反于成都，六军兵马使陈玄礼、剑南节度使李峘讨平，程铎随军平乱；时上皇在蜀，天策都统李承恩、军师随驾在成都（按：月份待核）。反的是蜀郡健儿，正是唐青阳当过的那种兵；唐哲小队在暗处。程铎与唐青阳三年来第一次照面，看见他背的是唐门的千机匣——自己营里最好的弩手，拉不开弩了。程铎告诉他赦了，可以回军籍、用回本名；唐青阳说不回":
    "Guo Qianren and other professional soldiers of Shu commandery rose in revolt at Chengdu; Chen Xuanli, commander of the Six Armies, and Li Huan, Military Commissioner of Jiannan, put it down, and Cheng Duo went with the army against them. The retired emperor was then in Shu, and Li Cheng’en, Commander-in-Chief of the Tiance Command, and the strategist were with him at Chengdu. Those who rose were professional soldiers of Shu, just the kind of soldier Tang Qingyang had once been; Tang Zhe’s squad was in the shadows. Cheng Duo and Tang Qingyang met face to face for the first time in three years, and he saw that Tang Qingyang carried a Tang Clan Thousand-Mechanism Case on his back: the best crossbowman in his own camp could no longer draw a crossbow. Cheng Duo told him he had been pardoned, and could go back on the army rolls and use his own name again; Tang Qingyang said he would not.",
  "陈瑞和领一队万花弟子，随南霁云自宁陵借来的援兵杀入睢阳（三千人仅千人得入），万花一队于此折损——南霁云先已求援临淮，贺兰进明不发，断指而去；城中罗雀掘鼠，张巡杀妾以食士。他去睢阳，守的是家乡门户——城蔽遮江淮，后头即庐州合肥（韩愈《张中丞传后叙》：「守一城，捍天下」）":
    "Chen Ruihe led a squad of Wanhua disciples into Suiyang with the relief force Nan Jiyun had borrowed from Ningling (of three thousand men only a thousand got in), and the Wanhua squad was lost there. Nan Jiyun had earlier begged for help at Linhuai, where Helan Jinming would send none, and had cut off a finger and left; inside the city they netted sparrows and dug out rats, and Zhang Xun killed his concubine to feed his soldiers. In going to Suiyang Chen Ruihe was holding the gate of his own home: the city screened the Jiang–Huai lands, and behind it lay Hefei in Luzhou (Han Yu, “Afterword to the Biography of Vice Censor-in-Chief Zhang”: “holding one city, he shielded the empire”).",
  "程锋派驻上党郡":
    "Cheng Feng was posted to Shangdang Commandery.",
  "九月初，燕将蔡希德围上党，程锋出城欲生擒之，桥梁塌陷、为伏兵刺伤所执——「乍可失帅，不可失城」；拒受伪官，押往洛阳城北苑舍严加看管，腰伤自此耽搁":
    "Early in the ninth month the Yan general Cai Xide besieged Shangdang; Cheng Feng went out of the city meaning to take him alive, the bridge collapsed, and he was stabbed and taken by men in ambush: “Better to lose the commander than to lose the city.” He refused the rebels’ office and was taken to the North Park lodgings north of Luoyang and closely guarded; from then on the injury to his back went untreated.",
  "秋，连朔在河西擢旅帅（马邑先登记功在前，随闵方城往河西平乱、留驻凉州有劳）；消息传回雁门，景惠时口中已称「小连旅帅」，年关席上柳戎以「新近升迁」相谑":
    "Autumn: Lian Shuo was promoted Battalion Commander in Hexi (his merit for being first up the wall at Mayi already on record, and on the strength of his service going with Min Fangcheng to put down the rising in Hexi and staying on at Liangzhou); by the time the news reached Yanmen, Jing Huishi was already calling him “little Battalion Commander Lian”, and at the year-end feast Liu Rong teased him about his “recent promotion”.",
  "岚川云自我流放北上苍云":
    "Lanchuan Yun went north to the Cangyun Army in self-exile.",
  "九至十月考课间，狄元恪初任军纪官——旋因擂台一变故，荔非承烈体况危殆退役，二团失主将，由此空降为第二团长官":
    "During the merit review of the ninth and tenth months Di Yuanke first served as provost; soon, after an upset in a challenge bout, Lifei Chenglie was in a critical state and retired, the Second Regiment lost its commander, and he was parachuted in as its commander.",
  "九月二十八日（香积寺之战次日），长安收复":
    "On the twenty-eighth day of the ninth month (the day after the battle of Xiangji Monastery), Chang’an was recovered.",
  "十月初九睢阳城陷，张巡、南霁云等遇害，许远被押往洛阳，城中仅余约四百人；陈瑞和亲历城中最后两个月——罗雀掘鼠之后便是食人，他给「吃剩下的人」接过骨——城陷后以医者身份被留用，混在约四百幸存者中，十六日安庆绪弃洛北走、燕军北撤后脱身":
    "On the ninth day of the tenth month Suiyang fell; Zhang Xun, Nan Jiyun and others were killed, Xu Yuan was taken to Luoyang under escort, and only about four hundred people were left in the city. Chen Ruihe lived through the city’s last two months: after the netting of sparrows and digging out of rats came the eating of people, and he set the bones of “those left over from the eating”. After the city fell he was kept on as a physician and hid among the four hundred or so survivors, getting away when An Qingxu abandoned Luoyang and fled north on the sixteenth and the Yan army withdrew north.",
  "月中 苍云举办仪式（比武擂台＋演兵）":
    "In the middle of the month the Cangyun Army held its ceremony (challenge bouts and a review of troops).",
  "考课结果【擂台一】荔非承烈败于邱鸿 伤重退役／狄元恪空降二团长官，邱鸿为副；狄元恪撞见闵方城刷马／岚川云到苍云时处在人事调动、代际交换期间":
    "Results of the merit review. Bout One: Lifei Chenglie lost to Qiu Hong, was badly hurt and retired / Di Yuanke was parachuted in as commander of the Second Regiment, with Qiu Hong as his deputy; Di Yuanke came upon Min Fangcheng grooming a horse / Lanchuan Yun arrived at the Cangyun Army in the middle of the reshuffle, the changing of the generations.",
  "擂台一细部：荔非承烈带伤不予人知、不欲示弱，饮酒一壶应战；二十合后攻势为邱鸿铁骨衣抗住、反于己身，气海震散吐血倒下，被抬下场，营中哗然；邱鸿大骇，卸盾刀去扶——「我赢的不该是这一场」。景惠时诊得「体如鼓面，一击或闻鸣响，连击即溃，二三年间不得轻动内劲」；闵方城打完自己三场匆匆赶至石室——「你怨我吧」「可不是嘛，那得怨你……我没本事，但咱们的过往在上头，你不许也丢这个人」「咱们都是一样，只知道怎么赢，不懂怎么输」":
    "Bout One in detail: Lifei Chenglie, keeping his injury to himself and unwilling to show weakness, drank a jug of wine and took the bout. After twenty rounds his attacks were held by Qiu Hong’s Iron-Bone Mantle and turned back on himself; the sea of his qi shattered, he coughed blood and fell, and was carried off, and the camp was in uproar. Qiu Hong, horrified, dropped his shield-and-blade to help him: “This isn’t the fight I should have won.” Jing Huishi’s diagnosis: “A body like a drumskin; one blow and it may ring, blow upon blow and it gives way; for two or three years he must not use his inner strength lightly.” Min Fangcheng, having fought his own three bouts, hurried to the stone chamber: “Blame me.” “Of course I blame you … I’m no good any more, but our past is up there, and you’re not to shame it too.” “We’re the same, you and I: we only know how to win, not how to lose.”",
  "擂台一战前（乱后首开考课，已停两年；长安新复，旧柱下场，众目所注，不能告免）：薛褚只对荔非说一句「他的铁骨，返劲了」，荔非一笑置之「那小子？」，伸手拿酒；薛褚不拦，替他系甲，勒紧左肋甲带，正压在河曲所裹之布上；荔非饮酒一壶应战（压肋下之疼，旁人只道豪气）":
    "Before Bout One (the first merit review since the rising, after two years without one; Chang’an newly recovered, the old pillars stepping into the ring, every eye on them, no begging off): Xue Chu said only one thing to Lifei, “His Iron-Bone turns force back now”; Lifei laughed it off, “That lad?”, and reached for the wine. Xue Chu did not stop him, and buckled on his armour for him, pulling the strap at the left ribs tight, right over the cloth he had bound there on the Hequ campaign; Lifei drank a jug of wine and took the bout (to dull the pain under his ribs; others thought it bravado).",
  "擂台一交手：分山对铁骨。前二十合荔非占上风，邱鸿退而入铁骨之静；荔非左肘始终压低护肋；当收不收，全力分山尽数返于己身，撞在旧伤上，吐血倒地不起；邱鸿只挡未击，终生不知长官带伤（营中只道「输了晚辈」）":
    "Bout One, the fight: Mountain-Splitting against Iron-Bone. For the first twenty passes Lifei had the upper hand, and Qiu Hong fell back into the stillness of Iron-Bone; Lifei’s left elbow stayed low the whole time, guarding his ribs. At the moment to pull back he did not, and the full force of his Mountain-Splitting came back on himself and struck the old wound; he coughed blood, went down and did not get up. Qiu Hong only blocked and never struck, and never knew, all his life, that his superior had been carrying a wound (the camp only said “he lost to a junior”).",
  "擂台一倒下之后：景惠时以当值军医首先抢上，解甲见旧布，不言（石室中那声叹息由此多一层）；狄元恪以军纪官于簿上记「荔非承烈，败」，是其入苍云第一件公事；邱鸿大骇，卸了盾刀便去扶，说「我赢的不该是这一场」（依《狄邱樊》原文），扶住时抬头看了薛褚一眼，薛褚不看他；闵方城自己三场打完方至":
    "After the fall in Bout One: Jing Huishi, as physician on duty, was first to reach him, and unbuckling the armour saw the old cloth and said nothing (which gives one more layer to that sigh in the stone chamber); Di Yuanke, as provost, wrote in the register “Lifei Chenglie, defeated”, his first official act in the Cangyun Army; Qiu Hong, appalled, put down his shield-and-blade and went to help him up, saying, “This isn’t the fight I should have won”, and as he held him looked up at Xue Chu, who did not look at him; Min Fangcheng only arrived when his own three bouts were done.",
  "荔非卧石室数日间，东京收复的消息传到雁门，营外庆贺（洛阳十月中下旬收复，传至代北需时日；正文一句带过）":
    "During the days Lifei lay in the stone chamber, news that the Eastern Capital had been recovered reached Yanmen, and there was celebrating outside the camp (Luoyang was recovered in the middle to late part of the tenth month, and the news took time to reach the lands north of Dai).",
  "狄元恪（和樊璋）始学盾刀；狄元恪私下与邱鸿对战，邱鸿胜；关岳暗示狄元恪看盾刀谱学，狄元恪开始刷题（最终武学方面成为教科书性质的苍云）；新官到任各种压力":
    "Di Yuanke (and Fan Zhang) began learning shield-and-blade; Di Yuanke fought Qiu Hong privately, and Qiu Hong won; Guan Yue hinted that Di Yuanke should study from the shield-and-blade manuals, and Di Yuanke began working through them like set exercises (in the end, in the martial arts, he became the Cangyun Army’s textbook case); the pressures of a new officer in post.",
  "闵方城岚川云始有交集（第一次交手，闵方城确认岚川能力），后岚川被任命为教官／闵方城接生马匹，岚川云关岳在场，狄元恪看见":
    "Min Fangcheng and Lanchuan Yun first crossed paths (their first bout, in which Min Fangcheng confirmed what she could do), and Lanchuan Yun was then appointed instructor / Min Fangcheng delivered a foal, with Lanchuan Yun and Guan Yue there, and Di Yuanke saw it.",
  "岚川云纳为营教一事，闵方城见其才，进言统帅便允——原本这等人事该让二、三团长官一并察看考校再上报，闵方城并不经过这个程序；狄元恪去帐中问，闵方城与关岳只说事情已定。狄元恪没有话了，由此了解闵方城在破阵营中地位之超然，因不免有立威之心":
    "On taking Lanchuan Yun on as camp instructor: Min Fangcheng saw her ability, put it to the Commander, and the Commander agreed. By rights such an appointment should have been looked over and tested by the commanders of the Second and Third Regiments together before being reported up, but Min Fangcheng did not go through that procedure; when Di Yuanke went to his tent to ask, Min Fangcheng and Guan Yue said only that the matter was settled. Di Yuanke had nothing more to say, and learned from it how far above the rest Min Fangcheng stood in the Rank-Breaker Corps, and so could not help wanting to assert himself.",
  "十月初唐军进围洛阳，宣杨探得城北苑舍囚系被俘将领（程锋在内），谋营救上报；程凯不顾伤势请命先赴北郊，魏谦伪作侍卫递信、填岗接应。十六夜安庆绪自苑门北走，严庄先行携诛俘之命——程凯出拦，截杀其随从与押令之将、驰返掷首，守军涣散，囚者尽出、苑舍付之一炬；严庄走脱（数日后持铁券降唐，授司农卿），哥舒翰另押，已先被提走遇害。程锋以生执贼庭固求自贬，于李光弼帐前练兵":
    "Early in the tenth month the Tang army advanced to besiege Luoyang, and Xuan Yang found out that captured generals (Cheng Feng among them) were held in the North Park lodgings north of the city, planned a rescue and reported it; Cheng Kai, disregarding his wounds, asked to go first to the northern outskirts, and Wei Qian, posing as a guard, carried messages and filled a post to help them. On the night of the sixteenth An Qingxu fled north through the park gate, and Yan Zhuang went ahead carrying orders to kill the prisoners: Cheng Kai came out to stop him, cut down his attendants and the officer carrying the order, and rode back to throw down the head; the guards scattered, the prisoners all got out, and the park lodgings were put to the torch. Yan Zhuang got away (some days later he surrendered to the Tang with an iron certificate and was made Chief Minister of the Court of the National Granaries); Geshu Han had been held separately and had already been taken away and killed. Cheng Feng, having been taken alive into the rebel court, insisted on asking to be demoted, and drilled troops before Li Guangbi’s tent.",
  "十月十五日新店之战，十八日广平王入东京；天策余部下旬回府":
    "The battle of Xindian on the fifteenth day of the tenth month; on the eighteenth the Prince of Guangping entered the Eastern Capital; the remains of the Tiance army went back to the Command late in the month.",
  "楼谯晋第三团副官（靳沉白之副）（月份推定，从考课人事）":
    "Lou Qiao was promoted deputy of the Third Regiment (Jin Chenbai’s second).",
  "石室中荔非欲荐薛褚接任「替我看着点这些老兄弟」，薛褚未应承；当晚入堡求见统帅，请辞副官，自陈「年来屡屡疏失，不能察知主将异状」（以不知情之说顺下知情之实；套话，统帅只作谦辞读），请回武库修缮甲兵，统帅准；任命狄元恪掌二团、邱鸿为副下得甚速，薛褚稍后方回过味来；闵方城事先半点不知（景惠时见旧布而不言，薛褚此说方得立住）":
    "In the stone chamber Lifei wanted to put Xue Chu forward to succeed him, “keep an eye on these old brothers for me”; Xue Chu would not take it on. That night he went into the stronghold to see the Commander and asked to resign as deputy, saying, “Over the past year I have been negligent time and again, and failed to notice that my commanding officer was not himself” (letting a claim that he did not know carry the fact that he did; a set phrase, which the Commander read only as modesty), and asked to go back to the armoury to repair armour and weapons; the Commander agreed. The appointments, Di Yuanke to head the Second Regiment and Qiu Hong as his deputy, came down so fast that Xue Chu only caught on a little later; Min Fangcheng had known nothing beforehand (Jing Huishi saw the old cloth and said nothing, which is what lets Xue Chu’s account stand).",
  "上皇自成都启程还京，十二月至长安（月份待核）":
    "The retired emperor set out from Chengdu to return to the capital, reaching Chang’an in the twelfth month.",
  "狄元恪挑衅岚川云 二人对擂":
    "Di Yuanke provoked Lanchuan Yun, and the two fought a challenge bout.",
  "荔非承烈败擂后留营处理交接；薛褚请命转回苍云堡武库，从此静水深潭，诸事不问":
    "After losing the bout, Lifei Chenglie stayed in camp to handle the handover; Xue Chu asked to be sent back to the Cangyun stronghold’s armoury, and from then on was still water in a deep pool, asking about nothing.",
  "邱鸿新拜二团副官，提了家乡羊肉欲上广武城闵方城住处，未出帐又停步，暗地交予关岳代为转交，当晚空手入广武请闵方城夜饮——「我不是为了越过荔非将军的。」闵方城看一眼墙上挂的羊肉，又看他：「我知道。」此后邱鸿终怀内疚，从不主动提起这场比试，不以此自傲":
    "Qiu Hong, newly made deputy of the Second Regiment, took mutton from his home country meaning to go up to Min Fangcheng’s quarters at Guangwu Fortress, stopped before he was out of the tent, quietly gave it to Guan Yue to pass on, and that evening went up to Guangwu empty-handed to ask Min Fangcheng to drink with him at night: “I didn’t do it to get past General Lifei.” Min Fangcheng glanced at the mutton hanging on the wall, then at him: “I know.” After that Qiu Hong carried his guilt always, never once brought up the bout himself, and took no pride in it.",
  "程锋九月初守上党为敌所擒，十月十六夜得救出于洛阳北苑，落下腰伤，自知有罪不欲多事，隐忍不延医；两月后实在支撑不住，又值幼子程骞风寒高热、营内军医不力，方着人寻医——陈瑞和恰从睢阳归，闻而前往诊治，由此偶然与程锋相识（762年阵前救护闵方城之缘由此始）":
    "Cheng Feng, captured by the enemy early in the ninth month while holding Shangdang, was rescued from the North Park at Luoyang on the night of the sixteenth of the tenth month with an injured back; knowing he stood guilty and not wanting a fuss, he bore it and sent for no physician. Two months later he could hold out no longer, and with his young son Cheng Qian in a high fever from a chill and the army physicians in the camp no help, he at last had someone find a physician: Chen Ruihe, just back from Suiyang, heard and went to treat them, and so by chance came to know Cheng Feng (the origin of his tending Min Fangcheng on the battlefield in 762).",
  "两京收复后，李庭沄（李庭深同辈幼妹）投身道门，入纯阳":
    "After the two capitals were recovered, Li Tingyun (Li Tingshen’s youngest sister of his generation) took up the Taoist life and entered Chunyang Palace.",
  "荔非得知薛褚请辞、狄元恪受任，比输阵还恼火：「薛季韬，我不见那小子，你自拿了那些簿子去，成全你的贤名。」话重而非裂痕——荔非心里能明白薛褚的选择，只是要一个出口，也只能对老副官这样讲（对闵方城则仍须体面）；薛褚不辩，持簿与狄元恪交接；荔非留营至除夕，始终未见狄元恪":
    "When Lifei learned that Xue Chu had resigned and Di Yuanke been appointed, he was angrier than at losing the bout: “Xue Jitao, I won’t see that lad. Take those registers to him yourself, and keep your name for virtue.” Harsh words, but not a rift: Lifei understood Xue Chu’s choice in his heart; he only needed an outlet, and his old deputy was the only one he could talk to like that (with Min Fangcheng he still had to keep up appearances). Xue Chu did not argue, and took the registers to hand over to Di Yuanke; Lifei stayed in camp until New Year’s Eve and never once saw Di Yuanke.",
  "荔非承烈年底祭拜吕定仪，留营交接至除夕":
    "At the end of the year Lifei Chenglie paid his respects at Lü Dingyi’s grave, staying in camp for the handover until New Year’s Eve.",
  "冬，寄放苍云的赵廷之天策旧甲，由闵方城亲手交予新至的岚川云——外祖父遗甲入手，她才对自己扶危忠臣之后的身份有所认识，愈发知道天策府是她归处，最初没有选错":
    "Winter: Zhao Tingzhi’s old Tiance armour, left in the Cangyun Army’s keeping, was handed by Min Fangcheng himself to the newly arrived Lanchuan Yun. With her grandfather’s armour in her hands she began to understand that she came of a loyal servant who had stood by the realm in its danger, and knew all the more that the Tiance Command was where she belonged, and that she had not chosen wrong in the first place.",
  "年关将近，墨昆（时年十五）摸查前营旗号岗哨后潜入主帐行刺，闵方城已换旗换哨，岚川云察觉、边赛远擒之；闵方城斩其同行者、令其目睹后放走，柳戎缚其手足弃于营外故地":
    "As the year’s end drew near, Mokun (then fifteen) scouted the banners and sentry posts of the forward camp and then slipped into the main tent to kill; Min Fangcheng had already changed the banners and the sentries, Lanchuan Yun noticed, and Bian Saiyuan seized him. Min Fangcheng beheaded his companions, made him watch, and let him go; Liu Rong tied him hand and foot and dumped him outside the camp, on the old ground.",
  "狄元恪因行刺事进言起草：关城军营内外出入一概查考，巡营加严；与军营往来之两蕃商货人等更新文牒（绘像、特征、钤印）":
    "After the assassination attempt Di Yuanke proposed, and drafted, new rules: every coming and going in and around the pass fortress and the camp to be checked, and camp patrols tightened; papers to be renewed for merchants and others of the Two Fan who dealt with the camp (with portrait, distinguishing marks and seal).",
  "两京收复后，雁门县官上表、女卫营统领请功，朝廷旌表景惠时门庭「节义」，景、关两家蠲免税赋（上表约在景惠时携岚川云返雁门前后，旌表随收京后恩赦封赏下达，年关抵代州）；靳沉白自此不复言其心意":
    "After the two capitals were recovered, the magistrate of Yanmen county sent up a memorial and the head of the Women’s Guard Corps asked for recognition of merit, and the court honoured Jing Huishi’s household with the inscription “Integrity and Righteousness”, remitting the taxes of the Jing and Guan families (the memorial went up around the time Jing Huishi brought Lanchuan Yun back to Yanmen; the honour came down with the amnesty and awards after the capitals were recovered, and reached Daizhou at the year’s end); from then on Jin Chenbai never spoke of his feelings again.",
  "至德二载十二月，史思明以所部十三郡及兵八万来降，河东节度使高秀岩亦以所部来降（《通鉴》卷220，作者核）；云中由是复归唐手——此后云州屯田之粮得以南运雁门，见758.6屈突真押粮":
    "Twelfth month of the second year of Zhide: Shi Siming came over to the Tang with the thirteen commanderies and eighty thousand troops under him, and Gao Xiuyan, Military Commissioner of Hedong, also came over with his command (Zizhi tongjian, juan 220); Yunzhong was thus back in Tang hands, and from then on the grain of the Yunzhou military farms could be shipped south to Yanmen (see 758.6, Qutu Zhen escorting grain).",
  // 758
  "约758–759年间，战事大局已定、北方余波渐平，骆文璧从天台山动身北上，海雕随行，抵太原——见到阔别多年的父亲，也见到一个被围城和战乱改变过的城市；她的蓬莱岁月在这满目疮痍的环境里显得极不真实":
    "Some time in 758–759, with the war’s outcome settled and the aftershocks in the north slowly dying down, Luo Wenbi set out north from Mount Tiantai with her sea eagle and reached Taiyuan, seeing her father for the first time in many years and a city changed by siege and war; her years on Penglai seemed utterly unreal in that devastation.",
  "万花谷蒙难，同门闻讯返援；陈瑞和冷静处之，为同辈中砥柱":
    "Wanhua Valley suffered disaster, and its disciples came back on hearing the news to help; Chen Ruihe kept a cool head through it, a pillar of his generation.",
  "唐青阳出师（约757—758，在郭千仞之变后），以青阳代名，冠唐姓；本名从此不用——名册上那个人，他自己抹掉了。他是唐哲队里唯一一个可以走、却留下的人":
    "Tang Qingyang finished his training (around 757–758, after the Guo Qianren mutiny), taking Qingyang in place of his name and Tang as his surname; his own name he never used again: the man on the roll, he had erased himself. He was the only one in Tang Zhe’s squad who could have left, and stayed.",
  "樊璋换洗衣袍时，有人看见那枚犬牙吊坠，说是屠狗之喻，「怕不是舞阳侯后裔。你家将军倒是会藏」——樊璋才意识到自己的樊姓有何渊源。狄元恪当即喝止，过午又有士兵议论，命杖责，自带樊璋入帐：「你觉得我需要靠别人的名声立足？……我若借此扬威，把你推到风口，成了什么人了？」邱鸿帐外静听，无声离去。末了狄元恪握住那犬牙坠子摩挲——「舞阳侯的渊源，你自己可以当是真的，提着这一口气，用功自励。我也盼它是真。是真，你就有祖源有血脉，不是流民野童，谁的家仆。是匣中宝剑，见了天光。」樊璋眼泪都要下来":
    "When Fan Zhang changed his clothes someone saw the dog-tooth pendant and called it an allusion to Fan Kuai, the dog butcher who became Marquis of Wuyang: “He couldn’t be a descendant of the Marquis of Wuyang, could he? Your general’s good at hiding things”; only then did Fan Zhang realise where his surname Fan might come from. Di Yuanke stopped it at once; when soldiers were talking about it again after noon, he had them beaten and took Fan Zhang into his tent himself: “Do you think I need to stand on someone else’s name? … If I used this to make a show of strength and pushed you out into the wind, what kind of man would I be?” Qiu Hong listened quietly outside the tent and left without a sound. At last Di Yuanke took the dog-tooth pendant and rubbed it between his fingers: “The line of the Marquis of Wuyang: you may take it as true for yourself, hold on to that breath, and work at it. I hope it’s true too. If it is, you have forebears and a bloodline, not a refugee, a wild child, anyone’s servant. A precious sword in its case that has seen the light of day.” Fan Zhang almost wept.",
  "除夕一过，荔非承烈离开苍云，称回原籍休养（中下旬岑杜卢方至，恰相错过）；归宁州故里，父母早已亡故；偶然再续旧缘，得一子，自知非可择地安居之人，托族兄收作名下，教养于定安故关外一处坞堡。后至凤翔节度帐前，结识参军吕遂（吕定仪族弟，颇习羌语、知边事），言及苍云军中事多唏嘘——「不如做个游侠，也算能多斩几个敌人，护佑故乡父老」；此后在凤翔三年，二人亲厚":
    "As soon as New Year’s Eve was over Lifei Chenglie left the Cangyun Army, saying he was going back to his native place to rest (Cen Han, Du Zheng and Lu Bingyu arrived in the middle or late part of the month, just missing him). He went home to Ningzhou; his parents were long dead. By chance an old bond was renewed and he had a son; knowing he was not a man who could choose a place and settle, he had a clan cousin enter the boy under his own name, and the boy was brought up in a fortified manor outside the old Ding’an Pass. Later he went to the headquarters of the Fengxiang Military Commission and came to know the administrator Lü Sui (a clan cousin of Lü Dingyi’s, well versed in the Qiang language and in frontier affairs), and sighed a good deal as he spoke of the Cangyun Army: “Better to be a wandering swordsman; at least I could cut down a few more enemies and protect the folk at home.” He stayed three years at Fengxiang, and the two became close.",
  "岑杜与卢秉毓过苍云，住数日：杜徵为闵方城复原吕定仪九原调并记谱；岑菡当面为边赛远取字「舍衡」":
    "Cen and Du, with Lu Bingyu, passed through the Cangyun Army and stayed a few days: Du Zheng reconstructed Lü Dingyi’s Jiuyuan tune for Min Fangcheng and wrote out the notation; Cen Han, there and then, chose Bian Saiyuan’s courtesy name, Sheheng.",
  "卢秉毓送岑杜经太原南归长歌门，见证李庭泽之名刻于明德树下石碑；卢秉毓独自北归，夏返霸刀府库":
    "Lu Bingyu saw Cen and Du home south through Taiyuan to the Changge School, and saw Li Tingze’s name carved on the stone stele under the Mingde Tree; then he went back north alone, and in the summer returned to the Badao armoury.",
  "连朔率部从凉州返苍云（正文时间线首次登场），已是旅帅（757年秋在河西时擢）":
    "Lian Shuo led his men back from Liangzhou to the Cangyun Army (his first appearance in the story’s main timeline), already a Battalion Commander (promoted in the autumn of 757, while he was in Hexi).",
  "（758春）景惠时另设静息帐，收治惊悸、不寐、失语兵士，名目只用医书本有之说；凭旌表名望得以开帐，靳沉白以伤退调养名目相助，贺兰为助手；闵方城从未入帐":
    "In the spring Jing Huishi set up a separate Quiet Breath tent to take in soldiers suffering from palpitations, sleeplessness and loss of speech, naming their conditions only in terms the medical books already had; she was able to open it on the strength of the honour paid to her household, Jin Chenbai helped by entering it as convalescence for the wounded, and He Lan was her assistant. Min Fangcheng never once went into the tent.",
  "连朔驻凉州归；休沐上广武看视母亲姑母，与母亲说做了旅帅、比从前更上一层了（马邑先登记功，757年秋在河西时擢旅帅，至此返营方得归省相告；当了旅帅在外行走始有字——「知晦」为景惠时所取，她知书达理又算长辈，营中不少年轻士兵都是她给取的字）。母亲让他问能否邀闵方城上来坐坐，晚间去请，竟然应了——奶茶、胡饼、炙羊肉，闵方城喝茶吃饼姿态坦然，还与母亲用磕磕绊绊的汉话聊两句羊羔的事；回程连朔脚步轻快，把玩套马索绳头——「你愿意就常上来」，闵方城看他，又看他绕着绳索的前臂，终只叹一口气，没答应也没驳。「什么都发生了，但这个人就是这样，只在长官和公心上和他说话。」他仍然笑着，舌头却在舔舐牙齿——那一天连朔开始有恨，尽管他自己还没认":
    "Back from his posting at Liangzhou, Lian Shuo went up to Guangwu on his day off to see his mother and aunt, and told his mother he had become a Battalion Commander, a step higher than before (his merit for being first up the wall at Mayi was recorded, and he was promoted Battalion Commander in the autumn of 757 while in Hexi, but only now, back in camp, could he go home and tell them; as a Battalion Commander going about outside he now had a courtesy name, Zhihui, chosen by Jing Huishi: she was lettered and counted as an elder, and had chosen courtesy names for many of the young soldiers in the camp). His mother asked him to see whether Min Fangcheng might be invited up to sit with them; he went that evening to ask, and to his surprise Min Fangcheng accepted. Milk tea, Hu flatbread and roast mutton; Min Fangcheng drank the tea and ate the bread quite at his ease, and even talked a little about lambs with his mother in halting Chinese. On the way back Lian Shuo walked with a light step, playing with the end of the lasso: “Come up often, if you like.” Min Fangcheng looked at him, then at his forearm wound with the rope, and in the end only sighed, neither agreeing nor refusing. “Everything has happened, but this man is just like that: he only speaks to him as a superior, and for the common good.” He was still smiling, but his tongue was running over his teeth: that day Lian Shuo began to hate, though he did not admit it to himself yet.",
  "夏，药宗复宗门，孟雪萦拜入门中，行了大礼；也在此间，柳戎并霸刀同门与夏、孟二人结识":
    "Summer: the Beitian School of Medicine restored its school, and Meng Xueying entered it, performing the full rites; it was also then that Liu Rong and her fellow Badao disciples came to know Xia and Meng.",
  "屈突真为苍云押运军粮时受伤，景惠时为之治伤，见其手上腕饰与身边几个孩子；她因745年曾以医官入奚营，略通奚俗奚语。所押之粮自云州来（757.12D高秀岩以河东来降，云中复归唐；是年乾元元年复称云州）——四年后762.10G，同一条路上南来的是云州饥民":
    "Qutu Zhen was hurt while escorting grain for the Cangyun Army, and Jing Huishi treated him, noticing the ornaments on his wrist and the several children with him; having gone into the Xi camps as a medical officer in 745, she knew a little of Xi customs and the Xi language. The grain came from Yunzhou (see 757.12D: Gao Xiuyan came over with Hedong, and Yunzhong was Tang again; that year, the first of Qianyuan, it took back the name Yunzhou). Four years later, at 762.10G, what came south along the same road was starving refugees from Yunzhou.",
  "江蓠闻谷中危难，与同门离天策府返回万花谷——临行不得李庭深回应，伤心而走":
    "Hearing of the danger in the Valley, Jiang Li left the Tiance Command with her fellow disciples to go back to Wanhua Valley; she left heartbroken, without an answer from Li Tingshen.",
  "擂台二 连朔对闵方城 不敌":
    "Bout Two: Lian Shuo against Min Fangcheng; he could not win.",
  "擂台二前后床帷之间，连朔说「你本来也不争功名。一切所得皆偶然，这都是你自己说的。如今既乏了，输给我吧，输给我你就自在了」；闵方城并未松口，那一年仍然没有败绩":
    "Around Bout Two, behind the bed curtains, Lian Shuo said, “You never cared about merit and fame anyway. Everything you’ve got came by chance; you said so yourself. Now you’re tired, so lose to me. Lose to me and you’ll be free.” Min Fangcheng did not give way, and that year he still lost no bout.",
  "九节度讨安庆绪，不置元帅，以鱼朝恩为观军容宣慰处置使；天策随李光弼北上围邺":
    "Nine military commissioners moved against An Qingxu with no supreme commander appointed, Yu Chao’en being made Army Supervisor and Pacification Commissioner; the Tiance army went north with Li Guangbi to besiege Ye.",
  "景惠时观屈突真安抚惊马与受惊孩童（缓近、不直视、守在一旁待其自来），渐以此法施于静息帐兵士；此法来源永不入医案":
    "Jing Huishi watched Qutu Zhen soothe frightened horses and frightened children (approaching slowly, not looking straight at them, staying close by and waiting for them to come of their own accord), and little by little used the same way with the soldiers of the Quiet Breath tent; where the method came from never went into the medical records.",
  "秋，江蓠抵谷，风波已去，惟余惨状；有山石经爆炸而不稳，再度震落，她为落石所伤，腰背错骨——陈瑞和将其救下，细心医治，协助康复，此后一两年间，渐有温情":
    "Autumn: when Jiang Li reached the Valley the storm had passed, leaving only devastation; rocks loosened by explosions fell again, and she was hurt by falling stones, dislocating bones in her lower back. Chen Ruihe got her out, treated her with care and helped her recover, and over the next year or two a tenderness grew between them.",
  "秋，祸乱及江南，灵隐寺首当其冲：鬼山会敌兵闯入禅房杀人夺兵，叶添灯依例解剑在外，赤手难敌，多处受创仍护僧人半步不离；僧奋身为其挡一冷箭，不治——临终言「万念归一，生生不已。兵戈、离散…也是你的功课」。叶添灯奔回山庄取兵器，整日转战不知伤痛疲倦，同门多战死伤残；此后守灵，一连数月和衣抱剑而眠，生怕再来一回让他赤手空拳。剑庐前辈叶泊秋亦战殁于山庄——当年说「修罗刀，菩提道」的人，「那人的血祭了敌人的剑」":
    "Autumn: the turmoil reached Jiangnan, and Lingyin Monastery bore the brunt. Soldiers of the Guishan Society broke into the meditation halls, killing and seizing weapons; Ye Tiandeng, who by custom had left his sword outside, could not hold them bare-handed, and though wounded in many places never left the monks’ side by half a step. A monk threw himself in front of a stray arrow for him and could not be saved; dying, he said: “Ten thousand thoughts return to one, and life goes on without end. War and separation… they are your lessons too.” Ye Tiandeng ran back to the manor for his weapons and fought all day without feeling pain or weariness, and many of his fellow disciples were killed or maimed; afterwards, keeping vigil, he slept for months fully clothed with his sword in his arms, afraid it would come again and find him empty-handed. Ye Boqiu, an elder of the Sword Lodge, also died fighting at the manor: the man who had once said “the blade of the asura, the path of bodhi”, “that man’s blood was offered up to the enemy’s sword”.",
  "秋，卢秉毓为霸刀知情高层逐出师门（缴刀匣、除紫裘）；深秋手无寸铁至苍云关岳帐前，时值考课；关岳寻薛褚商议，薛褚让其暂住己帐，知其锻冶之才、又知闵方城手中用了四五年的环柄陌刀正出于他手，与关岳二人请见统帅——「北地锻冶技法流落在外反是不好」「霸刀山庄处置叛逆，却让匠人留下了他的手」——统帅方许留人在苍云堡武库锻刀":
    "Autumn: Lu Bingyu was driven out of his school by the Badao leaders who knew what had happened (giving up his blade case and stripped of his purple fur cloak); in late autumn, without so much as a knife, he came before Guan Yue’s tent at the Cangyun Army, during the merit review. Guan Yue went to Xue Chu to talk it over, and Xue Chu let him stay in his own tent for the time being; knowing his gift as a smith, and knowing that the ring-pommel modao Min Fangcheng had used for four or five years came from his hands, he and Guan Yue asked to see the Commander: “It does no good for the smithing arts of the north to be lost to the world.” “When Badao Manor dealt with its traitor, it left the craftsman his hands.” Only then did the Commander allow him to stay and forge blades in the armoury of the Cangyun stronghold.",
  "深秋，朱鹭与七秀同门至藏剑协助诊治——见伤重肢残者，忽然想起当年湖畔落雪、神光断臂雪为之红的公案，「她觉得这些人身上都是零零碎碎的神光」；寻叶添灯不遇":
    "Late autumn: Zhu Lu came with her fellow disciples of the Qixiu House to help treat the wounded at Cangjian. Seeing the badly wounded and the maimed, she suddenly remembered the snow by the lake years before, and the story of Shenguang cutting off his arm and the snow turning red: “It seemed to her that all these people were bits and pieces of Shenguang”; she looked for Ye Tiandeng and did not find him.",
  "叶忱在山庄识得前来协助诊治的七秀朱鹭":
    "At the manor Ye Chen came to know Zhu Lu of the Qixiu House, who had come to help treat the wounded.",
  "冬，敌军大部来攻，岚川云提议带骑兵小队出东陉山谷绕后游射、扯散敌阵，只恨不能分身，况苍云配置绝大多数只会步射；连朔卸了重甲、骑马带弓到跟前，看一眼闵方城，不低头也不下马，一笑——「谁说苍云不能骑射的」，驱马随岚川云而去，留闵方城在后望着。（连朔入苍云即弃弓箭、一点不取巧只练盾刀，凭刀上能力从新兵选进破阵营，关岳在这事上也佩服他；飞羽营散后靶场空时自打两组箭，个个红心，看一会转头就走）（文档作758或759年，系年推定）":
    "Winter: the enemy attacked in force. Lanchuan Yun proposed taking a small troop of horsemen out through the valleys of the Eastern Pass to circle behind and harass with arrows, pulling the enemy lines apart; the trouble was she could not be in two places, and nearly all the Cangyun troops could only shoot on foot. Lian Shuo took off his heavy armour, rode up with a bow, glanced at Min Fangcheng, neither lowering his head nor dismounting, and smiled: “Who says the Cangyun Army can’t shoot from horseback?” He rode off after Lanchuan Yun, leaving Min Fangcheng behind watching. (On joining the Cangyun Army Lian Shuo had given up the bow and, taking no short cuts, trained only at shield-and-blade, and on the strength of his blade work was picked from the recruits for the Rank-Breaker Corps; Guan Yue admired him for it too. When the Flying Feather Corps was disbanded and the archery range stood empty, he would shoot two sets of arrows on his own, every one in the red, look a while, then turn and walk away.)",
  "入冬西湖飘雪，叶添灯一觉醒来「看身边剑不像剑，像最初锻它的石头」，操练竟连胜素来不敌的师兄师姐，同辈称大成，其人不喜——「藏器于身待时而动。最需要他动的时候，他身上没有器。那以后的有与无，藏与不藏，也没分别了」。道永因僧人离世消息数日前至灵隐；叶添灯久立佛前，扬剑削去发辫，金冠簪带纷纷坠地——道永为他理发，与他入内见院主":
    "As winter came on snow fell over West Lake, and Ye Tiandeng woke one morning to find “the sword beside him didn’t look like a sword, but like the stone it was first forged from”; at practice he beat, one after another, the senior brothers and sisters he had never been able to beat, and his generation called it mastery, which he did not like: “Keep the tool on your person and wait for the moment to act. When he was most needed to act, he had no tool on him. After that, having or not having, keeping or not keeping, made no difference.” Daoyong had come to Lingyin some days before on hearing of the monk’s death; Ye Tiandeng stood a long time before the Buddha, raised his sword and cut off his queue, and the golden crown, pin and ribbons fell to the floor. Daoyong cut his hair for him and went in with him to see the abbot.",
  "乾元元年冬，平卢节度使王玄志卒，裨将李怀玉（高丽人，即后之李正己）杀玄志之子，推侯希逸为平卢军使，朝廷因授节度副使——史家谓「节度使由军士废立自此始」（《通鉴》卷220）；孟雪萦之父为推立军将之一，后为侯希逸麾下参将":
    "Winter of the first year of Qianyuan: Wang Xuanzhi, Military Commissioner of Pinglu, died, and the subordinate general Li Huaiyu (of Goguryeo descent, later known as Li Zhengji) killed his son and raised Hou Xiyi as commissioner of the Pinglu Army, and the court accordingly made him Vice Military Commissioner; in the words of the Zizhi tongjian (juan 220), “from this time on, military commissioners were set up and deposed by their soldiers”. Meng Xueying’s father was one of the officers who raised him, and later a staff general under Hou Xiyi.",
  // 759
  "天平宝字三年，日本以高元度为迎入唐大使使，取渤海道，随渤海贺正使入唐，迎藤原清河（时已改名河清）归国":
    "In the third year of Tenpyō-hōji Japan sent Kō no Gendo as envoy to bring home the ambassador to the Tang; he took the Bohai route and entered the Tang with the Bohai New Year envoys, to fetch Fujiwara no Kiyokawa (who had by then taken the name Heqing) home.",
  "二月下至三月初，邺城拉锯，血战。叛军北面来援（魏州方向史思明），唐军腹背受敌。魏谦带轻骑外出探敌而被切断包围，自知不活，力保项旌突围报信，自率兵死战，牵制一支叛军使其不得进。项旌回大帐求见李光弼，被监军鱼朝恩挡下——鱼朝恩忌惮李光弼功勋，程凯等天策府兵为李光弼倚重，一样成为靶子——监军不予发兵援护，项旌又驰走乱军之中奔去寻程凯，那自然来不及":
    "From late in the second month to early in the third, the seesaw battle at Ye was fought in blood. Rebel relief came from the north (Shi Siming, from the direction of Weizhou), and the Tang army was attacked front and rear. Wei Qian, out with light horse scouting the enemy, was cut off and surrounded; knowing he would not live, he got Xiang Jing out to carry the news and fought to the death with his men, holding a rebel column so that it could not advance. Xiang Jing went back to headquarters to see Li Guangbi and was stopped by the Army Monitor Yu Chao’en: Yu Chao’en resented Li Guangbi’s merit, and Cheng Kai and the other Tiance soldiers, on whom Li Guangbi relied, became targets too. The Army Monitor would send no troops to their aid, and Xiang Jing galloped off through the chaos to find Cheng Kai; it was, of course, too late.",
  "三月初六安阳河北之战，大风昼晦，两军皆溃。程凯不惜抗命，大军撤退之际携了项旌回寻魏谦，人在相藉尸身中被翻找出来，是伤重力竭而亡":
    "In the battle north of the Anyang River on the sixth day of the third month, a great wind darkened the day and both armies broke. Cheng Kai, defying orders, took Xiang Jing back to look for Wei Qian as the army retreated; he was dug out from among the trampled bodies, dead of his wounds and exhaustion.",
  "相州溃后，郭子仪以朔方军断河阳桥保东京；东京士民散奔山谷；李光弼、王思礼全军以归，李光弼还太原":
    "After the rout at Xiangzhou, Guo Ziyi cut the Heyang Bridge with the Shuofang Army to protect the Eastern Capital; the people of the Eastern Capital fled into the hills and valleys; Li Guangbi and Wang Sili brought their whole armies back, and Li Guangbi returned to Taiyuan.",
  "随李光弼回师太原，程凯抗命受杖罚俸 禁足营帐 偶遇宣杨——宣杨为探宦官监军事入军营，负伤遭捕，反其道假作逃逸而不离大营，藏程凯帐中两日；监军探得帐内藏人、夜投迷香，程凯射杀来人、故意闹出「刺客」之事，李庭深与长史来问，监军不敢再动；宣杨枕下留笺辞行——「失散之人我会为你查。如不得，日后，也一定为你做件事」":
    "Returning to Taiyuan with Li Guangbi’s army, Cheng Kai, flogged and docked pay for defying orders and confined to his tent, chanced upon Xuan Yang: she had got into the camp to look into the eunuch Army Monitor’s affairs, been wounded and caught, and, turning the usual way round, pretended to escape but never left the camp, hiding two days in Cheng Kai’s tent. The Army Monitor found out someone was hidden in the tent and sent knockout incense in at night; Cheng Kai shot the man dead and deliberately made a fuss about an “assassin”, Li Tingshen and the aide came to ask, and the Army Monitor did not dare move again. Xuan Yang left a note under the pillow taking her leave: “I’ll look for the ones you lost. If I can’t find them, some day I’ll certainly do something for you.”",
  "春，靶场上岚川云看见连朔打箭，问过他两句；连朔忽然问「是我不好吗」，岚川云「像在雪地里看见南诏的大象一样看着他」——「什么事啊。你也不像能问出这话来的。」「那他怎么对我那样。」「谁？」两人对视，连朔再没说话":
    "Spring: on the archery range Lanchuan Yun saw Lian Shuo shooting and asked him a couple of things; suddenly Lian Shuo asked, “Is it that I’m no good?”, and Lanchuan Yun “looked at him as if she had seen one of Nanzhao’s elephants in the snow”: “What’s the matter? You don’t seem like someone who’d ask that.” “Then why does he treat me like that?” “Who?” The two looked at each other, and Lian Shuo said nothing more.",
  "四月初八佛诞日，朱鹭至灵隐寺祈福——前夜豪雨，青石洗得能照出人面；见一青袍僧人眉眼与叶添灯如出一辙，只是削了头发，唤住，那僧垂眼合掌见礼，旋身离去。「雨前缝百衲，叶下闭重关」":
    "On the eighth day of the fourth month, the Buddha’s Birthday, Zhu Lu went to Lingyin Monastery to pray for blessing; heavy rain the night before had washed the flagstones until they gave back faces. She saw a monk in a blue-green robe whose brows and eyes were just like Ye Tiandeng’s, only with his hair shaved off, and called out to him; the monk lowered his eyes, put his palms together in greeting, turned and walked away. “Before the rain he mends his patchwork robe; under the leaves he shuts the double gate.”",
  "前营推进，近奚人牧场；景惠时以为牧场孩童诊病为由往来":
    "The forward camp pushed out towards the Xi pastures; Jing Huishi went back and forth on the grounds of treating the pasture children.",
  "乾元二年春，杜甫自东都归华州，途经新安、石壕、潼关，作「三吏」「三别」——《石壕吏》之石壕村在陕州陕县，「急应河阳役，犹得备晨炊」，所征即相州溃后守河阳之役（月份推定）":
    "Spring of the second year of Qianyuan: Du Fu, going back from the Eastern Capital to Huazhou, passed through Xin’an, Shihao and Tongguan and wrote the “Three Officers” and the “Three Partings”. The village of Shihao in “The Officer at Shihao” was in Shan county, Shanzhou, and “I’ll hurry to answer the levy for Heyang; there’s still time to cook the morning meal”: the levy was for the defence of Heyang after the rout at Xiangzhou.",
  "盛夏，父病，狄元恪告假回太原照看服侍。见解暑冰块桶外结霜，忽问来处，账房账册载「代州」；回廊下掀开桶盖，闻得一股淡淡的泥煤矿石般的地下气味——想起苍云堡地窖冰牢与低温库、工兵硝石制冰、冬日自映雪湖采割成样的冰以马队拖回（「早先这也是咱们的生计」，那是薛褚说的）。他站了片刻，将桶盖重新合上；兄长元慎看出异样，他摇摇头。旬日后父病起色，返回雁门":
    "Midsummer: his father fell ill, and Di Yuanke took leave to go home to Taiyuan to look after him. Seeing frost on the outside of the bucket of ice for cooling, he asked suddenly where it came from; the steward’s accounts said “Daizhou”. Under the gallery he lifted the lid and caught a faint underground smell, like peat or ore, and thought of the cellar ice-store and cold stores of the Cangyun stronghold, the sappers making ice with saltpetre, the ice cut in blocks from Yingxue Lake in winter and dragged back by horse trains (“In the old days this was our living too”: Xue Chu had said that). He stood a moment and put the lid back on; his elder brother Yuanshen saw something was wrong, and he shook his head. Ten days later, his father mending, he went back to Yanmen.",
  "元慎借答谢骆家馈赠之名设一席便饭，请骆家父女来坐。狄元恪执礼周全而心不在此——刚在后院冰桶上闻到苍云堡地窖的气味——对年轻女子只有一个礼节性的目光交接；骆文璧看他，看到的是「端正」两个字：每一条线都是直的、紧的，不同于她见惯的道士的松垮、渔民的粗放、蓬莱剑客的飘逸。樊璋帐前侍立，事后忍不住说：「二郎，骆家那位小娘子……好像练过功夫。」「嗯。」樊璋把剩下的话咽了回去":
    "Yuanshen, by way of thanking the Luo family for their gifts, gave a simple dinner and asked Luo and his daughter to come. Di Yuanke observed every courtesy, but his mind was elsewhere (he had just smelled the cellars of the Cangyun stronghold on the ice bucket in the back courtyard), and gave the young woman only a polite meeting of the eyes; Luo Wenbi, looking at him, saw two words, “upright and correct”: every line in him straight and taut, unlike the slackness of the Taoists she was used to, the roughness of fishermen, the airiness of Penglai swordsmen. Fan Zhang, standing in attendance, could not help saying afterwards: “Erlang, that young lady of the Luo family… I think she’s trained in martial arts.” “Mm.” Fan Zhang swallowed the rest of what he had to say.",
  "鱼朝恩以相州之败短郭子仪，召还京师；李光弼代为朔方节度、兵马副元帅；天策随李光弼至东都、回府":
    "Yu Chao’en blamed Guo Ziyi for the defeat at Xiangzhou, and he was recalled to the capital; Li Guangbi took his place as Military Commissioner of Shuofang and Deputy Supreme Commander; the Tiance army went with Li Guangbi to the Eastern Capital and back to the Command.",
  "李光弼弃东都，移军河阳：天策府所出粮草马匹与军械（李庭深两年间在府中经营）随军输入河阳，府城再度空置；东京官民西撤入关、入陕；程凯等随李光弼殿后，夜过石桥入河阳三城；史思明入洛阳，屯白马寺南，筑月城于河阳南":
    "Li Guangbi abandoned the Eastern Capital and moved his army to Heyang: the grain, horses and weapons produced by the Tiance Command (built up by Li Tingshen over two years in the Command) went with the army to Heyang, and the Command stood empty once more; the officials and people of the Eastern Capital withdrew west into the passes and into Shan; Cheng Kai and others covered the rear with Li Guangbi, crossing the stone bridge into the three cities of Heyang by night; Shi Siming entered Luoyang, camped south of Baima Monastery and built a crescent fort south of Heyang.",
  "擂台三（闵方城下场受下级军官挑战，众所瞩目）：闵方城为求速效向景惠时讨猛药，前夜、晨间两服麻黄；连朔自贺兰处得知，午间顺口嘱伙房于闵方城那碗羊肉汤饼多下姜、秦椒；上场发作，输头一合后翻盘，险杀连朔；连朔：「你把我当过人吗」":
    "Bout Three (Min Fangcheng stepped down into the ring to take challenges from junior officers, with every eye on him): wanting quick relief, Min Fangcheng asked Jing Huishi for a strong medicine and took two doses of ephedra, the night before and that morning; Lian Shuo learned of it from He Lan, and at noon casually told the kitchen to put more ginger and Qin pepper in Min Fangcheng’s bowl of mutton noodle soup. In the ring it took effect: he lost the first round, then turned the bout round and nearly killed Lian Shuo. Lian Shuo: “Did you ever treat me as a person?”",
  "擂台三细部：连朔知舆论大于事实，只要闵方城今年「输掉」的结果便足动摇其名——于药食动手脚；景惠时其时正以麻黄为闵方城速效治关节冷痛，连朔原只想令其发汗失准、乍热乍冷格外不适，并非欲毒伤。闵方城输了头一合，一瞬想「输了也罢了，左右是自己教出来的」，而见关岳神情，念及关山、薛直青眼与「恒」字，卯起翻盘，一力降十会将连朔砸至台沿；该收手的气口没收，反手擎盾直奔颈侧，正砸锁骨——连朔飞出台下数步，肋断至少两根，仰面躺着，嘴角渗血，眼里却含一种笑。下来对闵方城说：「我早该知道你是这样的人。喜欢了纵着捧着，不喜欢了就杀。敌人和情人一回事，我算是看清楚了。你把我当过人吗。」":
    "Bout Three in detail: Lian Shuo knew that talk counted for more than fact, and that the mere result of Min Fangcheng “losing” that year would be enough to shake his name, so he tampered with the medicine and the food. Jing Huishi was then giving Min Fangcheng ephedra for quick relief of cold pain in his joints, and Lian Shuo had only meant to make him sweat and lose his precision, hot and cold by turns and especially uncomfortable, not to poison or injure him. Min Fangcheng lost the first round and for an instant thought, “Losing is fine too; he’s my own pupil, after all,” but then he saw Guan Yue’s face, and thought of Guan Shan, of the favour Xue Zhi had shown him and of the character Heng in his name, threw everything into turning it round and, brute strength beating skill, smashed Lian Shuo to the edge of the ring. At the breath where he should have held back he did not; he brought the shield up backhand straight at the side of the neck and struck the collarbone. Lian Shuo flew several paces off the stage and lay on his back with at least two ribs broken and blood at the corner of his mouth, but a kind of smile in his eyes. Coming down, he said to Min Fangcheng: “I should have known what kind of man you are. When you like something you indulge it and hold it up; when you don’t, you kill it. Enemy and lover, it’s all one to you; now I see it plainly. Did you ever treat me as a person?”",
  "当晚闵方城帐中心悸自汗、伏案昏沉，只传岚川云——到这一步，这个外来者竟成了他在军营里最信任的人；岚川云自景惠时处取药救急，关岳在场。岚川云由汤饼（伙房曾对关岳言连旅帅交代）推到连朔，问「把柄」——「我不必知道那是什么」。岚川云复命时略去姜椒一节，景惠时断为闵方城犯忌口（肉面五辛），自责":
    "That night in his tent Min Fangcheng had palpitations and cold sweats and slumped over his desk, half conscious, and sent only for Lanchuan Yun: it had come to this, that the outsider had become the person he trusted most in the camp. Lanchuan Yun fetched medicine from Jing Huishi for the emergency, with Guan Yue there. From the soup (the kitchen had told Guan Yue it was Battalion Commander Lian’s instruction) Lanchuan Yun worked back to Lian Shuo, and asked about the “hold”: “I don’t need to know what it is.” Reporting back, Lanchuan Yun left out the ginger and pepper, and Jing Huishi, concluding that Min Fangcheng had broken his dietary prohibitions (meat noodles and the five pungent spices), blamed herself.",
  "狄元恪以擂台本该点到为止而闵方城几杀旅帅，欲按军纪查闵方城下手过重；闵方城不肯以遭暗算自辩，连朔亦不能告（否则汤饼事出），查问无苦主，闵方城不许而罢":
    "Di Yuanke, holding that a challenge bout should stop at a touch and that Min Fangcheng had nearly killed a Battalion Commander, wanted to investigate Min Fangcheng under military law for using excessive force; Min Fangcheng would not defend himself by saying he had been tricked, and Lian Shuo could not complain either (or the soup would come out); with no injured party to question, and Min Fangcheng refusing, it was dropped.",
  "河阳之战（十月四日史思明至城下）：白孝德单骑斩刘龙仙，李光弼以牝马诱敌马、拒火船，李抱玉守南城，荔非元礼出战羊马城；天策府兵随李光弼守河阳":
    "The battle of Heyang (Shi Siming reached the walls on the fourth day of the tenth month): Bai Xiaode rode out alone and beheaded Liu Longxian, Li Guangbi lured the enemy’s horses with mares and fended off the fire ships, Li Baoyu held the south city, and Lifei Yuanli sallied out at the outer works; the Tiance soldiers held Heyang with Li Guangbi.",
  "连朔得知闵方城压下狄元恪查问（亦使自己逃过），当面爆发：「怕输，怕被谁知道，怕辜负谁！…为什么一定要钉在这里，又为什么不走呢？…愿意爱什么人，就…爱什么人。」闵方城不答":
    "When Lian Shuo learned that Min Fangcheng had quashed Di Yuanke’s inquiry (which had let him off too), he blew up at him to his face: “Afraid of losing, afraid of someone finding out, afraid of letting someone down! … Why do you have to stay nailed here, and why don’t you just go? … Whoever you want to love, then… love them.” Min Fangcheng did not answer.",
  "擂台三后，连朔于堡内靶场再与岚川云比射（「你回去么」）；数日后借风寒入医帐，向景惠时透露闵方城取向及枕边绸包玉牌，景惠时夜泣（系年推定：759.9擂台后、760.9前）":
    "After Bout Three, Lian Shuo shot against Lanchuan Yun again on the range inside the stronghold (“Are you going back?”); a few days later, using a chill as his excuse to go to the medical tent, he let Jing Huishi know of Min Fangcheng’s leanings and of the jade token in a silk pouch by his pillow, and Jing Huishi wept that night.",
  "河阳守城，营中执炊者有自陕州石壕一带急征而来的老妪；项旌守的是自己的故乡（注：暗合《石壕吏》「急应河阳役，犹得备晨炊」）":
    "Holding the city of Heyang: among those cooking in the camp were old women levied in haste from around Shihao in Shanzhou; what Xiang Jing was defending was his own home country (note: a quiet echo of “The Officer at Shihao”: “I’ll hurry to answer the levy for Heyang; there’s still time to cook the morning meal”).",
  "景惠时为闵方城调方治冷痛（停用麻黄），目光掠过枕边绸包——玉牌绳结为她当年所打；她不言，闵方城未觉":
    "Jing Huishi adjusted a prescription for Min Fangcheng’s cold pains (stopping the ephedra), and her eyes passed over the silk pouch by his pillow: the knot in the jade token’s cord was one she had tied years before. She said nothing, and Min Fangcheng did not notice.",
  "杜甫自同谷入成都，次年于浣花溪畔筑草堂，前后居蜀约四年":
    "Du Fu came from Tonggu into Chengdu, and the next year built his thatched cottage by the Huanhua Stream; in all he lived in Shu about four years.",
  // 760
  "此前两年间营州或为叛军所困、或为游牧民族袭扰，虽军将勇武、屡溃来敌，终究疲敝；孟雪萦坚持之下，夏明沧与其同出宗门返营州救护军民，二人更在孟父跟前行礼，定了终身":
    "For the past two years Yingzhou had been now besieged by the rebels, now harried by nomads, and though its officers were brave and drove off the enemy again and again, it was worn out in the end; at Meng Xueying’s insistence, Xia Mingcang left the school with her to go back to Yingzhou to tend soldiers and people, and the two of them made their bows before her father and pledged themselves for life.",
  "上元元年正月，党项羌寇边":
    "First month of the first year of Shangyuan: the Dangxiang Qiang raided the frontier.",
  "上半年，狄元恪在太原成婚，夫人骆氏讳文璧、字荆山，蓬莱门派中人。他一向饷银归家用，除按规矩报苍云堡内留档外，营中除樊璋无人知此事，也不许樊璋说，自然免了纳礼。婚后返苍云，行囊是樊璋收拾的——文璧趁人不注意把一只海螺（或珊瑚小镇纸）塞进包袱，不是当面赠送，而是让它自己出现在行李中；樊璋在苍云打开包袱看到，问二郎这是什么，狄元恪看一眼，认出不是自己的东西，也就明白了来路。没有丢掉，放在案上。樊璋没再多问，但从此知道：夫人是有些心思的，只是二郎未必接得住":
    "In the first half of the year Di Yuanke married at Taiyuan; his wife was of the Luo family, named Wenbi, courtesy name Jingshan, of the Penglai school. He had always sent his pay home for the household; apart from the record kept on file in the Cangyun stronghold as the rules required, no one in the camp but Fan Zhang knew of it, and Fan Zhang was not allowed to tell, so the customary wedding gifts were naturally spared. Back at Cangyun after the wedding, it was Fan Zhang who had packed his bags: when no one was looking Wenbi had slipped a conch shell (or a small coral paperweight) into the bundle, not giving it to him face to face but letting it turn up by itself in his luggage. Fan Zhang, opening the bundle at Cangyun, asked Erlang what this was; Di Yuanke glanced at it, saw it was not his, and understood where it had come from. He did not throw it away, but set it on his desk. Fan Zhang asked no more, but knew from then on: the lady had her own heart in things, only Erlang might not know how to catch it.",
  "景惠时为牧场奚人求情，闵方城准许；靳沉白在旁（为十月求情之先例）":
    "Jing Huishi pleaded for the Xi of the pastures, and Min Fangcheng granted it; Jin Chenbai was there (the precedent for her plea in the tenth month).",
  "六月置凤翔节度使（首任崔光远，李鼎继之）；荔非入凤翔节度幕当在此后":
    "In the sixth month the Fengxiang Military Commission was set up (first Cui Guangyuan, then Li Ding); Lifei must have joined the Fengxiang commission’s staff after this.",
  "六月至十一月党项、羌屡屡寇边，苍云分兵协防凤翔、朔方、坊州、邠州等地，破阵营建制不动（分兵如至凤翔，须避开荔非）；墨昆与舅父探知破阵营防务吃紧":
    "From the sixth to the eleventh month the Dangxiang and Qiang raided the frontier again and again, and the Cangyun Army split off troops to help defend Fengxiang, Shuofang, Fangzhou, Binzhou and other places, leaving the establishment of the Rank-Breaker Corps untouched (any troops sent to Fengxiang would have to keep clear of Lifei); Mokun and his maternal uncle found out that the Rank-Breaker Corps’ defences were stretched.",
  "靳沉白以利军口吻私下向闵方城进言：屈突真往来关城内外数载，宜设法整饬，以防生变；不说破私情，闵方城无暇细想":
    "Jin Chenbai, speaking as if for the good of the army, privately advised Min Fangcheng that Qutu Zhen had been going in and out of the pass fortress for several years and something should be done to regulate it, in case of trouble; he did not speak of the affair, and Min Fangcheng had no time to think about it.",
  "景惠时与屈突真「有了一回」（八月中，正文不写）；边赛远巡前营撞见，岚川云令其绝口不提；靳沉白或隐约知道，不言":
    "Jing Huishi and Qutu Zhen “had a time together” (the middle of the eighth month; the story does not write it); Bian Saiyuan, patrolling the forward camp, came upon them, and Lanchuan Yun ordered him never to speak of it; Jin Chenbai perhaps half knew, and said nothing.",
  "东陉雪岭 闵方城山洞杀连朔":
    "On the snowy ridges of the Eastern Pass, Min Fangcheng killed Lian Shuo in a cave.",
  "对面山体高处，监视唐军动向的奚人／狼牙斥候自结构相似的狭长岩洞缺口，望见两个披苍云军甲胄的兵将厮杀、一人最终倒地；其中一人听到连朔最后的喊声，似乎正是闵方城的大名——此人后精神失常，被擒讯问时说出「高大的汉将杀了自己人」之类话，遂有一团换防出关即被传唤回堡问话诸事":
    "From high on the mountain opposite, Xi / Langya scouts watching the Tang army’s movements looked through the mouth of a long, narrow cave much like it and saw two officers in Cangyun armour fighting, and one of them at last fall; one of the scouts heard Lian Shuo’s last shout, and it seemed to be the very name of Min Fangcheng. That man later lost his mind, and when he was caught and questioned said things like “the tall Han general killed one of his own”: hence the First Regiment being summoned back to the stronghold for questioning as soon as it rotated out beyond the pass, and all that followed.",
  "奚人探子被擒 岚川云讯问 传言汉将杀自己人":
    "A Xi spy captured; Lanchuan Yun questioned him; the rumour that a Han general had killed one of his own.",
  "景惠时处置闵方城左肩匕首伤，见其角度不似敌刺，不言":
    "Jing Huishi treated the dagger wound in Min Fangcheng’s left shoulder, saw that its angle was not like an enemy’s thrust, and said nothing.",
  "是年考课停办，擂台空缺（分兵协防、前营吃紧）":
    "That year the merit review was not held, and the bouts were left empty (troops split off to help defend elsewhere; the forward camp stretched).",
  "月初 墨昆袭雁门关复仇事件起始 破阵营二团无妄之灾 狄元恪被误认为闵方城而受重创 樊璋重伤 邱鸿断臂":
    "Early in the month: the start of Mokun’s raid on Yanmen Pass for revenge; disaster out of nowhere for the Second Regiment of the Rank-Breaker Corps; Di Yuanke, taken for Min Fangcheng, was badly wounded; Fan Zhang gravely wounded; Qiu Hong lost an arm.",
  "袭关战中，樊璋以身作盾一路护卫狄元恪到前营指挥，自己因消耗过大而昏迷数日；有他相助，狄元恪受伤虽重，至少免于性命之忧，而苍云前营又因狄元恪尚能支撑指挥而未散，保住地界不被攻破":
    "In the fighting at the pass Fan Zhang made himself a shield and guarded Di Yuanke all the way to the forward camp to take command, then fell unconscious for several days from exhaustion; with his help Di Yuanke, though badly hurt, was at least out of danger of his life, and because Di Yuanke could still hold on and command, the Cangyun forward camp did not break and its ground was not overrun.",
  "袭关细部：墨昆方知闵方城不在前营，撤兵时命人留下皮绳、鹿骨、铜铃等牧民佩物，指向屈突真与友奚牧场；闵方城自雪岭救起邱鸿，俘部分敌兵与屈突真等牧民押回，关入冰牢；归途想起荔非承烈醉骂：守得再牢，「不过在墙下翻土」；景惠时闻屈突真入狱，手上的药碗掉在地上":
    "The raid in detail: Mokun, learning only then that Min Fangcheng was not at the forward camp, had his men leave behind as they withdrew things herders wear (leather cords, deer bones, bronze bells), pointing to Qutu Zhen and the friendly Xi pastures. Min Fangcheng rescued Qiu Hong from the snowy ridge and brought back some enemy soldiers as prisoners together with Qutu Zhen and other herders, and shut them in the ice prison; on the way back he remembered Lifei Chenglie’s drunken curse: hold it as tight as you like, “you’re only turning over the dirt under the wall”. When Jing Huishi heard that Qutu Zhen had been jailed, the medicine bowl fell from her hands.",
  "闵方城冤杀屈突真等奚众 景惠时痛揭疑窦":
    "Min Fangcheng wrongly put Qutu Zhen and other Xi to death; Jing Huishi, in grief, laid bare the doubts.",
  "主帐议罪：岚川云、边赛远重查交战山谷，得皮绳、鹿骨、铜铃；景惠时认出皮绳花纹不是屈突真之物，却不能言其所以知；岚川云称证物「到不了个人身上，定罪处斩不妥」；闵方城：「吕爻先膝，邱衔芦臂，这些年没的手足，找个人背，应当的。」岚川云问「薛帅也会如此吗」——「当初是他让我去。」":
    "Judgement in the main tent: Lanchuan Yun and Bian Saiyuan searched the valley of the fighting again and found the leather cords, deer bones and bronze bells; Jing Huishi saw that the pattern on the leather cord was not Qutu Zhen’s, but could not say how she knew; Lanchuan Yun said the evidence “can’t be pinned on any one man; sentencing them to death isn’t right”. Min Fangcheng: “Lü Yaoxian’s knee, Qiu Xianlu’s arm: the hands and feet we’ve lost all these years, someone has to carry them. That’s only right.” Lanchuan Yun asked, “Would Commander Xue have done the same?” “It was he who told me to go, back then.”",
  "军前处斩：景惠时再度求情不得，当众质问「当真这是你刀下唯一无辜之人吗」「连朔之死是否也如此」；关岳起身站到二人中间；边赛远私问「将军杀两蕃与狼牙，何错之有」，岚川云按下他：「忠与不忠不是此时此刻可算的」；靳沉白旁观此间一切，细细写了文书呈报苍云堡；闵方城抬手：「斩。」":
    "Execution before the army: Jing Huishi pleaded again in vain, and asked him in front of everyone, “Is this truly the only innocent man under your blade?” “Was Lian Shuo’s death like this too?” Guan Yue rose and stood between the two of them; Bian Saiyuan asked under his breath, “The general kills the Two Fan and the Langya; what’s wrong with that?”, and Lanchuan Yun held him back: “Loyal or disloyal isn’t something to be reckoned here and now.” Jin Chenbai watched all of it and wrote a careful report to the Cangyun stronghold; Min Fangcheng raised his hand: “Behead them.”",
  "狄元恪不顾重伤赶去阻止：「狼牙兵可杀，但牧人平民，证据不凿，就是屠戮。苍云军没有这样规矩！」闵方城：「墙够高，城门够严，人还是冤伤冤死。不能出关，不能寻仇。」狄元恪转身欲报统帅，闵方城看了关岳一眼；关岳一时顿住，终将狄元恪带离，一半拉扯一半扶着——「此时此地有闵将军，当然不与你相干！但此时此地之后…要与你相干的事可不少。」狄元恪伤口迸裂，吐血昏厥，被抬回寝帐":
    "Di Yuanke, regardless of his grave wounds, hurried to stop it: “Langya soldiers may be killed, but herders are civilians; without solid evidence it’s slaughter. The Cangyun Army has no such rule!” Min Fangcheng: “The walls are high enough, the gates strict enough, and still people are wrongly wounded and wrongly killed. We can’t go out beyond the pass; we can’t seek revenge.” Di Yuanke turned to report to the Commander; Min Fangcheng glanced at Guan Yue; Guan Yue hesitated a moment, then took Di Yuanke away, half dragging, half holding him up: “Here and now there’s General Min, so of course it’s nothing to do with you! But after here and now… there’ll be plenty to do with you.” Di Yuanke’s wound burst open, he coughed blood and fainted, and was carried back to his tent.",
  "事后：闵方城押入堡内冰牢，景惠时以无据妄言受责。关岳：「邱鸿拼掉一条胳膊，换来什么？……那个帮我们押送军粮的牧民被一刀砍了头，所有人改了嘴脸！我不明白。」岚川云：「将军的令，叫你拦下狄将军，你如何了？」「那是两回事。」岚川云又道：「此事是我欠他。」":
    "Afterwards: Min Fangcheng was taken into the stronghold and held in the ice prison, and Jing Huishi was reprimanded for baseless, reckless talk. Guan Yue: “Qiu Hong gave up an arm, and for what? … The herder who helped us escort grain had his head cut off with one stroke, and everyone changed their faces! I don’t understand.” Lanchuan Yun: “The general’s order was for you to stop General Di; what did you do?” “That’s a different thing.” Lanchuan Yun went on: “I owe him for this.”",
  "闵方城羁押待罪 后幽居 景惠时停职问话 狄元恪掌破阵营事；二团士兵于伙房、寝帐私语传议闵方城事，狄元恪军前杖责，罪名不言其事；夜调阵亡名籍":
    "Min Fangcheng held awaiting sentence, and later kept in seclusion; Jing Huishi suspended and questioned; Di Yuanke in charge of the Rank-Breaker Corps. Soldiers of the Second Regiment whispered and passed on talk of the Min Fangcheng affair in the kitchens and sleeping tents, and Di Yuanke had them beaten before the army, without naming the matter in the charge; at night he called up the rolls of the dead.",
  "战后二三日，樊璋昏迷中「魇住」——身如铁板，牙关紧咬，手指半握如仍抓盾带，本能抵住针不肯露出缝隙；贺兰言「气不肯归，恐伤元神」「怕是从功夫心法上来的」。狄元恪带伤径奔苍云堡，统帅台前单跪：「末将请暂释罪将闵恒三刻功夫……倘有违制，都在末将身上。」长孙忘情许之。闵方城自冰牢被带出——面色泛青，耳垂只剩环痕，腕上链痕——入帐揽樊璋起身，点按肩井、胸骨、脊线，掌覆后心：「放手，樊璋，放手。」樊璋咳出一口乌血，整个身子松了下来，像一捆柴被剪去捆它的麻绳。「这是好了？他因何这样？」「铁骨衣。」「荒唐。尚未修得，先要把人迫死。」闵方城如若不闻，出帐时对追来的关岳只说一句：「我该早醒。」":
    "Two or three days after the battle Fan Zhang, still unconscious, was “locked”: his body stiff as an iron plate, jaws clenched, fingers half closed as if still gripping a shield strap, by instinct resisting the needles and giving them no gap. He Lan said, “His qi won’t come back; I’m afraid it will harm his spirit”, and “I think it comes from his martial method.” Di Yuanke, wounded as he was, went straight to the Cangyun stronghold and knelt on one knee before the Commander’s dais: “I ask that the condemned officer Min Heng be released for three quarters of an hour … If it breaks the rules, let it all fall on me.” Zhangsun Wangqing granted it. Min Fangcheng was brought out of the ice prison (his face blue-grey, nothing left at his earlobes but the marks of his rings, chain marks on his wrists), went into the tent and raised Fan Zhang up, pressed the points at the shoulders, the breastbone and along the spine, and laid his palm on the middle of his back: “Let go, Fan Zhang, let go.” Fan Zhang coughed up a mouthful of black blood and his whole body went slack, like a bundle of firewood with the twine cut. “Is he well now? Why was he like that?” “Iron-Bone.” “Absurd. Not even learned yet, and already it’s crushing him to death.” Min Fangcheng seemed not to hear; leaving the tent, he said only one thing to Guan Yue, who came after him: “I should have woken sooner.”",
  "邱鸿断臂后昏迷，二团伤亡惨重、医帐调度紧张，贺兰虽牵挂万分只能一日几遍汤药膏药；薛褚自堡内赶往寝帐看顾安抚，为其梳头剃须保持洁净。半月后邱鸿方醒，闻师父羁押欲往见，勉强走到帐门，一遭风雪腿软晕眩跪地喘缓，终摇头——「营中局面，再叫人见我这样还去寻师父，愈发要多些揣测」；薛褚扶他回榻：「是你心真。」":
    "After losing his arm Qiu Hong lay unconscious; the Second Regiment had heavy losses and the medical tents were stretched, and He Lan, though worried sick, could only bring decoctions and plasters a few times a day; Xue Chu came from the stronghold to his tent to look after and comfort him, combing his hair and shaving him to keep him clean. Only after half a month did Qiu Hong wake; hearing that his master was in custody he wanted to go to him, struggled as far as the tent door, met the wind and snow, went weak and dizzy and knelt on the ground to get his breath back, and at last shook his head: “The way things are in the camp, if people see me going to find my master like this, there’ll only be more guessing.” Xue Chu helped him back to bed: “Your heart is true.”",
  "景惠时痛揭所用皆医者所知：医帐中连朔所言、伤口所见，破了医帐的封口；回帐呕酸不止，岚川云以为悲恸，未知其有孕（受孕约在八月中）":
    "Everything Jing Huishi used in laying bare the doubts was what only a physician could know: what Lian Shuo had said in the medical tent, what she had seen in wounds; she broke the seal of the medical tent. Back in her tent she could not stop retching, and Lanchuan Yun took it for grief, not knowing she was with child (conceived around the middle of the eighth month).",
  "景惠时停职期间，医帐由贺兰调度；她教贺兰以绳结记录兵士情状，唯医者能读":
    "While Jing Huishi was suspended, the medical tent was run by He Lan; she taught He Lan to record the soldiers’ conditions with knotted cords, which only physicians could read.",
  "邱鸿养伤 挣扎摇摆 关外歌谣风传（11月后一个月左右）":
    "Qiu Hong recovering, struggling and wavering; songs going round from beyond the pass (for about a month from the eleventh month).",
  "下旬 邱鸿向狄元恪请辞 狄元恪绝望气怒；岚川云调停缓和，暂留邱鸿为教官，并假托邱鸿之名请战，预备新岁演阵一场，以定军心":
    "Late in the month: Qiu Hong asked Di Yuanke to let him resign; Di Yuanke, in despair, flew into a rage. Lanchuan Yun mediated and calmed things, kept Qiu Hong on for the time being as an instructor, and asked in Qiu Hong’s name to take the field, preparing a formation exercise for the new year to steady the army.",
  "狄元恪肩上带伤、数日未眠、面色灰败、嗓子喑哑；元慎上来看他——「小樊那孩子愿意留下，挣个功名，也罢了。你。你也有了家室，未必非得留在这里。」「我知道。」「你一味地只说知道。」狄元恪起身走到帐门口，看山上的关城南大门——那门像百戏艺人的机关镜匣：门北是杀伐、边野、无尽的雪，从门里一过，万事万物荡涤尽净，变成木桶里的冰，莹白透明地送到府门面前。「长兄，你可知道咱们府上夏天用的那些冰块……是哪里来的吗。」":
    "Di Yuanke, a wound in his shoulder, sleepless for days, grey in the face, hoarse; Yuanshen came up to see him: “If young Fan wants to stay and earn himself some merit, well and good. You. You have a family now; you don’t have to stay here.” “I know.” “All you ever say is that you know.” Di Yuanke got up, went to the tent door and looked at the great south gate of the pass fortress up the mountain: the gate was like a variety performer’s trick mirror box. North of it, killing, the wild frontier, endless snow; pass through the gate, and everything is washed clean and turned into ice in a wooden bucket, delivered white and clear to the door of the house. “Elder brother, do you know where the ice we use at home in summer… comes from?”",
  "关岳于广武镇救民女陶氏（后为其妻）":
    "Guan Yue rescued a young woman of the Tao family at Guangwu town (later his wife).",
  "邱鸿在薛褚协助下恢复和渐渐回到正轨，并发现樊璋显现出铁骨衣根骨（薛褚知757年擂台实情，邱鸿终生不知；照料中有不言之偿，正文不点破）":
    "With Xue Chu’s help Qiu Hong recovered and gradually got back on track, and found that Fan Zhang showed the aptitude for Iron-Bone (Xue Chu knew the truth of the 757 bout; Qiu Hong never knew it all his life; in Xue Chu’s care for him there is an unspoken repayment, which the story leaves unsaid).",
  "薛褚早期陪练协助邱鸿恢复，又为其打制肩盾最初雏形，琢磨革带固定之法，先作配重使用，使邱鸿持刀维持力线中正，不至左右失衡耗损脊柱":
    "In the early days Xue Chu sparred with Qiu Hong to help him recover, and made the first rough shape of a shoulder shield for him, working out how to fix it with leather straps and using it at first as a counterweight, so that Qiu Hong could keep his line of force centred when holding the blade and not wear out his spine from being off balance.",
  "近年关，狄元恪自觉邱鸿的事该亲自向闵方城交待一句，傍晚上广武城；到时闵方城正劈柴打捆，又蹲在踩实的雪地上用小树枝写「方城」、写「关」，笔画刮下粉状的雪，像给什么釉面雕花——那字歪斜僵硬，就像他手里枯枝的形状，狄元恪小时候刚学书写的字不过如此。闵方城起身，脚在雪地上碾了几下，裘衣下摆把字迹遮去些，定定看着他。狄元恪在栽歪矮门外站着，想起太原家府书房里当世书家的泼墨与满柜的书，愣住，半晌忽然笑了一下，敛起神情摇摇头：「罢了。将军……将军安好。」转身离去":
    "Near the year’s end Di Yuanke felt he should tell Min Fangcheng about Qiu Hong himself, and went up to Guangwu at dusk. When he got there Min Fangcheng was splitting and bundling firewood; then he squatted on the trodden snow writing with a twig, the characters of his name, Fangcheng, and the character for “pass”, the strokes scraping up powdery snow like a pattern carved on a glaze. The writing was crooked and stiff, like the shape of the dry twig in his hand; Di Yuanke’s own, when he first learned as a child, had been no worse. Min Fangcheng got up, scuffed the snow a few times with his foot, let the hem of his fur coat cover some of the writing, and looked at him steadily. Di Yuanke, standing outside the crooked little gate, thought of the splashed ink of the great calligraphers of the day and the cabinets full of books in the study of his family’s house in Taiyuan, stood stunned, and after a long while suddenly smiled, composed his face and shook his head: “Never mind. General… be well, General.” He turned and left.",
  // 761
  "江蓠与陈瑞和成婚":
    "Jiang Li and Chen Ruihe married.",
  "演阵后破阵营主帐，关岳正位：流言「折翅难任」今已勘破，二团副将之职仍归邱鸿；邱鸿去闵方城幽居处见他，二人饮酒，一扇窗吹开，闵方城抬头，见岚川云下马立在栅栏外":
    "After the formation exercise, in the main tent of the Rank-Breaker Corps, with Guan Yue presiding: the rumour “a broken wing can’t bear the post” has now been seen through, and the post of deputy of the Second Regiment stays with Qiu Hong. Qiu Hong went to see Min Fangcheng where he lived in seclusion, and the two drank; a window blew open, Min Fangcheng looked up, and saw Lanchuan Yun, dismounted, standing outside the fence.",
  "演阵前夜，邱鸿在苍云堡地下冰室「坐禅」凝神聚气；薛褚早知他会如此，从武库到冰室传内力与他，又与卢秉毓一同备兵甲——皮革护垫、肩盾及调配重量的刀具。邱鸿摩挲革垫肩盾，问「季韬将军，还是只想做无名匠人么」，自取炉边铁叉，夹起铸台铁印烙「韬」字于革垫一角——「如此，在下还是个全身」；薛褚握其伤侧肩头：「……你啊。」":
    "The night before the formation exercise Qiu Hong sat in meditation in the ice cellar under the Cangyun stronghold, gathering his qi; Xue Chu, who had known he would, came from the armoury to the ice cellar to pass him inner strength, and with Lu Bingyu got his arms and armour ready: leather pads, the shoulder shield, and blades with their weight adjusted. Qiu Hong ran his hand over the leather pad and the shoulder shield and asked, “General Jitao, do you still only want to be a nameless craftsman?”, then took the iron fork by the furnace, picked up the iron stamp from the forging bench and branded the character Tao on a corner of the pad: “There. Now I’m still a whole man.” Xue Chu gripped him by his injured shoulder: “… You.”",
  "上旬 演阵 邱鸿强出但可以坚持 终得再次自立；狄元恪重骑马槊在场压阵":
    "Early in the month: the formation exercise; Qiu Hong pushed himself but could hold out, and at last stood on his own again; Di Yuanke, as heavy cavalry with his lance, anchored the field.",
  "演阵之日：墨昆一事后狄元恪养伤兼杂冗，久未在校场现身，士兵不知他会如何——却看他出阵，人马俱甲从关城走出，执旧日长槊，端严雍容，正是从前被老兽医一眼当作故统帅的披挂，一时士兵震肃；当场暗为邱鸿压阵、引导，助其重新自立。统帅堡内闻此，似有一口气经久未舒，自语：「总算值得。」":
    "The day of the exercise: since the Mokun affair Di Yuanke, recovering from his wounds and taken up with odd duties, had long not appeared on the drill ground, and the soldiers did not know what he would do; then they saw him ride out of the pass fortress, man and horse in armour, holding his long lance of old, stern and stately: the very harness in which the old horse doctor had once at a glance taken him for the late Commander. The soldiers were awed. There and then he quietly anchored the formation for Qiu Hong and guided him, helping him to stand on his own again. The Commander, hearing of it in the stronghold, seemed to let out a breath long held, and said to herself: “Worth it at last.”",
  "奴剌、党项消息传出 凤翔节度幕府书信求援（荔非暗中促成，不具名；闵方城至凤翔帐前方知其未归田）【预警】 岚川云代闵方城求情 请统帅许闵带兵出；苍云方面不欲外人知晓去岁主力军动荡，兼之破阵营未稳，狄、靳二将此刻不得离营，便仍命闵方城戴罪与关岳旧制整军拔营":
    "News of the Nula and the Dangxiang got out; the staff of the Fengxiang Military Commission wrote asking for help (Lifei had quietly brought this about, without signing his name; Min Fangcheng only learned that he had not gone back to the land when he came before the tent at Fengxiang) [content warning]. Lanchuan Yun interceded for Min Fangcheng and asked the Commander to let him lead troops out; the Cangyun side did not want outsiders to know of the upheaval in its main force the year before, and with the Rank-Breaker Corps still unsettled Di and Jin could not leave camp at this point, so it still ordered Min Fangcheng, under the cloud of his offence, to put the troops in order on the old establishment with Guan Yue and break camp.",
  "景惠时问话已结，自请随军赴凤州为军医，女卫营准；无人知其有孕（约五月，裹于冬袍）":
    "Jing Huishi’s questioning was over, and she asked to go with the army to Fengzhou as a physician, which the Women’s Guard Corps allowed; no one knew she was with child (about five months, hidden under her winter robe).",
  "上元二年二月，奴剌、党项寇宝鸡，烧大散关，南侵凤州，杀刺史，大掠而西；凤翔节度使李鼎追击，破之":
    "Second month of the second year of Shangyuan: the Nula and the Dangxiang raided Baoji, burned the Dasan Pass, pushed south into Fengzhou, killed the prefect, plundered widely and went west; Li Ding, Military Commissioner of Fengxiang, pursued and defeated them.",
  "凤州之战 闵方城见荔非承烈 景惠时身亡（设定2月中）":
    "The battle of Fengzhou; Min Fangcheng saw Lifei Chenglie; Jing Huishi died.",
  "北邙之败：李光弼囤兵北邙待决战，原应据邙山之险列兵，最后却无奈列于平原上；程凯、李庭深死谏而不能违拗。邙山败，又失河阳、怀州等地。程凯此役后伤势复发":
    "The defeat at Beimang: Li Guangbi had massed troops at Beimang for a decisive battle; they should have drawn up on the strong ground of Mount Mang, but in the end had no choice but to draw up on the plain; Cheng Kai and Li Tingshen remonstrated to the death but could not overturn it. After the defeat at Mount Mang, Heyang, Huaizhou and other places were lost too. After this battle Cheng Kai’s wounds broke out again.",
  "凤州：景惠时为救边赛远而死（边赛远初生时曾受她哺乳，二人皆不知）；岚川云收殓时方知其有孕，对谁都不说（对闵方城说无意义，对关岳等徒增其痛）；靳沉白或隐约知道，亦不说；景惠时以节妇之身归葬（关山之侧），旌表无损":
    "Fengzhou: Jing Huishi died saving Bian Saiyuan (when he was newborn she had nursed him at her breast; neither of them knew). Only when Lanchuan Yun laid her out for burial did she learn that she had been with child, and she told no one (telling Min Fangcheng would mean nothing; telling Guan Yue and the others would only add to their pain); Jin Chenbai perhaps half knew, and also said nothing. Jing Huishi was buried as a chaste widow (beside Guan Shan), the honour paid her untouched.",
  "春起（推定），邱鸿断臂后自知力有不逮，见樊璋有根骨，向闵方城、狄元恪提出令樊璋修铁骨衣；狄元恪数年观闵、邱二人，明白铁骨衣分量，初不忍加诸樊璋，然念其护卫赴救诚是赤子之心，终由之——唯樊璋日课打坐冰室时偶往一瞧。761–763年间，邱鸿一面传授樊璋武技，一面徐徐劝说闵方城「传灯不绝」；闵方城念吕定仪孤绝不传艺、荔非草草退隐，渐渐回过劲来，欲寻第三条路":
    "From the spring, Qiu Hong, knowing after losing his arm that his strength fell short, and seeing that Fan Zhang had the aptitude, proposed to Min Fangcheng and Di Yuanke that Fan Zhang train in Iron-Bone; Di Yuanke, who had watched Min and Qiu for years, understood what Iron-Bone weighed and at first could not bear to put it on Fan Zhang, but thinking that his guarding and his rescue had truly come from a child’s pure heart, in the end let it be, only going now and then to look in when Fan Zhang sat at his daily meditation in the ice cellar. Through 761–763 Qiu Hong taught Fan Zhang martial skills while slowly persuading Min Fangcheng that “the lamp must be passed on unbroken”; Min Fangcheng, thinking how Lü Dingyi in his solitude had passed his art to no one and Lifei had retired in haste, gradually came round, and wanted to find a third way.",
  "闵方城返回雁门，仍幽居至次年九月":
    "Min Fangcheng went back to Yanmen, still in seclusion until the ninth month of the following year.",
  "邙山败后，鱼朝恩、卫伯玉退保陕州（李光弼、仆固怀恩渡河保闻喜）；史思明遣史朝义为前锋攻陕，屡为神策军节度使卫伯玉所败于礓子岭；思明怒欲按军法，朝义惧，与部将骆悦等缢杀思明于鹿桥驿":
    "After the defeat at Mount Mang, Yu Chao’en and Wei Boyu fell back to hold Shanzhou (Li Guangbi and Pugu Huai’en crossed the river to hold Wenxi); Shi Siming sent Shi Chaoyi as vanguard to attack Shan, and he was beaten again and again at Jiangzi Ridge by Wei Boyu, Military Commissioner of the Shence Army; Siming in anger meant to punish him under military law, and Chaoyi, afraid, with his officer Luo Yue and others, strangled Siming at the Luqiao post station.",
  "北邙败后天策残部西退陕州，归鱼朝恩、卫伯玉节制——府城再失，河阳亦陷，西撤为唯一之路；史朝义攻陕，天策随神策守城，功归卫伯玉；程凯伤重随军；项旌家眷自河阳西逃至陕（注：天策第二次流亡，驻陕至762年十月会师）":
    "After the defeat at Beimang the Tiance remnant withdrew west to Shanzhou, under the command of Yu Chao’en and Wei Boyu: the Command lost again and Heyang fallen too, going west was the only road. When Shi Chaoyi attacked Shan, the Tiance men held the city with the Shence Army, and the credit went to Wei Boyu; Cheng Kai, badly wounded, went with the army; Xiang Jing’s family fled west from Heyang to Shan (note: the Tiance Command’s second exile, stationed at Shan until the armies joined in the tenth month of 762).",
  "陕州城中有华州彩戏班流寓，乃齐晟父族旧班；守城间奏《秦王破阵乐》，天策府兵于神策旗下闻之（注：秦王即天策上将）":
    "In the city of Shanzhou there was a variety troupe from Huazhou living as refugees, the old troupe of Qi Sheng’s father’s family; during the defence of the city they played “The Prince of Qin Breaks the Ranks”, and the Tiance soldiers heard it under the Shence banners (note: the Prince of Qin was the Supreme General of Heavenly Strategy, the Tiance Shangjiang).",
  "蓟门杀胡事件":
    "The killing of the Hu at Jimen.",
  "东川节度副使、梓州刺史段子璋反，袭节度使李奂于绵州，自称梁王、改元黄龙；五月西川节度使崔光远与李奂讨平，崔部将花惊定纵兵大掠东川（待核）":
    "Duan Zizhang, Vice Military Commissioner of Dongchuan and prefect of Zizhou, rebelled, attacked the Military Commissioner Li Huan at Mianzhou, called himself Prince of Liang and changed the era name to Huanglong; in the fifth month Cui Guangyuan, Military Commissioner of Xichuan, and Li Huan put him down, and Cui’s officer Hua Jingding let his troops loose to plunder Dongchuan.",
  "闵方城、岚川云映雪湖畔沐马（此前闵跪李牧祠碑前；对谈前之沉默，与762.4驯捕野马成对）（月份推定）":
    "Min Fangcheng and Lanchuan Yun washed the horses by Yingxue Lake (before this Min had knelt before the stele at the Li Mu shrine; the silence before their talk, a pair with the breaking-in of wild horses at 762.4).",
  "天平宝字五年八月，高元度自唐归：唐以「残贼未平，道路多难」不放河清，令元度取南路先归，于苏州造船、遣沈惟岳等送之；唐帝（肃宗）言禄山乱后兵器多亡，托求牛角造弓——十月，日本令东海、东山、北陆、山阴、山阳、南海诸道贡牛角七千八百只（注：可与天策之弓相勾连）":
    "Eighth month of the fifth year of Tenpyō-hōji: Kō no Gendo came back from the Tang. Saying that “the remnant rebels are not yet put down and the roads are full of danger”, the Tang would not let Heqing go, and had Gendo go home first by the southern route, building ships at Suzhou and sending Shen Weiyue and others to see him off; the Tang emperor (Suzong) said that since An Lushan’s rising many weapons had been lost, and asked for ox horn to make bows. In the tenth month Japan ordered the Tōkaidō, Tōsandō, Hokurikudō, San’indō, San’yōdō and Nankaidō circuits to send seven thousand eight hundred ox horns.",
  "林叶矢之父的家书随高元度带回日本，是叶矢动身的引信":
    "Hayashi Kyōya’s father’s letter home was carried back to Japan by Kō no Gendo; it was the spark that set Kyōya off.",
  "考课【擂台四】照常举行，狄元恪主持；台上已无旧柱（闵方城幽居，荔非已去）（正文一句带过）":
    "The merit review (Bout Four) was held as usual, presided over by Di Yuanke; there were no old pillars on the stage any more (Min Fangcheng in seclusion, Lifei gone).",
  "秋，狄元恪与骆文璧双生一子一女出生于太原":
    "Autumn: twins, a son and a daughter, were born to Di Yuanke and Luo Wenbi at Taiyuan.",
  "闵方城与岚川云对谈 一切过去【有怨无悔】":
    "Min Fangcheng and Lanchuan Yun talked: all of it in the past (“Resentment Without Regret”).",
  "是年末，严武首镇剑南，为成都尹（月份待核）":
    "At the end of the year Yan Wu took up his first post in Jiannan, as Governor of Chengdu.",
  "上元二年冬十二月，平卢节度使侯希逸「与范阳相攻连年，救援既绝，又为奚所侵，乃悉举其军二万余人袭李怀仙，破之，因引兵而南」（《通鉴》）——走陆路，非渡海；营州自此陷于奚、契丹，唐廷不复实控":
    "Twelfth month, winter, of the second year of Shangyuan: Hou Xiyi, Military Commissioner of Pinglu, “having fought Fanyang year after year, with relief cut off and harried by the Xi besides, raised his whole army of more than twenty thousand, fell upon Li Huaixian and defeated him, and then led his troops south” (Zizhi tongjian): by land, not across the sea. From then on Yingzhou fell to the Xi and the Khitan, and the Tang court no longer truly held it.",
  "营州陷落：侯希逸主力南袭范阳，孟雪萦之父留营州为其断后，战亡；奚人据城，圈禁遗留百姓，擒杀残兵；柳戎等霸刀塞北营驰援已迟，救下悲愤欲以身撞敌刀的孟雪萦——夏明沧诊之，方知她初有身孕（时闵方城尚在幽居，苍云不预其事；闵方城事后方从柳戎口中听闻，「有人得救了」）":
    "The fall of Yingzhou: as Hou Xiyi’s main force went south to attack Fanyang, Meng Xueying’s father stayed at Yingzhou to cover his rear and was killed; the Xi took the city, penned in the people left behind and hunted down and killed the remnant soldiers. Liu Rong and the others of Badao’s Saibei Corps came to help too late, and saved Meng Xueying, who in grief and fury meant to throw herself onto the enemy’s blades; Xia Mingcang examined her, and only then learned that she was newly with child (Min Fangcheng was still in seclusion then, and the Cangyun Army had no part in this; Min Fangcheng heard of it afterwards from Liu Rong: “someone was saved”).",
  // 762
  "崔旰（后名崔宁）因裴冕事被召入京，严武荐为利州刺史，治盗":
    "Cui Gan (later named Cui Ning) was summoned to the capital over the Pei Mian affair; Yan Wu recommended him as prefect of Lizhou, to put down the bandits.",
  "宝应元年正月，侯希逸「于青州北渡河而会田神功、能元皓于兖州」（《通鉴》）":
    "First month of the first year of Baoying: Hou Xiyi “crossed the river north of Qingzhou and joined Tian Shengong and Neng Yuanhao at Yanzhou” (Zizhi tongjian).",
  "孟雪萦赶去城外交战处敛父遗骨，全了丧礼；与夏明沧返宗门，柳戎置办车马自请同行一程；途中孟雪萦心力交瘁、高热腹痛，暂居荒村空房，夏明沧出外寻药，柳戎救邻人回来时杀死来劫孟雪萦的匪盗，然其受惊，孩儿终究未能保下——醒转时还叫夏明沧不要责怪柳戎；返宗门后细心照料，又请老萨满医治，缓缓养了半年方复原（约至762年秋）":
    "Meng Xueying hurried to the battlefield outside the city to gather her father’s bones and gave him full funeral rites; she went back to the school with Xia Mingcang, and Liu Rong got carts and horses together and asked to go part of the way with them. On the road Meng Xueying, worn out in body and mind, ran a high fever with pains in her belly, and they stopped for a while in an empty house in an abandoned village; Xia Mingcang went out to look for medicine, and Liu Rong, coming back from rescuing a neighbour, killed bandits who had come to seize Meng Xueying, but she had had a fright, and in the end the child could not be saved. When she came to she still told Xia Mingcang not to blame Liu Rong; back at the school he cared for her closely, and also asked an old shaman to treat her, and she slowly recovered over half a year (until about the autumn of 762).",
  "闵方城、岚川云驯捕野马【夏日牧场】；关岳与民女陶氏成婚":
    "Min Fangcheng and Lanchuan Yun broke in wild horses (“The Summer Pasture”); Guan Yue married the young woman of the Tao family.",
  "宝应元年五月，以侯希逸为平卢、青、淄等六州节度，「由是青州节度有平卢之号」（《通鉴》）——平卢之名移于青州，营州故地不复（底色：孟父推立之节度、为之断后而死之城，名号与土地自此脱钩；大历年间朝廷追赠孟父，无人接旨）":
    "Fifth month of the first year of Baoying: Hou Xiyi was made Military Commissioner of the six prefectures of Pinglu, Qing, Zi and others, and “from this the Qingzhou commission bore the name Pinglu” (Zizhi tongjian): the name Pinglu moved to Qingzhou, and the old lands of Yingzhou were gone (Background: the commissioner Meng’s father had helped raise, the city he had died covering the rear for: name and land were parted from then on; in the Dali years the court posthumously honoured Meng’s father, and there was no one to receive the edict).",
  "严武奉召入朝，剑南兵马使徐知道据成都拒之，月余为部将所杀；程铎与徐知道同僚，从朝廷，却发现自己营里已有人跟了徐知道——一个年年管军纪的人，军纪在自己营里失效（按：月份待核）。底色：从754年唐青阳走后，营里没人再替他把军令讲给兵听":
    "Yan Wu was summoned to court, and Xu Zhidao, Commander of Troops of Jiannan, seized Chengdu to keep him out, and a month or so later was killed by his own officers; Cheng Duo, Xu Zhidao’s colleague, sided with the court, but found that some in his own camp had already followed Xu Zhidao: a man who had kept army discipline year after year, and discipline had failed in his own camp. Background: since Tang Qingyang left in 754, no one in the camp had explained his orders to the soldiers for him.",
  "天平宝字五年所任遣唐使，六年四月遣唐船至难波江口触滩损坏而罢；改遣中臣鹰主为送唐人使，七月以风波无便不得渡海，又罢":
    "The envoys to the Tang appointed in the fifth year of Tenpyō-hōji: in the fourth month of the sixth year the embassy ship ran aground and was damaged at the mouth of the Naniwa river, and the mission was called off; Nakatomi no Takanushi was sent instead as envoy to escort the Tang people home, and in the seventh month, with no fair wind or sea, he could not cross, and that too was called off.",
  "林叶矢等不到官船，家中已无人，遂决意孤身出海寻父":
    "Unable to wait for an official ship, and with no one left at home, Hayashi Kyōya resolved to go to sea alone to look for his father.",
  "闵方城与邱鸿说 在当年9月考课后 据樊璋表现而定传功与否":
    "Min Fangcheng told Qiu Hong that after that year’s merit review in the ninth month he would decide, by how Fan Zhang did, whether to pass on his art.",
  "高适代严武为成都尹、西川节度使，至 764 年（待核；月份不详，系于七月严武入朝、徐知道之乱后）":
    "Gao Shi took Yan Wu’s place as Governor of Chengdu and Military Commissioner of Xichuan, until 764.",
  "八月，回纥登里可汗受史朝义所诱，倾国南下；至三城北，见边城无戍、州县空虚，有轻唐之志，遣人收单于府兵马仓粮，辱中使刘清潭；清潭奏「倾国自来，有众十万」，京师震骇（据《旧唐书·回纥传》）":
    "Eighth month: the Uighur Tengri Qaghan, enticed by Shi Chaoyi, came south with his whole nation; north of the Three Cities, seeing the frontier towns ungarrisoned and the prefectures and counties empty, he grew contemptuous of the Tang, sent men to take over the troops, horses, granaries and grain of the Chanyu Protectorate, and insulted the palace envoy Liu Qingtan; Qingtan reported that “he has come with his whole nation, a hundred thousand strong”, and the capital was thrown into alarm (after the Old Book of Tang, Biography of the Uighurs).",
  "考课 擂台五 樊璋果有所成（时闵方城尚在幽居，统帅特许观考）":
    "The merit review, Bout Five: Fan Zhang had indeed come into his own (Min Fangcheng was still in seclusion at the time; the Commander gave him special leave to watch).",
  "考课期间 樊璋还在台上时 薛直昔年坐骑摔伤后致死 闵方城抱马痛哭 传功一事未成；事后闵方城卧病，期间得统帅文书许其病愈归营":
    "During the merit review, while Fan Zhang was still on the stage, Xue Zhi’s old warhorse was hurt in a fall and died of it; Min Fangcheng held the horse and wept bitterly, and the passing on of his art did not happen. Afterwards Min Fangcheng lay ill, and while he was ill received a letter from the Commander allowing him back to the camp once he recovered.",
  "考课未毕、樊璋还在台上，士兵悄声急报，闵方城当即离席——被岚川云派去的士兵叫去马厩，薛直昔年坐骑摔伤，他就在那里跪守三五日，老马死去，哀痛逾甚，呕血昏厥，此后病下直到洛阳整军。那边樊璋连胜而闵方城未在场，许诺落空；狄元恪在旁不解、又不禁暗恼，四处找人，被岚川云截住，带上广武城后山老马掩埋之处，说了缘故":
    "With the merit review not yet over and Fan Zhang still on the stage, a soldier brought urgent word in a whisper and Min Fangcheng left his seat at once: he had been called to the stables by a soldier Lanchuan Yun sent; Xue Zhi’s old warhorse had been hurt in a fall. He knelt there keeping watch for three or five days; when the old horse died his grief went beyond bearing, he vomited blood and fainted, and was ill from then until the army mustered at Luoyang. Meanwhile Fan Zhang won bout after bout with Min Fangcheng not there, and the promise came to nothing; Di Yuanke, looking on, could not understand it and could not help being quietly angry, and went looking everywhere for him, until Lanchuan Yun stopped him, took him up to the hill behind Guangwu where the old horse was buried, and told him why.",
  "苍云点兵组建行军，与诸节度会兵洛阳，一团规模约三百人；仍命闵方城为主将，调狄元恪随行，岚川云在团内；破阵营暂由关岳代领，靳沉白、邱鸿、樊璋等留守":
    "The Cangyun Army mustered a marching force to join the military commissioners’ armies at Luoyang, one regiment of about three hundred men; Min Fangcheng was again made its commander, Di Yuanke was ordered to go with it, and Lanchuan Yun was in the regiment; the Rank-Breaker Corps was put for the time being under Guan Yue, with Jin Chenbai, Qiu Hong, Fan Zhang and others staying behind.",
  "九月（推定，月内先后待定），回纥自单于府南下，过代北赴忻、太，苍云奉命开关放行（作者定）。①其时敌友未明：代宗即位之初遣中使刘清潭往回纥修好征兵，纸面上是应召之援；而回纥实为史朝义所诱而来，至三城北见州县空虚，收单于府兵马仓粮、辱中使，清潭密奏「倾国自来，有众十万」，京师震骇——「友军」之名要到药子昂迎劳于忻州南、仆固怀恩在太原会可汗之后才谈定（见762.9E），回纥过雁门时尚未定。②路线：药子昂迎于太原以北、忻州以南，可知回纥取代州—忻州一道，须过勾注山、经雁门（推定，史无明文；旧作「不入雁门关城」，今改）。③雁门见其北来，举烽示警、关城戒严，烽是当敌情举的（回纥眼里河东「边城无戍」，雁门的烽是有人守的）。④河东节度转来朝命：回纥应召讨贼，所过勿阻——苍云全军上城，严兵以待，开关，看其一队队过关，不交兵，守到最后一骑出关。这是苍云的旧伤：745年外族破关，755年弃关西去，此番奉命亲手开关，让一支谁也信不过的胡骑从关下走过。河东对回纥的戒心由此可见：怀恩在太原会可汗时，辛云京闭城、不犒师（见762.9E）；北归时再度闭城不与相闻（763.2A）。⑤其时闵方城因老马之死病卧（762.9B），不在城上，只听得关下马蹄数日不绝；城上望见者宜邱鸿（云中人，识得北来之路）。北归时同一道关门再开一回，见763.3B":
    "In the ninth month the Uighurs came south from the Chanyu Protectorate, passing through the lands north of Dai on their way to Xin and Tai, and the Cangyun Army was ordered to open the pass and let them through. (1) At the time it was not clear whether they were friend or foe. At the start of his reign Daizong had sent the palace envoy Liu Qingtan to the Uighurs to renew friendship and ask for troops, so on paper they were allies answering a summons; but the Uighurs had in fact come at Shi Chaoyi’s invitation, and north of the Three Cities, seeing the prefectures and counties empty, had taken over the troops, horses and granaries of the Chanyu Protectorate and insulted the palace envoy, and Qingtan had sent a secret report that “he has come with his whole nation, a hundred thousand strong”, throwing the capital into alarm. The name of “allied army” was only settled after Yao Zi’ang welcomed them south of Xinzhou and Pugu Huai’en met the qaghan at Taiyuan (see 762.9E); when the Uighurs passed Yanmen it was still unsettled. (2) The route: since Yao Zi’ang met them north of Taiyuan and south of Xinzhou, the Uighurs must have taken the Daizhou–Xinzhou road, which has to cross Mount Gouzhu and pass Yanmen. (3) When Yanmen saw them coming from the north, it raised the beacons in alarm and put the pass fortress on alert; the beacons were lit as for an enemy (in Uighur eyes the frontier towns of Hedong were “ungarrisoned”; Yanmen’s beacons had men keeping them). (4) The Hedong Military Commission passed on the court’s order: the Uighurs were answering a summons to fight the rebels, and were not to be hindered on their way. The whole Cangyun Army went up on the walls and waited under arms, opened the pass, and watched them go through troop by troop, without crossing blades, holding on until the last rider had gone through. This was the Cangyun Army’s old wound: in 745 foreigners had broken the pass, in 755 it had abandoned the pass and gone west, and now, under orders, it opened the pass with its own hands to let a horde of Hu riders no one trusted pass beneath it. Here one can see Hedong’s wariness of the Uighurs: when Huai’en met the qaghan at Taiyuan, Xin Yunjing shut the city and gave the army no feast (see 762.9E); on their way back north he shut it again and would have nothing to do with them (763.2A). (5) At the time Min Fangcheng lay ill after the death of the old horse (762.9B) and was not on the walls; he only heard the hoofbeats below the pass go on for days without end. The one on the walls who sees it should be Qiu Hong (a man of Yunzhong, who knew the road from the north). On their way back north the same gate of the pass opened once more; see 763.3B.",
  "九月（推定，在回纥过雁门之后），殿中监药子昂迎劳于太原以北、忻州以南，密点其众：丁壮约四千、老弱万余、马四万（号称与实数相去甚远）；仆固怀恩自汾州赴太原，与可汗及可敦（怀恩女）相见，河东节度使辛云京以可汗乃怀恩婿，恐其合谋袭军府，闭城自守，亦不犒师（《通鉴》卷223，广德元年追叙）。议进军：蒲关—沙苑、土门、怀州太行诸路皆不从，终取陕州太阳津渡河，就食太原仓粟（仓在陕州，非太原府），与泽潞、河南、怀郑诸军会（据《旧唐书·回纥传》）":
    "In the ninth month, after the Uighurs had passed Yanmen, Yao Zi’ang, Director of the Palace Administration, went to welcome them north of Taiyuan and south of Xinzhou, and secretly counted their numbers: about four thousand able-bodied men, more than ten thousand old and weak, forty thousand horses (far from the figure claimed); Pugu Huai’en came from Fenzhou to Taiyuan and met the qaghan and the qatun (Huai’en’s daughter), and Xin Yunjing, Military Commissioner of Hedong, since the qaghan was Huai’en’s son-in-law and he feared they might plot together to fall upon his headquarters, shut the city and held it, and gave the army no feast either (Zizhi tongjian, juan 223, told in retrospect under the first year of Guangde). On the line of advance: the Puguan–Shayuan, Tumen and Huaizhou–Taihang routes were all refused, and in the end they crossed the river at the Taiyang ford of Shanzhou, to be fed from the Taiyuan granary (the granary was at Shanzhou, not at Taiyuan), joining the armies of Ze–Lu, Henan and Huai–Zheng (after the Old Book of Tang, Biography of the Uighurs).",
  "闵方城、岚川云等整军赴洛阳（十月末大决战）昭觉寺 闵方城重伤":
    "Min Fangcheng, Lanchuan Yun and the others put the army in order and went to Luoyang (the great decisive battle at the end of the tenth month); at Zhaojue Monastery Min Fangcheng was gravely wounded.",
  "雍王李适为天下兵马元帅，会诸道节度使及回纥于陕州；雍王诣回纥可汗营，可汗责其不蹈舞，药子昂以嫡皇孙、二宫在殡辞之，回纥遂鞭药子昂、李进、韦少华、魏琚各一百，少华、琚一夕而死；官军欲讨回纥，雍王以贼未灭止之":
    "Li Kuo, Prince of Yong, was made Supreme Commander of the armies of the realm, and met the military commissioners of all the circuits and the Uighurs at Shanzhou; the Prince of Yong went to the Uighur qaghan’s camp, and the qaghan rebuked him for not performing the dance of obeisance; Yao Zi’ang excused him on the grounds that he was the emperor’s eldest grandson in the direct line and that two sovereigns lay unburied, whereupon the Uighurs gave Yao Zi’ang, Li Jin, Wei Shaohua and Wei Ju a hundred lashes each, and Shaohua and Ju died that night; the government army wanted to attack the Uighurs, but the Prince of Yong stopped them because the rebels were not yet destroyed.",
  "诸军发陕州，三路进讨史朝义：仆固怀恩与回纥为前锋，郭英乂、鱼朝恩为殿，出渑池；潞泽李抱玉自河阳入；李光弼自陈留入；雍王留陕州坐镇":
    "The armies set out from Shanzhou to move against Shi Chaoyi by three routes: Pugu Huai’en and the Uighurs as vanguard and Guo Yingyi and Yu Chao’en as the rear, out through Mianchi; Li Baoyu of Lu–Ze in from Heyang; Li Guangbi in from Chenliu; the Prince of Yong stayed at Shanzhou in command.",
  "天策残部编入郭英乂、鱼朝恩后殿出渑池，李庭深随军；程凯伤重留守陕州雍王行营，燕军小股袭扰行营与三门漕路，程凯力疾拒之，伤势复重；李庭深在陕州闻雍王受辱、韦少华魏琚死（注：程凯回府后「因伤不得行动」由此，见《程家系列》【7】；史书无陕州遭袭之载，规模宜小）":
    "The Tiance remnant was put into the rear guard of Guo Yingyi and Yu Chao’en going out through Mianchi, with Li Tingshen going with the army; Cheng Kai, badly wounded, stayed behind at the Prince of Yong’s field headquarters at Shanzhou; small bands of Yan troops harried the headquarters and the Sanmen grain-transport road, and Cheng Kai, forcing himself up through his illness, drove them off, and his wounds grew worse again; at Shanzhou Li Tingshen heard of the Prince of Yong’s humiliation and the deaths of Wei Shaohua and Wei Ju (note: this is why Cheng Kai, after returning to the Command, “could not move about because of his wounds”).",
  "程锋随仆固怀恩前锋发陕州，其后追击燕军残部往河北；陈瑞和随程锋军中（注：追击河北见《程家系列》【7】；陈瑞和随军为11月洛阳救治闵方城之前因）":
    "Cheng Feng set out from Shanzhou with Pugu Huai’en’s vanguard, and afterwards pursued the remnants of the Yan army into Hebei; Chen Ruihe was with Cheng Feng’s army (note: Chen Ruihe being with the army is what leads to his treating Min Fangcheng at Luoyang in the eleventh month).",
  "苍云自河东经泽潞，随李抱玉一路自河阳入，不经陕州，后战于昭觉寺（注：河东兵马按三路进军之北路行）":
    "The Cangyun Army came from Hedong through Ze and Lu and went in from Heyang with Li Baoyu all the way, not passing through Shanzhou, and later fought at Zhaojue Monastery (note: the Hedong forces took the northern of the three routes of advance).",
  "十月末，仆固怀恩等破史朝义于洛阳北郊横水、昭觉寺，史朝义北走；东京收复，回纥入城大掠，死者万计，火累旬不灭":
    "At the end of the tenth month Pugu Huai’en and others defeated Shi Chaoyi at Hengshui and Zhaojue Monastery in the northern outskirts of Luoyang, and Shi Chaoyi fled north; the Eastern Capital was recovered, the Uighurs entered the city and plundered it, the dead were counted by the ten thousand, and the fires did not die for weeks.",
  "秋冬（推定），大军南下后雁门留守（关岳代领破阵营，靳沉白、邱鸿、樊璋等）——留下的恰是两个云州人：邱鸿生于云中，樊璋745年即云州流民。是岁代北以北州县空虚（即回纥所见「州县空虚」），云州饥馑，流民南来代州境，靳沉白粮簿上多出一笔流民口粮（呼应《剑网3》云州饥馑设定，史无明文；正文作背景，不另起事件；不交代邱鸿家人下落，樊璋不认亲）；与758.6「粮自云州来」相对——同一条路，四年前运来的是粮，此时逃来的是人":
    "Autumn and winter: after the main army went south, those left holding Yanmen (Guan Yue in temporary command of the Rank-Breaker Corps, with Jin Chenbai, Qiu Hong, Fan Zhang and others) happened to include two men of Yunzhou: Qiu Hong was born at Yunzhong, and Fan Zhang had been a refugee from Yunzhou in 745. That year the prefectures and counties north of Dai stood empty (the very emptiness the Uighurs saw), Yunzhou was in famine, refugees came south into Daizhou, and one more item appeared in Jin Chenbai’s grain ledger: rations for refugees (the story does not say what became of Qiu Hong’s family, and Fan Zhang does not claim his kin). Set against 758.6, “the grain came from Yunzhou”: the same road; four years before it was grain that came along it, now it was people fleeing.",
  "程锋遣陈瑞和救闵方城 岚川云安置闵方城后返回天策府见到程凯":
    "Cheng Feng sent Chen Ruihe to save Min Fangcheng; having seen Min Fangcheng settled, Lanchuan Yun went back to the Tiance Command and saw Cheng Kai.",
  "洛阳会战间隙，狄元恪统管苍云行营，唯抽出一日功夫赴天策府，确认秦徽下落，上邙山祭拜；岚川云与程凯、李庭深等欲留他晚饭，他没答允，傍晚仍回行营理事，半月余率军返雁门":
    "In a lull in the fighting at Luoyang, Di Yuanke, in charge of the Cangyun field headquarters, took only one day away to go to the Tiance Command, make sure of what had become of Qin Hui, and go up Mount Beimang to pay his respects; Lanchuan Yun, Cheng Kai, Li Tingshen and the others wanted to keep him for supper, but he would not stay, and went back to the field headquarters at dusk to see to business; a little over half a month later he led the troops back to Yanmen.",
  "回纥至东京，以贼平恣行残忍，士女惧，登圣善寺、白马寺二阁避之，回纥纵火焚阁，伤死者万计，累旬火焰不止；朔方军及郭英乂、鱼朝恩等军不能禁暴，与回纥纵掠坊市及汝、郑等州，比屋荡尽，人悉以纸为衣，或有衣经者（《旧唐书·回纥传》；上承762.10F）":
    "The Uighurs reached the Eastern Capital and, the rebels being put down, gave free rein to their cruelty; the men and women of the city, in terror, climbed the two towers of Shengshan Monastery and Baima Monastery to escape them, and the Uighurs set fire to the towers, killing and wounding people by the ten thousand, and the flames did not die for weeks. The Shuofang Army and the armies of Guo Yingyi, Yu Chao’en and others could not stop the violence, and plundered the wards and markets together with the Uighurs, and the prefectures of Ru, Zheng and others, house after house stripped bare; people all wore paper for clothes, and some wore sutras (Old Book of Tang, Biography of the Uighurs; continues from 762.10F).",
  "东京收复后旬月间，狄元恪统管苍云行营驻洛阳城中，亲历回纥大掠：寺阁火累旬不灭，坊市比屋荡尽，街上有以纸为衣、以经为衣者；掠者非独回纥，朔方及郭英乂、鱼朝恩诸军亦与之纵掠（苍云755年弃关西去，所投正是朔方）。狄元恪约束本部不得出营掳掠——拦得住自己的兵，拦不住友军，更拦不住回纥；不上书、不与友军争执，只把营守住（正文不写成正面冲突）。其时闵方城昭觉寺重伤后，为岚川云安置于城中一处小院，卧屋内不能起，院墙外火光、哭喊彻夜可闻；身边有陈瑞和与程锋安排的一名仆从（见正文）。半月余狄元恪率军北返，快，可读作一种拒绝；闵方城留在小院中（至762.12强行动身）。注：天策残部虽编在郭英乂、鱼朝恩后殿，都统李承恩尚在，相对独立，不随掠（作者定）":
    "In the month or so after the Eastern Capital was recovered, Di Yuanke, in charge of the Cangyun field headquarters stationed in Luoyang, lived through the Uighur plunder at first hand: the monastery towers burning for weeks, the wards and markets stripped bare house after house, people in the streets wearing paper and wearing sutras for clothes; and the plunderers were not only the Uighurs, but the Shuofang Army and the armies of Guo Yingyi and Yu Chao’en too (in 755, when the Cangyun Army abandoned the pass and went west, it was the Shuofang Army it went to join). Di Yuanke forbade his own men to leave camp to loot: he could stop his own soldiers, but not the allied armies, still less the Uighurs; he wrote no memorial and did not quarrel with the allied armies, but simply held his camp (the story does not make it an open clash). At the time Min Fangcheng, gravely wounded at Zhaojue Monastery, had been settled by Lanchuan Yun in a small courtyard in the city, lying indoors unable to rise, the firelight and the wailing beyond the courtyard wall to be heard all night; with him were Chen Ruihe and a servant Cheng Feng had arranged. A little over half a month later Di Yuanke led the troops back north: quickly, which can be read as a kind of refusal; Min Fangcheng stayed in the small courtyard (until he insisted on setting out at 762.12). Note: although the Tiance remnant was placed in the rear guard of Guo Yingyi and Yu Chao’en, Li Cheng’en, Commander-in-Chief of the Tiance Command, was still there, and it stood relatively apart and took no part in the plunder.",
  "狄元恪抽一日赴天策府（站内推补条：确认秦徽下落、上邙山祭拜、不留晚饭），门口两三句间闻陕州之事——雍王不蹈舞，药子昂等四人各鞭一百，韦少华、魏琚一夕而死（李庭深在陕州亲闻，见762.10C）；狄元恪不评一语（正文一句带过；苍云不经陕州，此为二手）":
    "Di Yuanke took one day to go to the Tiance Command (see the supplementary entry: making sure of what had become of Qin Hui, paying his respects on Mount Beimang, not staying to supper), and in two or three sentences at the gate heard what had happened at Shanzhou: the Prince of Yong had not danced his obeisance, Yao Zi’ang and the three others had been given a hundred lashes each, and Wei Shaohua and Wei Ju had died that night (Li Tingshen heard it himself at Shanzhou; see 762.10C); Di Yuanke did not say a word on it (the Cangyun Army did not pass through Shanzhou; this was second-hand).",
  "薛坚随朔方军在东京（郭子仪罢后朔方军归仆固怀恩）：朔方军与回纥纵掠时，他的部伍抢未抢、他拦未拦，正文不说破，作者心中有数；与762.11B狄元恪同城，狄元恪知否亦留白":
    "Xue Jian was at the Eastern Capital with the Shuofang Army (after Guo Ziyi was dismissed, the Shuofang Army went to Pugu Huai’en): when the Shuofang Army plundered with the Uighurs, whether his men looted or not, whether he stopped them or not, the story does not say, though the author knows; he was in the same city as Di Yuanke at 762.11B, and whether Di Yuanke knew is also left blank.",
  "苍云凯旋北归，仍取河阳—泽潞—太原一路；时回纥驻河阳剽掠，归途自其营侧经过（狄元恪「半月余北返」之「快」多此一层，正文一句带过）；抵雁门后各营将领率部上李牧祠敬香，闵方城尚在洛阳（据《闵方城763到765》柳戎语）":
    "The Cangyun Army went home north in triumph, again by the Heyang–Ze–Lu–Taiyuan road; the Uighurs were then stationed at Heyang plundering, and the way home passed beside their camp (one more layer to the “speed” of Di Yuanke’s return north after a little over half a month); on reaching Yanmen the officers of each camp led their men up to the Li Mu shrine to burn incense, while Min Fangcheng was still at Luoyang.",
  "闵方城强行从洛阳动身 在代县被柳戎捡起来送回雁门（自763.1移：文档中闵方城到雁门后「年终岁末」上李牧祠、其后方过新岁，故动身当在农历762年十二月；到关后刀口化脓高热数日，柳戎守在榻边）":
    "Min Fangcheng insisted on setting out from Luoyang, and at Dai county was picked up by Liu Rong and brought back to Yanmen (on reaching the pass his wound festered and he ran a high fever for several days, with Liu Rong keeping watch by his bed).",
  "年终岁末，闵方城伤后头一回独自步行上李牧祠见薛直（骑马受不住，广武镇马道走得虚汗直冒）；柳戎沿马道追上，攥住他手扶他上城——「他们是他们，我…是我」；「从来没有人会急切地用力握住他的手」":
    "At the year’s end Min Fangcheng, for the first time since his wounds, went alone on foot up to the Li Mu shrine to see Xue Zhi (he could not bear to ride, and on the bridle road at Guangwu town he broke out in cold sweats); Liu Rong came after him up the bridle road, seized his hand and helped him up to the wall: “They are them, and I… am me”; “No one had ever grasped his hand so urgently and so hard.”",
  // 763
  "春间（推定，来唐约半年后逢十月吐蕃之乱），林叶矢搭新罗商船孤身渡海寻父，途中为蓬莱春山遥（方眠树）所救，登州登岸；至长安，经父亲当年的大使藤原清河（河清，时任秘书监）寻得其父（注：是年无日本官船，原「随日本商船」改作新罗船）":
    "In the spring (about half a year after arriving he would meet the Tibetan turmoil of the tenth month), Hayashi Kyōya crossed the sea alone on a Silla merchant ship to look for his father; on the way he was saved by Haruyama Haruka of Penglai (Fang Mianshu), and came ashore at Dengzhou; in Chang’an he found his father through Fujiwara no Kiyokawa (Heqing, then Director of the Palace Library), the ambassador his father had once come with.",
  "宝应二年正月，史朝义北走范阳，李怀仙拒之，朝义穷蹙缢死，安史之乱平；河北降将相继分领节度（张忠志赐名李宝臣、据恒州即旧常山郡，田承嗣、李怀仙、薛嵩等），藩镇之局自此始；苍云时在雁门，闵方城卧病（消息传到时无反应，正文一句带过）":
    "First month of the second year of Baoying: Shi Chaoyi fled north to Fanyang, Li Huaixian shut him out, and Chaoyi, at the end of his road, hanged himself; the An Lushan Rebellion was over. The surrendered generals of Hebei took over military commissions one after another (Zhang Zhongzhi, given the name Li Baochen, holding Hengzhou, the old Changshan commandery; Tian Chengsi, Li Huaixian, Xue Song and others), and the pattern of the autonomous military provinces began from this. The Cangyun Army was then at Yanmen, and Min Fangcheng lay ill (he showed no reaction when the news came).",
  "新岁，柳戎回师门过节数日又返雁门，带来棉袍裘衣；闵方城吐泻绞痛，年过得一塌糊涂，赶人出帐，边赛远无法；柳戎自伙房拎粥喂他，言明心意（「那我可就当你应了」），闵方城抽手背身不语（伤情底子：昭觉寺腹部重创、陈瑞和于洛阳施大手术，百日后方离流质，饮食不能生冷粗糙油荤；脑后一击落下头痛晕眩，并早年运木料时扑救爬犁撞树之暗伤）":
    "New Year: Liu Rong went back to her school for a few days of the festival and then returned to Yanmen, bringing a cotton robe and a fur coat; Min Fangcheng had vomiting, diarrhoea and griping pains, spent the New Year in utter misery, and drove people out of his tent, and Bian Saiyuan could do nothing; Liu Rong brought porridge from the kitchen and fed him, and spoke her heart (“Then I’ll take it that you’ve said yes”), and Min Fangcheng drew his hand back, turned away and said nothing (the injuries beneath this: a grave wound to the belly at Zhaojue Monastery, on which Chen Ruihe had operated at length in Luoyang, so that only after a hundred days could he leave liquid food, and he could take nothing cold, raw, coarse, oily or rich; a blow to the back of the head that left headaches and dizziness; and an old hidden injury from years before, when hauling timber he had thrown himself to save a sledge and been dashed against a tree).",
  "关岳女（关榆）出生":
    "Guan Yue’s daughter (Guan Yu) was born.",
  "春，回纥驻河阳约三月、部众剽掠之后北归：「可汗出泽、潞，与怀恩会，道太原去」（《新唐书·回鹘传》）；仆固怀恩送可汗出塞，往来过太原，河东节度辛云京亦闭城不与相闻；怀恩怒，具表其状，不报，由是怨望（《通鉴》卷223，广德元年追叙）":
    "Spring: the Uighurs, after about three months at Heyang with their people plundering, went back north: “the qaghan went out by Ze and Lu, met Huai’en, and left by way of Taiyuan” (New Book of Tang, Biography of the Uighurs); Pugu Huai’en saw the qaghan out beyond the frontier, passing Taiyuan both ways, and Xin Yunjing, Military Commissioner of Hedong, again shut the city and would have nothing to do with them; Huai’en, angry, set it all out in a memorial and got no answer, and bore a grudge from then on (Zizhi tongjian, juan 223, told in retrospect under the first year of Guangde).",
  "闵方城伤势有异 一度失去视力 柳戎唤夏明沧从药宗南下医治（三月二十生辰当夜头痛、翌晨目盲；颅脑外伤瘀肿压迫所致，一旬后视力大体恢复而有减损；夏明沧留苍云月余，时孟雪萦有孕不足三月；夏明沧言其「人不在这」「在西头。广袤的西」，闵方城答「报应」）":
    "Something went wrong with Min Fangcheng’s injuries and for a time he lost his sight; Liu Rong called Xia Mingcang south from the Beitian School of Medicine to treat him (on the night of his birthday, the twentieth of the third month, his head ached, and the next morning he was blind; it was caused by swelling and bruising from the head injury pressing on the brain, and after ten days his sight largely came back, though weakened. Xia Mingcang stayed at Cangyun over a month, while Meng Xueying was less than three months pregnant; Xia Mingcang said of him, “He isn’t here”, “Out west. The wide west”, and Min Fangcheng answered, “Retribution”).",
  "程锋北追叛军还洛；程宇（十七岁）入天策府——生在军营，久在唐军随父历练，中原战乱而随父归":
    "Cheng Feng came back to Luoyang from pursuing the rebels north; Cheng Yu (seventeen) entered the Tiance Command: born in an army camp, he had long been with the Tang army, learning beside his father, and came back with him when the war in the central plains ended.",
  "春（推定，与闵方城失明同月而不必同日），回纥北归，自太原经代北出塞，仍过雁门（路线推定，与762.9D同道）：同一道关门再开一回，这一回是送其出塞——辛云京闭太原城、不与相闻（763.2A），雁门开关只为让其早去；驮满东京财物的骑队自南而北，与762.9D南下时空鞍之骑相对。闵方城正目盲卧榻，又是只听得马蹄——762.9D时病卧，此时目盲，回纥一南一北两次过关，他都只听见，一次也没看见；望见者宜仍为邱鸿":
    "In the spring (the same month as Min Fangcheng’s blindness, though not necessarily the same day) the Uighurs went back north, leaving the frontier from Taiyuan through the lands north of Dai and passing Yanmen again (the same road as at 762.9D): the same gate of the pass opened once more, this time to see them out beyond the frontier. Xin Yunjing had shut Taiyuan and would have nothing to do with them (763.2A), and Yanmen opened the pass only to see them gone the sooner; the columns of riders, laden with the wealth of the Eastern Capital, going from south to north, set against the empty saddles of their ride south at 762.9D. Min Fangcheng lay blind in bed, and again only heard the hoofbeats: at 762.9D he lay ill, now he was blind; the Uighurs passed through the pass twice, once south and once north, and both times he only heard them and never once saw. The one who sees it should again be Qiu Hong.",
  "险些失明之后，闵方城忽给杜徵回信：「我因旧伤，经过一劫。目盲是什么情形，我知道了。你不容易。要保重。」无头无款；白霖念信，杜徵笑他「每回好容易写几句，都像平生第一次学会说话」（白霖，岑菡长姐之子，747年生，随杜徵学琴为书童）；卢秉毓所刻「闵恒」章闵方城只挂在革带上，从未蘸过红泥（月份推定）":
    "After nearly losing his sight, Min Fangcheng suddenly wrote back to Du Zheng: “Because of an old injury, I have been through an ordeal. Now I know what it is to be blind. It is not easy for you. Take care of yourself.” No heading and no name; Bai Lin read the letter out, and Du Zheng laughed that “every time he manages a few lines, it’s as if he’s just learned to talk for the first time in his life” (Bai Lin, son of Cen Han’s eldest sister, born 747, studied the qin with Du Zheng as his page); the seal “Min Heng” that Lu Bingyu had carved, Min Fangcheng only hung on his belt, and never once dipped in red seal paste.",
  "甘州危急 闵方城请命出援故土 成行而不得（城皆虚防，独木难支） 奉命护送流民、粮资等入凉州（此役有关岳为副，廖群随行；长孙忘情「我的宿将，我不许有失」，闵方城叩首而去；甘州难民中老者识其河西口音而拜）归返后卧病 后闻荔非承烈事（注：原作「甘州陷落」，据史与文档改——凉州764、甘州766方陷；月份从《通鉴》吐蕃入大震关系七月）":
    "Ganzhou in danger: Min Fangcheng asked to go to the relief of his homeland and was allowed to set out, but could do nothing (the cities were all empty of defence; one tree cannot hold up a house); under orders, he escorted refugees, grain and supplies into Liangzhou (on this campaign Guan Yue was his second and Liao Qun went with him; Zhangsun Wangqing: “My veteran general: I will not have him lost”, and Min Fangcheng bowed his head to the ground and went; among the refugees from Ganzhou an old man knew his Hexi accent and bowed to him). After returning he lay ill, and later heard of what had happened to Lifei Chenglie.",
  "七月，吐蕃入大震关，陷兰、廓、河、鄯、洮、岷、秦、成、渭等州，陇右尽失，河西自此与关中隔断（《通鉴》作「尽取河西、陇右之地」，实则凉州764、甘州766方陷）；是月改元广德（下接闵方城援河西）":
    "Seventh month: the Tibetans came in through the Dazhen Pass and took the prefectures of Lan, Kuo, He, Shan, Tao, Min, Qin, Cheng, Wei and others; all Longyou was lost, and Hexi was cut off from the land within the passes from then on (the Zizhi tongjian has “took all the lands of Hexi and Longyou”, but in fact Liangzhou fell only in 764 and Ganzhou in 766); in this month the era name was changed to Guangde (leading on to Min Fangcheng’s relief of Hexi).",
  "西归途中于灵武留一队兵马：队正廖群（凉州天宝县人，故土已失，灵武是离它最近之处，自请留驻）；闵方城留下此队，是他一个人的承诺（据《闵方城763到765》「后于灵武留下一队兵马」）":
    "On the way back west he left a squad at Lingwu: its leader Liao Qun (from Tianbao county in Liangzhou; his home was lost, and Lingwu was the nearest place to it, so he asked to stay); leaving this squad was Min Fangcheng’s own promise.",
  "闵方城自河西返雁门，郁结连同伤病，掩门不出；营中议其「只念一己之私、劝得统帅派了他去，却出兵无功」；关岳言其行营中宁可不吃、硬熬，晕过一回醒来只问地图；闵方城上书统帅乞骸骨；柳戎归来，在他手心写「郎心有脚」，端来伙房的汤饭（「为什么要去。知道打不赢。」）（月份推定）":
    "Min Fangcheng came back to Yanmen from Hexi, his misery bound up with his wounds and illness, and shut his door and would not come out; in the camp people said he “thought only of his own affairs, talked the Commander into sending him, and then took the field for nothing”; Guan Yue said that in the field headquarters he would rather not eat and just grit his teeth, and that once he fainted and on coming to asked only for the map; Min Fangcheng wrote to the Commander begging leave to retire; Liu Rong came back, wrote in the palm of his hand “a man’s heart has its own two feet” (that is, it will find its way back across river and sea), and brought him soup and rice from the kitchen (“Why did you go? You knew you couldn’t win.”).",
  "荔非承烈在邠州 假作入寇羌将行刺刺史 以身入局告边情 被邠州守军射死（一说假死 其人在西北边境复为游侠 有明教中人遇见过他）":
    "At Binzhou Lifei Chenglie, posing as a raiding Qiang commander, made an attempt on the prefect’s life, putting himself into the game to bring news of the frontier, and was shot dead by the Binzhou garrison (some say the death was faked, that he became a wandering swordsman again on the north-western frontier, and that someone of the Mingjiao met him).",
  "邠州兵乱烈火中，吕遂（知荔非谋划）暗遣羌汉混编队先一步入场搜捕，自断墙下救出荔非；荔非陌刀留在原地，旁有面目模糊、体貌几乎相当的羌部武人尸首，凤翔密探盖以刀与衣饰误认为其遗骨。荔非暗地被送出邠州，于城外羌寨休养，醒来渐渐回过味，知有人放自己自在，就此隐姓埋名——后人只见一老羌人游荡西陲，持巨斧斩敌擒贼，边民立小碑：「义斧三落，镇得一春」":
    "In the fire of the mutiny at Binzhou, Lü Sui (who knew Lifei’s plan) secretly sent a mixed Qiang and Han troop in ahead to search, and got Lifei out from under a broken wall; Lifei’s modao was left where it lay, beside it the body of a Qiang fighter with his face beyond recognition and almost his build, and the Fengxiang agents took it, by the blade and the clothes, for his remains. Lifei was secretly taken out of Binzhou to recover in a Qiang stockade outside the city; when he woke he gradually understood that someone had set him free, and from then on lived under another name. Those who came after saw only an old Qiang wandering the western frontier, cutting down enemies and seizing bandits with a great axe, and the frontier folk put up a small stele: “Three strokes of the righteous axe; one spring of peace.”",
  "秋，仆固怀恩与河东节度辛云京、监军骆奉仙相攻讦，云京、奉仙奏怀恩谋反，怀恩上书自讼，屯兵汾州不入朝，并令其子仆固玚率万人屯驻榆次（太原以东）；河东（太原）与朔方主力（汾州、榆次）自此相忌（月份推定，俟核；辛云京762年二月前为代州刺史，雁门即在代州，与苍云本有旧）":
    "Autumn: Pugu Huai’en traded accusations with Xin Yunjing, Military Commissioner of Hedong, and the Army Monitor Luo Fengxian; Yunjing and Fengxian reported that Huai’en was plotting rebellion, Huai’en sent up a memorial in his own defence, kept his troops at Fenzhou and would not go to court, and had his son Pugu Yang station ten thousand men at Yuci (east of Taiyuan); from then on Hedong (Taiyuan) and the main force of the Shuofang Army (Fenzhou, Yuci) were wary of each other (Xin Yunjing had been prefect of Daizhou until the second month of 762; Yanmen lies in Daizhou, so he had old ties with the Cangyun Army).",
  "河东与朔方相忌（见763.9A），辛云京不容河东之兵留驻朔方治所，苍云统帅奉命召回灵武那一队——一纸调令；闵方城卧病、上书乞骸骨，插不上话；廖群奉调东归，十月间回到雁门，离故土最近的那一处也退了（下接763.12B：闵方城对薛坚说「灵武、朔方，不能再退了」时，此队已撤回三月；正文不解释）":
    "With Hedong and Shuofang wary of each other (see 763.9A), Xin Yunjing would not allow Hedong troops to stay at the seat of the Shuofang commission, and the Cangyun Commander was ordered to recall the squad at Lingwu: a single order of transfer. Min Fangcheng, ill and begging leave to retire, could not get a word in; Liao Qun was transferred back east and reached Yanmen in the tenth month, and the place nearest his homeland was given up too (leading on to 763.12B: when Min Fangcheng tells Xue Jian “Lingwu, Shuofang: we can’t fall back any further”, this squad has already been withdrawn three months; the story does not explain).",
  "广德元年十月，泾州刺史高晖降吐蕃，引之深入至邠州；此前吐蕃屡入寇、边将告急而宦官程元振皆不奏闻，至此代宗始知入寇之急，下诏以雍王适为关内元帅、郭子仪为副元帅出镇咸阳（子仪闲赋日久部曲离散，召募才得二十骑而行）；吐蕃帅吐谷浑、党项、氐、羌二十余万众，弥漫数十里，渡渭沿山向东进军":
    "Tenth month of the first year of Guangde: Gao Hui, prefect of Jingzhou, went over to the Tibetans and led them deep in as far as Binzhou. Before this, though the Tibetans had raided again and again and the frontier generals had sent urgent reports, the eunuch Cheng Yuanzhen had passed none of them on; only now did Daizong learn how urgent the raids were, and by edict made Li Kuo, Prince of Yong, Supreme Commander of Guannei and Guo Ziyi Deputy Supreme Commander, to go out and hold Xianyang (Guo Ziyi had long been idle and his men had scattered; recruiting, he could find only twenty horsemen to set out with). The Tibetans led more than two hundred thousand Tuyuhun, Dangxiang, Di and Qiang, spread over dozens of li, crossed the Wei and advanced east along the hills.",
  "秋（约十月，去夏明沧苍云看诊又半年），孟雪萦诞下男婴，有惊无险；孩儿取名嘉荣——《山海经》灵植，取义草秀赤华，不畏雷霆":
    "Autumn (around the tenth month, half a year after Xia Mingcang went to Cangyun to treat Min Fangcheng): Meng Xueying gave birth to a boy, a scare but no harm; the child was named Jiarong, after a magical plant of the Classic of Mountains and Seas, for its meaning: a grass that flourishes, red-flowered, unafraid of thunder.",
  "闵方城并苍云诸将呈文 为荔非承烈正名（闵方城亏虚已甚 此事狄元恪出面主导 与靳沉白一同起草）":
    "Min Fangcheng and the Cangyun generals sent up a memorial to clear Lifei Chenglie’s name (Min Fangcheng being badly drained, Di Yuanke came forward to lead it, drafting it together with Jin Chenbai).",
  "邠州事传入京畿关内，多称羌将入寇杀刺史，传荔非为贰臣，圣人盛怒责问。污名传至苍云：薛褚想起年轻时家宅廊下听过的薛直「名声之论」，撂下手中兵器出武库求见，被关岳拦劝暂不声张；帐内闵方城忧愤呕血，不知从哪里挤出声音——「季韬，去，去找他」":
    "When the Binzhou affair reached the capital region and the land within the passes, most said that a Qiang commander had raided and killed the prefect, and Lifei was spoken of as a turncoat; the emperor, in great anger, demanded answers. The stain on his name reached Cangyun: Xue Chu remembered Xue Zhi’s “talk on reputation”, heard under the gallery of the family house when he was young, put down the weapon in his hands and left the armoury to ask for an audience, and was stopped by Guan Yue, who urged him to keep quiet for now; in his tent Min Fangcheng, grieving and angry, vomited blood, and from somewhere forced out a voice: “Jitao, go, go and find him.”",
  "吐蕃陷长安，代宗出幸陕州；鱼朝恩以陕州神策军迎扈，神策军自此入为天子禁军（《程家系列》「神策军因之复起」之根）":
    "The Tibetans took Chang’an and Daizong left for Shanzhou; Yu Chao’en met and escorted him with the Shence Army of Shanzhou, and from then on the Shence Army entered the capital as the emperor’s own palace army (the root of the Shence Army’s revival).",
  "闵方城推举关岳为破阵营副 邱鸿预备为一团长官（继任闵）樊璋脱离狄元恪 预备调任为邱鸿副官（一团团副）":
    "Min Fangcheng put forward Guan Yue as Deputy Corps Commander of the Rank-Breaker Corps; Qiu Hong to be readied as head of the First Regiment (succeeding Min); Fan Zhang to leave Di Yuanke and be readied for transfer as Qiu Hong’s deputy (deputy of the First Regiment).",
  "渭北行营兵马使吕遂（史实原型：吕月将）帅精兵二千初败吐蕃于周至县西；数日后吐蕃反扑，围其行营，吕遂被俘，不屈而死——距其遣队救出荔非，未及半月":
    "Lü Sui, Commander of Troops of the Weibei field headquarters (historical model: Lü Yuejiang), led two thousand picked troops and first defeated the Tibetans west of Zhouzhi county; some days later the Tibetans struck back and surrounded his headquarters, and Lü Sui was taken and died without yielding: not half a month after he had sent the troop that saved Lifei.",
  "十月九日吐蕃入长安，高晖与吐蕃大将马重英等立广武王承宏为帝，改元、设置百官；纵兵大掠，焚府库市里，长安萧然一空；六军逃散者所至剽掠，士民避乱皆入山谷；十二日代宗至陕郡，百官才有至者":
    "On the ninth day of the tenth month the Tibetans entered Chang’an, and Gao Hui and the Tibetan general Ma Chongying and others set up Li Chenghong, Prince of Guangwu, as emperor, changing the era name and appointing a full court; they let their soldiers loose to plunder, burned the treasuries and the markets and wards, and Chang’an was left desolate and empty; deserters from the Six Armies plundered wherever they went, and officials and people fleeing the turmoil all went into the hills and valleys. On the twelfth Daizong reached Shan commandery, and only then did some of the officials join him.",
  "苍云遣靳沉白往凤翔详查，邱鸿请命随行，薛褚同往备验骨。靳沉白见节度使幕府掌书记，封存往来邠州书牍副本、调令底稿，并取用印信照合年月；又遣邱鸿带亲兵疾赴邠州，扣住亲见刺史临场易计、伏兵出入门闼的旧录事参军，以军情核验为名送回凤翔——人证物证俱备，只剩薛褚看认遗骨":
    "The Cangyun Army sent Jin Chenbai to Fengxiang to look into it closely; Qiu Hong asked to go with him, and Xue Chu went too, ready to examine the bones. Jin Chenbai saw the secretary of the Military Commissioner’s staff, sealed the copies of letters to and from Binzhou and the drafts of orders, and used the seals to check the dates against each other; he also sent Qiu Hong with personal guards at speed to Binzhou to hold the former Administrative Supervisor, who had seen with his own eyes the prefect change the plan on the spot and the hidden troops going in and out of the gates, and send him back to Fengxiang on the pretext of verifying military intelligence. With witnesses and evidence complete, all that was left was for Xue Chu to identify the remains.",
  "吐蕃陷长安，日本少年林叶矢（来唐半年，搭新罗商船孤身寻父）被烧毁倒落的房屋木梁砸伤双腿，其父舍命护之于敌刀之下，身亡；岚川云救之带回安置点，陈瑞和为其诊治双腿——少年聋哑不通汉文，稍吃痛便一味哭泣，他跪在旁一点点摆正两腿、固定、喂药、一遍遍想法询问安慰。后岚川云携之归天策府，请许秋生诊治照料，以纸笔谈、教授汉文，收为养子":
    "When the Tibetans took Chang’an, the Japanese boy Hayashi Kyōya (half a year in the Tang, come alone on a Silla merchant ship to look for his father) had both legs crushed by a burning beam from a collapsing house, and his father, shielding him from an enemy blade at the cost of his own life, was killed; Lanchuan Yun saved him and took him back to the refuge, and Chen Ruihe treated his legs. The boy, all but deaf, unable to speak and knowing no Chinese, wept helplessly at the slightest pain, and Chen Ruihe knelt beside him, setting both legs straight little by little, splinting them, feeding him medicine, trying again and again to find ways to ask and to comfort. Later Lanchuan Yun took him back to the Tiance Command and asked Xu Qiusheng to treat and care for him; they talked with paper and brush, she taught him Chinese, and took him as her adopted son.",
  "墨昆袭关 扣押柳戎一行霸刀中人 狄元恪携樊璋出阵 而墨昆叫阵闵方城 闵方城出关应战（此生最后一次拿刀在阵前）关岳协助设计 墨昆被杀死":
    "Mokun raided the pass and seized Liu Rong’s party of Badao people; Di Yuanke took the field with Fan Zhang, but Mokun called out Min Fangcheng to fight, and Min Fangcheng went out of the pass to meet him (the last time in his life he held a blade before a battle line); with Guan Yue helping to lay the plan, Mokun was killed.",
  "薛褚看认遗骨：对魁梧骨架细察半日，视线移到牙齿——昔年守城，荔非下颌中奚兵牛骨朵，一侧臼齿碎裂，薛褚曾以烧过的细铜丝兜住残齿、绕邻牙固定、蜂蜡封口；而眼前遗骨臼齿齐整。他沉默——说不是，又要再查，关内愈乱，恐把凤翔、苍云都拖进去——故点头认定：宁信点头真能换来什么铁券，宁信那人已经逃出生天":
    "Xue Chu identifies the remains: he studied the big frame for half a day, then his eyes moved to the teeth. Years before, holding the city, Lifei had taken a blow to the jaw from a Xi soldier’s ox-bone mace that split a molar on one side, and Xue Chu had cradled the broken tooth in fine copper wire he had heated, wound it round the next teeth to hold it, and sealed it with beeswax; the molars of the bones before him were whole. He was silent: to say it was not him would mean more inquiry, and with the land within the passes in growing turmoil, he feared dragging Fengxiang and Cangyun into it. So he nodded and confirmed it: choosing to believe that a nod could truly buy some iron certificate, choosing to believe that the man had already escaped with his life.",
  "吐蕃退后，江蓠与程凯长安重逢，时已怀妊；陈瑞和闻天策府来将与江蓠是旧识，自卑而刻意避见，程凯提出相见时江蓠为他说话。天策军停留长安两月有余方归，江蓠有药材相送、欲往城外送行——陈瑞和念其月份大又有腰伤，反而自携往天策军营自报家门，替她把话一一说尽":
    "After the Tibetans withdrew, Jiang Li and Cheng Kai met again at Chang’an; she was by then with child. Chen Ruihe, hearing that the officer from the Tiance Command was an old friend of Jiang Li’s, felt himself unworthy and kept out of his way on purpose, and when Cheng Kai asked to meet him Jiang Li spoke up for him. The Tiance army stayed at Chang’an more than two months before going back, and Jiang Li had medicinal herbs to send and wanted to go outside the city to see them off; Chen Ruihe, mindful of how far along she was and of her injured back, instead took the herbs himself to the Tiance camp, gave his name, and said everything she had to say for her.",
  "靳沉白、邱鸿、薛褚赴凤翔取证验骨：靳沉白封存凤翔幕府往来邠州书牍副本与调令底稿；邱鸿赴邠州扣下旧录事参军；薛褚验骨，见臼齿齐整而点头（吐蕃围凤翔解后方至）":
    "Jin Chenbai, Qiu Hong and Xue Chu went to Fengxiang to gather evidence and examine the bones: Jin Chenbai sealed copies of the Fengxiang staff’s letters to and from Binzhou and the drafts of orders; Qiu Hong went to Binzhou and held the former Administrative Supervisor; Xue Chu examined the bones, saw the molars whole, and nodded (they arrived only after the Tibetan siege of Fengxiang was lifted).",
  "冬，营中煮羊肉，柳戎令伙头把汤筛过、下面、撒葱花送去（呼应759.9羊肉汤饼：同一道饭，筛去油荤与姜椒，由加害变为照料；正文不点破）；闵方城读杜徵寄来之书，念「白狼河北音书断」（沈佺期《独不见》），问军报、地图里的地方也能写进诗里；「是你所求，是我能的，那就…尽量」「肝肠寸断来着」「…真没有肉？」；柳戎道早年塞北营来破阵营切磋时已见过他":
    "Winter: mutton was being boiled in the camp, and Liu Rong had the cook strain the broth, put noodles in, scatter chopped scallion on top and send it over (an echo of the mutton noodle soup of 759.9: the same dish, with the fat and the ginger and pepper strained out, turned from harm to care; the story leaves it unsaid). Min Fangcheng read a book Du Zheng had sent and read out “North of the White Wolf River, letters are cut off” (Shen Quanqi, “Alone and Unseen”), and asked whether places from army reports and maps could also go into poems; “If it’s what you ask, and it’s in my power, then… I’ll try”; “It was supposed to break your heart”; “… Really no meat?” Liu Rong said she had seen him years before, when the Saibei Corps came to spar with the Rank-Breaker Corps.",
  "唐军与吐蕃拉锯至十二月，代宗方得还京":
    "The Tang army and the Tibetans fought back and forth until the twelfth month, when at last Daizong could return to the capital.",
  "腊月，柳戎欲与闵方城亲近，同榻而闵方城退却（「你就当…为我好。你要原谅我」；柳戎：「总觉得你是一个什么天兵天将，犯了事，被贬下来」）；翌晨柳戎替他穿甲，敲革带狮首「这狮子头一看就不会骗人」，闵方城替她掩衣襟「穿…就穿好。腊月里…」；营中流言「相识十年、尽平胡虏方叙儿女之情」；后岚川云来时闵方城对她说「我不知道有一天我要故意对人说谎，在人面前装作可怜」（见765.1A）":
    "Twelfth month: Liu Rong wanted to be close to Min Fangcheng, and when they shared a bed Min Fangcheng drew back (“Take it as… for my own good. You must forgive me”; Liu Rong: “I always feel you’re some general from heaven who did something wrong and was banished down here”); the next morning Liu Rong helped him into his armour, tapped the lion’s head on his belt, “You can tell at a glance this lion’s head couldn’t lie”, and Min Fangcheng pulled the front of her robe closed for her: “If you’re going to wear it… wear it properly. In the twelfth month…”; the rumour in the camp went, “ten years they’ve known each other, and only once the barbarians are all put down do they get round to love.” Later, when Lanchuan Yun came, Min Fangcheng said to her, “I never knew that one day I would lie to someone on purpose, and play the pitiable in front of people” (see 765.1A).",
  "吐蕃陷松、维、保三州及云山新筑二城，西川节度使高适不能救，剑南西山诸州入吐蕃":
    "The Tibetans took the prefectures of Song, Wei and Bao and the two newly built cities at Yunshan; Gao Shi, Military Commissioner of Xichuan, could not save them, and the prefectures of the Western Hills of Jiannan passed to the Tibetans.",
  "年关（腊月末，怀恩起兵消息传到之前；新正初即返汾州营中），薛坚自朔方军归省祭父，上广武城小房探闵方城（闵方城已移居广武城，常俯瞰练兵场）：「郎君」；闵方城抄《出师表》「盖追先帝之殊遇，欲报之于陛下也」；「去夏，我在河西……那是我最后一次看见祁连山」「郎君，灵武、朔方，不能再退了」——薛坚：「为此，我不惜己身」（此时闵方城留在灵武那一队已被召回三月，见763.9B，他知道，薛坚未必知道）；事后闵方城托柳戎寻一匹毛色铁青的马（旧事：薛直战亡后，闵方城扛手靶任十一岁的薛坚打到跪地）；可选：时河东与朔方对峙，朔方军官过太原入河东须验文牒，狄元恪掌关防（文档原系764年新岁，据「年关」与怀恩起兵先后移此）":
    "At the year’s end (late in the twelfth month, before the news of Huai’en’s rising arrived; he went back to the camp at Fenzhou at the start of the new year), Xue Jian came home from the Shuofang Army to visit and make offerings to his father, and went up to the little house at Guangwu to see Min Fangcheng (Min Fangcheng had by then moved to Guangwu, and often looked down on the drill ground): “Langjun.” Min Fangcheng was copying the “Memorial on Sending Out the Troops”: “for they remember the special favour of the late emperor, and wish to repay it to Your Majesty”; “Last summer I was in Hexi … that was the last time I saw the Qilian Mountains”; “Langjun, Lingwu, Shuofang: we can’t fall back any further.” Xue Jian: “For that, I will not spare myself” (by now the squad Min Fangcheng had left at Lingwu had been recalled three months before, see 763.9B; he knew, and Xue Jian may not have). Afterwards Min Fangcheng asked Liu Rong to find him a horse with an iron-grey coat (an old story: after Xue Zhi fell in battle, Min Fangcheng held up a hand target and let the eleven-year-old Xue Jian strike at it until he dropped to his knees). An optional detail: with Hedong and Shuofang facing off at the time, Shuofang officers passing Taiyuan into Hedong had to have their papers checked, and Di Yuanke was in charge of the pass defences.",
  "西山诸州入吐蕃后，唐青阳回岷江上游的祖地一趟，唐哲陪他去：松、维、保一带是氐羌之地，十二月的岷山雪路，又是吐蕃新占之地，一个人走不了。他第一次看见祖先的山（740 年安戎城），穿的是官军的衣服；最后一次，那里已经换了主人":
    "After the prefectures of the Western Hills passed to the Tibetans, Tang Qingyang went back once to his ancestral land on the upper Min River, and Tang Zhe went with him: the Song–Wei–Bao country was the land of the Di and Qiang, the snowy roads of the Min Mountains in the twelfth month, and newly taken by the Tibetans besides; one man alone could not make it. The first time he saw his forefathers’ mountains (Anrong, 740) he was wearing the uniform of the government army; the last time, they had changed masters.",
  // 764
  "年内，狄元恪与闵方城交集渐多，偶然让他试过自己的马槊——闵方城一辈子只拿盾刀，而马槊长、重、韧，将门子弟自幼练起尚未必窥其门径，他还是重伤之躯：不见意外也不推让，掂了一下，指腹抹过槊杆，一抽一移便持握得当；手腕一沉，肩背自然一正，两腿扎住，对裹了皮面的草靶一击贯透，抽出又刺，一连数次无一不中。还给狄元恪，什么也没说，走了，留下他看着那个身被数疮的草靶":
    "In the course of the year Di Yuanke and Min Fangcheng crossed paths more and more, and once, by chance, he let him try his cavalry lance. Min Fangcheng had held nothing but shield-and-blade all his life, and the lance is long, heavy and supple, so that even sons of military houses who train from childhood may never find the way into it, and he was gravely injured besides; he showed neither surprise nor reluctance, weighed it once, ran the pad of his finger along the shaft, and with one draw and shift had his grip right; a sink of the wrist, his shoulders and back squared of themselves, legs planted, and one thrust went clean through a straw target wrapped in hide; he drew it out and thrust again, several times in a row, and not one missed. He gave it back to Di Yuanke without a word and left, leaving him looking at the straw target and its many wounds.",
  "许秋生授天策府医博士（战后叙功），此后终老天策府":
    "Xu Qiusheng was made Medical Erudite of the Tiance Command (in the awards for merit after the war), and spent the rest of his life there.",
  "吐蕃陷凉州，河西节度使杨志烈西走甘州（年份据通行说，月份待核；763.7闵方城护送百姓所入之凉州自此亦失）":
    "The Tibetans took Liangzhou, and Yang Zhilie, Military Commissioner of Hexi, fled west to Ganzhou (the Liangzhou into which Min Fangcheng had escorted the people at 763.7 was now lost too).",
  "程骞入天策府试训":
    "Cheng Qian entered the Tiance Command on trial.",
  "程锋议修族谱，程凯拒归宗；程钊名下记「未娶，有女一人，从母姓」":
    "Cheng Feng proposed revising the clan genealogy, and Cheng Kai refused to return to the clan; under Cheng Zhao’s name was written “unmarried; one daughter, who takes her mother’s surname”.",
  "江蓠产女":
    "Jiang Li gave birth to a daughter.",
  "合剑南东、西川为一道，复以严武为节度使":
    "Jiannan East and West Circuits were combined into one, and Yan Wu was again made Military Commissioner.",
  "广德二年正月，仆固怀恩反：怀恩既不为朝廷所用，与河东都将李竭诚潜谋取太原，辛云京觉之，杀竭诚，乘城设备；怀恩使其子玚将兵攻太原，云京出与战，玚大败而还，遂与浑瑊引兵围榆次，与河东军相持（《通鉴》卷223，《旧唐书·马燧传》作「斩竭诚，固城自守」；下接764.2A仆固玚之死、怀恩北走灵武；764.2C浑释之之死）":
    "First month of the second year of Guangde: Pugu Huai’en rebelled. No longer of use to the court, Huai’en secretly plotted with Li Jiecheng, a senior commander of Hedong, to take Taiyuan; Xin Yunjing found out, killed Jiecheng and manned the walls; Huai’en sent his son Yang with troops to attack Taiyuan, Yunjing came out to fight, and Yang was badly beaten and fell back, then with Hun Jian laid siege to Yuci, facing the Hedong army (Zizhi tongjian, juan 223; the Old Book of Tang, Biography of Ma Sui, has “beheaded Jiecheng and held the city fast”; leading on to 764.2A, the death of Pugu Yang and Huai’en’s flight north to Lingwu, and 764.2C, the death of Hun Shizhi).",
  "正月至二月（仆固怀恩之变），辛云京严守太原，最惧怀恩与回纥合谋自北而来；苍云差事在钉死北面——关岳以新营副守关，狄元恪带二团南下戒备忻、代一线，并为太原北路押粮，辛云京由此识之（764.9召为行军司马之伏笔；又接762.11B：狄元恪亲见朔方军东京纵掠而本部不出营）；闵方城居广武城，不预其事":
    "First to second month (Pugu Huai’en’s rising): Xin Yunjing held Taiyuan tightly, fearing most of all that Huai’en and the Uighurs would come down together from the north; the Cangyun Army’s task was to nail down the north. Guan Yue, as the new Deputy Corps Commander, held the pass, and Di Yuanke took the Second Regiment south to guard the Xin–Dai line and escort grain on the northern road of Taiyuan, and so Xin Yunjing came to know him (foreshadowing his recall as Adjutant at 764.9; it also follows on from 762.11B, where Di Yuanke saw the Shuofang Army plunder the Eastern Capital and kept his own men in camp); Min Fangcheng lived at Guangwu and took no part.",
  "薛坚新正初回到汾州营中，旋即怀恩反，被编入仆固玚攻榆次的兵马（浑瑊式：名在朔方军籍，非其所择）；苍云这边狄元恪二团正在忻、代一线戒备，同在一条战线上，始终没有照面；闵方城在广武城、薛褚在武库，各自等消息，一个月里彼此一句话不说（兑现二人「远远关注故统帅儿子」之默契）":
    "At the start of the new year Xue Jian went back to the camp at Fenzhou, and soon after Huai’en rebelled and he was put into Pugu Yang’s force attacking Yuci (as with Hun Jian: his name was on the Shuofang Army’s rolls, not by his own choice); on the Cangyun side Di Yuanke’s Second Regiment was on guard along the Xin–Dai line, on the same front, and they never met; Min Fangcheng at Guangwu and Xue Chu in the armoury each waited for news, and for a month neither said a word to the other (keeping their unspoken understanding to “keep a distant eye on the late Commander’s son”).",
  "二月，仆固玚为部将焦晖、白玉所杀，部众哗变；怀恩与麾下三百人渡河北走灵武；郭子仪至汾州，「怀恩之众数万悉归之」（《通鉴》卷223），浑瑊重归郭子仪":
    "Second month: Pugu Yang was killed by his officers Jiao Hui and Bai Yu, and his men mutinied; Huai’en crossed the river north to Lingwu with three hundred of his followers; Guo Ziyi reached Fenzhou, and “Huai’en’s men, several tens of thousands, all came over to him” (Zizhi tongjian, juan 223), Hun Jian returning to Guo Ziyi.",
  "仆固玚死后朔方将士归郭子仪，归顺者名籍随军报传至太原北路；狄元恪押粮途中于文书里见「薛坚」之名，遣人传话回雁门——生死凭一纸名册得知（名籍母题）；闵方城听罢无话，薛褚在武库照旧修甲":
    "After Pugu Yang’s death the Shuofang officers and men came over to Guo Ziyi, and the rolls of those who submitted came with the army reports to the northern road of Taiyuan; Di Yuanke, on the road escorting grain, saw the name “Xue Jian” in the papers and sent word back to Yanmen: life or death known through a single roll of names (the motif of the rolls); Min Fangcheng heard it and said nothing, and Xue Chu went on mending armour in the armoury.",
  "二月，仆固怀恩北走至灵州，杀守将浑释之，收其军（浑释之即浑瑊之父；两唐书作战死于吐蕃，此从《通鉴》卷223）；灵武自此为怀恩据点，至765.9其死":
    "Second month: Pugu Huai’en, fleeing north, reached Lingzhou, killed Hun Shizhi, the commander there, and took over his army (Hun Shizhi was Hun Jian’s father; both Books of Tang have him killed fighting the Tibetans; this follows the Zizhi tongjian, juan 223); Lingwu was Huai’en’s stronghold from then until his death at 765.9.",
  "荔非承烈归葬李牧祠 闵方城退居二线 763年10月的预期人事变动生效":
    "Lifei Chenglie reburied at the Li Mu shrine; Min Fangcheng stepped back from front-line command; the changes of post planned in the tenth month of 763 took effect.",
  "荔非一案批复，追认为忠挚之士，赐归葬苍云李牧祠；薛褚迎遗骨归葬毕，又回到武库去，偶尔捻起一根铜丝出神":
    "The ruling on Lifei’s case came down: he was recognised as a loyal and devoted man and granted burial at the Cangyun Army’s Li Mu shrine; Xue Chu, having brought his remains home and seen them buried, went back to the armoury, and now and then would pick up a length of copper wire and lose himself in thought.",
  "雁门边地粮站：靳沉白遇少年书手任迪简，廪给簿册出入——簿记须真，人另设法护之（与荔非归葬平行）（月份推定）":
    "At a frontier grain station at Yanmen, Jin Chenbai came upon the young copyist Ren Dijian, and discrepancies in the ration ledgers: the books must be true, and the person is protected some other way (parallel with Lifei’s reburial).",
  "闵方城传功樊璋（广武城小院，私下完成，在场唯关岳，狄元恪后至）":
    "Min Fangcheng passed on his art to Fan Zhang (in the little courtyard at Guangwu, done privately, with only Guan Yue present; Di Yuanke arrived later).",
  "传功之日：关岳送来汤饼，闵方城对着面碗看了一会热气，忽然说「叫樊璋上来」。小院中令樊璋脱甲持盾，一下一下让他承劲，示意何处松开、何处收紧，一个多时辰；狄元恪自映雪湖亲巡归来才听通报——永远是闵方城说做就执行，旁人只能后一步听说——纵马入广武，恰见樊璋抵住闵方城一击，闵方城一顿，竟退了半步。樊璋掣盾跽地，胸腹间内力震荡如钟，余响不绝；狄元恪立于近旁，隐隐「听」到樊璋背影里的雷音——他在邱鸿那里见识过，薛褚曾引他把手放在武库炉边狸猫肚皮上：「我从没能和人讲清何为铁骨衣。佛音说法，声如雷震，在里头。」闵方城脸色灰白：「带他下去。……你们试他。要在人前。」关岳：「给你留个人？」「下去罢。」「闵大哥，汤饼凉了。」离去时樊璋回身望了闵方城好一会，如幼狮离群；狄元恪犹自望着，见他缓缓坐下去，靠着墙垛，变成城墙的一部分":
    "The day of the passing on: Guan Yue brought noodle soup, and Min Fangcheng looked at the steam over the bowl for a while and suddenly said, “Have Fan Zhang come up.” In the little courtyard he had Fan Zhang take off his armour and hold the shield, and let him take the force blow by blow, showing him where to loosen and where to tighten, for more than two hours; Di Yuanke, back from inspecting Yingxue Lake himself, only then heard the report (it was always so: Min Fangcheng said it and it was done, and others could only hear of it a step behind), rode into Guangwu, and arrived just as Fan Zhang held off a blow from Min Fangcheng, and Min Fangcheng checked and actually gave back half a step. Fan Zhang dropped his shield and knelt, the inner strength in his chest and belly ringing like a bell, the echo going on and on; Di Yuanke, standing close by, faintly “heard” the thunder in Fan Zhang’s back. He had met it before with Qiu Hong: Xue Chu had once had him put his hand on the belly of the cat by the armoury forge: “I have never been able to explain to anyone what Iron-Bone is. When the Buddha preaches the Law, the voice is like thunder; it’s in there.” Min Fangcheng, grey-faced: “Take him down. … You test him. It has to be in front of people.” Guan Yue: “Shall I leave someone with you?” “Go down.” “Brother Min, the noodles have gone cold.” As he left, Fan Zhang turned and looked back at Min Fangcheng a long while, like a lion cub leaving the pride; Di Yuanke was still looking when he saw him slowly sit down against the battlement and become part of the city wall.",
  "夏，柳戎为闵方城寻得青黑马；闵方城携柳戎赴北边草场遛马，映雪湖边柳戎睡着，闵方城说草原上睡着魂会走，得喊自己名字把它喊回来；柳戎喊了自己名字，又喊了他大名，闵方城赧然「你…胡闹」（月份推定）":
    "Summer: Liu Rong found the black-green horse for Min Fangcheng; Min Fangcheng took Liu Rong to the northern grasslands to walk the horse, and by Yingxue Lake Liu Rong fell asleep; Min Fangcheng said that if you fall asleep on the grassland your soul wanders off, and you have to call your own name to call it back; Liu Rong called her own name, and then called his full name, and Min Fangcheng, embarrassed: “You… are being silly.”",
  "樊璋经人前试艺，定为一团（邱鸿）副官，出狄元恪帐下；任命下时樊璋帐中叩首，狄元恪亦跪而相拥（月份推定）":
    "After the test of his skill in front of people, Fan Zhang was confirmed as deputy of the First Regiment (Qiu Hong’s), leaving Di Yuanke’s command; when the appointment came down Fan Zhang knelt in the tent and bowed his head to the ground, and Di Yuanke too knelt and embraced him.",
  "狄元恪离苍云，南归太原任河东节度（辛云京）行军司马；关岳以营副暂兼领二团，再遴选主将（月份推定；伏笔：764年初怀恩之变中辛云京识之，见764.1B；又接762.11B）":
    "Di Yuanke left the Cangyun Army and went south to Taiyuan as Adjutant to the Military Commissioner of Hedong (Xin Yunjing); Guan Yue, as Deputy Corps Commander, took temporary charge of the Second Regiment as well until a new commander was chosen (foreshadowing: Xin Yunjing came to know him during Huai’en’s rising early in 764, see 764.1B; it also follows on from 762.11B).",
  "严武破吐蕃七万众，拔当狗城；十月又拔盐川城；崔旰随严武于汉州，取吐蕃四城":
    "Yan Wu defeated seventy thousand Tibetans and took Danggou city; in the tenth month he also took Yanchuan city; Cui Gan, with Yan Wu at Hanzhou, took four Tibetan cities.",
  "秋冬，仆固怀恩引回纥、吐蕃十万寇邠州、奉天，郭子仪屯奉天拒之，敌引去（月份推定）":
    "Autumn and winter: Pugu Huai’en led a hundred thousand Uighurs and Tibetans to raid Binzhou and Fengtian; Guo Ziyi camped at Fengtian to hold them off, and the enemy drew back.",
  "冬至讲武，天策与神策军竞猎：程宇好胜，独追虎入林遇狼群（后查为神策算计），程凯飞身接住程宇，后背重重着地、带起旧患，连日不得安寝；岚川云接苍云来信，邀新年北上一会，程凯：「去。再不应啊，没时候了」（文档原标十月，冬至在农历十一月，从十一月）":
    "The winter-solstice military review: the Tiance Command and the Shence Army held a hunting contest; Cheng Yu, eager to win, chased a tiger alone into the woods and met a wolf pack (it later turned out to be a Shence trap); Cheng Kai leapt to catch Cheng Yu and landed hard on his back, bringing his old injuries back, and for days could not sleep; Lanchuan Yun got a letter from the Cangyun Army inviting them north for the new year, and Cheng Kai said: “Go. If we don’t accept this time, there won’t be time left.”",
  "关岳带训时把女儿关榆放在闵方城寝帐，闵方城裹毯把她安置在腿窝里，一边看文书一边应她；关榆攀马颈伏上马背，闵方城：「你少动这念头。不好。」（后：关榆长大不识碑上之名，在广武城上成婚；关氏子女无一人再沾军伍，年节上李牧祠祭扫「一个无亲无故的苍云将军」）":
    "When Guan Yue was leading training he left his daughter Guan Yu in Min Fangcheng’s tent, and Min Fangcheng wrapped her in a blanket and settled her in the crook of his legs, answering her while he read his papers; Guan Yu climbed a horse’s neck and lay along its back, and Min Fangcheng: “Put that idea out of your head. It’s no good.” (Afterwards: Guan Yu grew up not knowing the names on the stele, and married on the walls of Guangwu; not one of the Guan children ever had anything to do with the army again, and at New Year they went up to the Li Mu shrine to sweep the grave of “a Cangyun general with no kin”.)",
  // 765
  "（结局位置）此时邱鸿已在一团长官任上（764.3 接掌）、樊璋为其副（764.8），二人组合继承闵方城／关岳成为破阵营核心——邱鸿右臂齐肘而断，右上肢位置带肩盾包住残端、左手持刀，为「无盾」铁骨衣；樊璋持斩马刑天，为「重盾」铁骨衣，战阵上补足其薄弱处。后邱鸿与医女贺兰成婚，军饷用以收容边地孤幼":
    "(Where things stand at the end) By now Qiu Hong was head of the First Regiment (taking over at 764.3) and Fan Zhang his deputy (764.8), and the two together had inherited from Min Fangcheng and Guan Yue the core of the Rank-Breaker Corps: Qiu Hong, his right arm off at the elbow, a shoulder shield covering the stump where the right arm had been and his blade in his left hand, an Iron-Bone “without a shield”; Fan Zhang, wielding Zhanma Xingtian, an Iron-Bone of the “heavy shield”, making up for Qiu Hong’s weak side in battle. Later Qiu Hong married the physician He Lan, and his army pay went to taking in the orphans of the frontier.",
  "邱鸿接掌一团后，以军饷收容边地孤幼，其中有几个说奚语的孩子（作者定：即屈突真身边那几个孩子；正文不点名，不交代来历）；贺兰以医女协理（与婚事拆开，婚事另见767条；系年月份待定，在邱鸿接掌一团之后，不与闵方城亡故同月）":
    "After Qiu Hong took over the First Regiment, he used his army pay to take in the orphans of the frontier, among them a few children who spoke Xi (they are the children who were with Qutu Zhen; the story does not name them or say where they came from); He Lan, as physician, helped with the work (the marriage: see 767).",
  "南诏命凤伽异于昆川筑拓东城（今昆明）；德化碑作「赞普钟十四年」，换算待核":
    "Nanzhao had Fengjiayi build the city of Tuodong at Kunchuan (present-day Kunming); the Dehua Stele gives “the fourteenth year of Zanpuzhong”.",
  "正月，岚川云、程凯应邀至苍云（三邀方成：762年末岚川云赴洛阳扑空，763年秋因吐蕃入长安未成行）：宴上击鼓催花，闵方城把花球丢给程凯，程凯一箭射散彩球；关岳打铁花；闵方城与程凯论「偶然」「手印」「是还回去了」，「我这个人，非常幸运。程子阳，你也是」；岚川云与闵方城两上长城（「两下里，总得有一个人高兴」；「不可辜负」「你也让我回来了」）；上元夜闵方城对柳戎道「谢了……种种」":
    "First month: Lanchuan Yun and Cheng Kai came to the Cangyun Army at its invitation (it took three invitations: at the end of 762 Lanchuan Yun went to Luoyang and missed him, and in the autumn of 763 they could not go because the Tibetans had entered Chang’an); at the feast they played drum-and-pass-the-flower, Min Fangcheng tossed the flower ball to Cheng Kai, and Cheng Kai shot the coloured ball apart with one arrow; Guan Yue put on the iron-flower display; Min Fangcheng and Cheng Kai talked of “chance”, of “handprints”, of “it has been given back”: “I am a very lucky man. Cheng Ziyang, so are you”; Lanchuan Yun and Min Fangcheng went up the Great Wall twice (“Between the two of us, one of us should be happy”; “It must not be let down”; “You let me come back too”); on the night of the Lantern Festival Min Fangcheng said to Liu Rong: “Thank you… for everything.”",
  "闵方城帐中亡故（时岚川云、程凯正访苍云）：正月十六晨（上元次日），送走天策二人后久无动静，关岳入视、柳戎以狐尾挠其鼻尖而不应；边赛远飞马追回岚川云、程凯；翌日薛坚返苍云（年节归省途中，时已在郭子仪麾下），关岳引至马厩牵出青黑马：「闵大哥留了话，说这是存在」":
    "Min Fangcheng died in his tent (Lanchuan Yun and Cheng Kai were then visiting the Cangyun Army): on the morning of the sixteenth of the first month (the day after the Lantern Festival), after he had seen the two from the Tiance Command off, there was no sound from him for a long time; Guan Yue went in to look, and Liu Rong tickled the tip of his nose with a fox tail and he did not stir; Bian Saiyuan galloped after Lanchuan Yun and Cheng Kai and brought them back. The next day Xue Jian came back to Cangyun (on his way home for the New Year visit; by then he was under Guo Ziyi), and Guan Yue took him to the stable and led out the black-green horse: “Brother Min left word. He said: this is being.”",
  "关岳儿子（关槐）出生":
    "Guan Yue’s son (Guan Huai) was born.",
  "严武卒。在任厚敛奢侈，梓州刺史章彝小忤即被杖杀，然吐蕃畏之不敢犯境；其母叹「今始免为官婢矣」。是年夏，杜甫携家离成都东下（待核）":
    "Yan Wu died. In office he had taxed heavily and lived extravagantly, and Zhang Yi, prefect of Zizhou, was flogged to death for a small offence against him, but the Tibetans feared him and did not dare cross the border; his mother sighed, “Only now am I safe from becoming a government slave.” That summer Du Fu left Chengdu with his family and went east.",
  "郭英乂为剑南节度使":
    "Guo Yingyi became Military Commissioner of Jiannan.",
  "永泰元年九月，仆固怀恩诱吐蕃、回纥、党项、吐谷浑、奴剌等数十万入寇，怀恩死于鸣沙（下接765.10郭子仪泾阳单骑见回纥；闵方城已于是年正月亡故）":
    "Ninth month of the first year of Yongtai: Pugu Huai’en enticed several hundred thousand Tibetans, Uighurs, Dangxiang, Tuyuhun, Nula and others to raid, and Huai’en died at Mingsha (leading on to 765.10, Guo Ziyi riding alone to meet the Uighurs at Jingyang; Min Fangcheng had died in the first month of that year).",
  "郭英乂杀王崇俊、逼崔旰回成都，崔旰乘大雪败其军，郭英乂出奔被杀；柏茂琳、杨子琳、李昌夔起兵讨旰，蜀中大乱。程铎站朝廷委任的节度使，郭死后随柏茂琳诸将讨旰（待定；月份待核）":
    "Guo Yingyi killed Wang Chongjun and forced Cui Gan back to Chengdu; Cui Gan, taking advantage of a heavy snowfall, defeated his army, and Guo Yingyi fled and was killed; Bai Maolin, Yang Zilin and Li Changkui raised troops against Cui Gan, and Shu was thrown into chaos. Cheng Duo stood with the Military Commissioner the court had appointed, and after Guo’s death went with Bai Maolin and the other generals against Cui Gan (undecided).",
  "郭子仪泾阳单骑说回纥（史）；程锋京西防秋，初识回纥上层":
    "Guo Ziyi rode alone at Jingyang to win over the Uighurs (historical); Cheng Feng, on autumn frontier duty west of the capital, first came to know the Uighur leaders.",
  // 766
  "林叶矢随李庭深携程骞下江南，途经湖州苕溪，见陆羽（756年南渡，760年结庐苕溪，此后长居湖州）与其风炉——三足之一铸「圣唐灭胡明年铸」，即764年，把战争的终结铸进器物；「茶道」一词首见于湖州诗僧皎然诗，叶矢佛性与茶道于此合流（注：年份推定，约766–767；原「万花谷中见陆羽」移此，慧木仍在谷中）":
    "Hayashi Kyōya went south of the Yangzi with Li Tingshen and Cheng Qian, and passing the Tiao Stream at Huzhou saw Lu Yu (who had crossed south in 756, built a hut on the Tiao Stream in 760, and lived at Huzhou long after) and his wind stove: on one of its three legs was cast “made in the year after the holy Tang destroyed the Hu”, that is, 764, casting the end of the war into the vessel itself; the term “the way of tea” first appears in a poem by Jiaoran, the poet-monk of Huzhou, and here Kyōya’s Buddha-nature and the way of tea flowed together (around 766–767).",
  "程骞服毒草，随李庭深下江南入长歌；李庭深娶朱鹭":
    "Cheng Qian, having failed to make the grade, tried to take his own life with a poisonous herb; he went south of the Yangzi with Li Tingshen into the Changge School; Li Tingshen married Zhu Lu.",
  "吐蕃陷甘州、肃州，河西节度杨休明徙治沙州（大历元年；月份待核；闵方城故土自此尽失，其死后一年）":
    "The Tibetans took Ganzhou and Suzhou, and Yang Xiuming, Military Commissioner of Hexi, moved his seat to Shazhou (first year of Dali; Min Fangcheng’s homeland was now wholly lost, a year after his death).",
  "杜鸿渐入蜀，姑息崔旰，分置东川；次年崔旰为西川节度使。讨旰诸将各得安置，程铎被闲置——守了一辈子的规矩，最后是规矩不要他（待定）":
    "Du Hongjian came into Shu, indulged Cui Gan, and divided off Dongchuan; the next year Cui Gan became Military Commissioner of Xichuan. The generals who had moved against Cui Gan were each provided for, and Cheng Duo was left idle: he had kept the rules all his life, and in the end the rules did not want him (undecided).",
  "南诏立《南诏德化碑》于太和城，自述为合乎华夏礼法的藩国，叛唐「非本心」；段韶在立碑之列——一个 751 年在西洱河打赢的人，听着碑文说自己从未想叛":
    "Nanzhao set up the Nanzhao Dehua Stele at Taihe city, describing itself as a vassal state in keeping with Chinese rites and law, and its break with the Tang as “not its true intent”; Duan Shao was among those present when the stele was set up: a man who had won at the Xi’er River in 751, listening to the inscription say he had never meant to rebel.",
  "程锋奉命西行，经灵州至天德军；李庭深的信追到天德军，回信「满纸愧悔」":
    "Cheng Feng was sent west under orders, by way of Lingzhou to the Tiande Army; Li Tingshen’s letter caught up with him at the Tiande Army, and his reply was “a page full of remorse”.",
  // 767
  "邱鸿与贺兰成婚（自765条拆出：闵方城765年正月亡故，弟子事师「心丧三年」（《礼记·檀弓上》），婚事至早在767年前后；具体年月待定）":
    "Qiu Hong and He Lan married (Min Fangcheng died in the first month of 765, and a disciple keeps “mourning in the heart for three years” for his master (Book of Rites, “Tangong I”), so the marriage was around 767 at the earliest).",
  "程锋取道回鹘抵北庭，遇杨休明遇害余波，识曹令忠":
    "Cheng Feng reached Beiting by the Uighur road, met the aftermath of Yang Xiuming’s murder, and came to know Cao Lingzhong.",
  "程钊生母亡故，程锋葬之于程钊侧并作墓志（790年北庭陷落，墓地湮没）":
    "Cheng Zhao’s mother died, and Cheng Feng buried her beside Cheng Zhao and wrote her epitaph (when Beiting fell in 790 the graves were lost).",
  // 768
  "陈瑞和携江蓠与女儿返故乡庐州安居":
    "Chen Ruihe took Jiang Li and their daughter home to Luzhou to settle.",
  "崔旰入朝，赐名崔宁，留弟崔宽守成都；杨子琳乘虚袭入，崔宁妾任氏出家财募兵，崔宽借此击退。杨子琳是程铎当年并肩讨旰的人，崔宁是他不肯认的人，而朝廷认的已是崔宁——他按规矩替崔宁守城，与唐遐同在一面城墙上。规矩没变，变的是规矩指着的人（待定）。唐遐在这时把754年「十五天」的事告诉唐青阳；知道了也不改什么：肩上的伤还在，姓还是唐":
    "Cui Gan went to court and was given the name Cui Ning, leaving his younger brother Cui Kuan to hold Chengdu; Yang Zilin seized the chance to break in, Cui Ning’s concubine Lady Ren paid for recruits out of the family’s wealth, and with them Cui Kuan drove him back. Yang Zilin was a man Cheng Duo had fought beside against Cui Gan, Cui Ning a man he would not acknowledge, and the man the court acknowledged was now Cui Ning: by the rules, he held the city for Cui Ning, on the same wall as Tang Xia. The rules had not changed; what had changed was the man they pointed to (undecided). It was now that Tang Xia told Tang Qingyang about the “fifteen days” of 754; knowing changed nothing: the wound in his shoulder was still there, and his surname was still Tang.",
  "程锋自北庭东返，757年腰伤加重，因伤辞官返洛——战乱后宦官专权、鱼朝恩势大，神策军因之复起，程氏军功卓著之族少不得受磋磨":
    "Cheng Feng came back east from Beiting; the back injury of 757 had grown worse, and he resigned his post on account of it and returned to Luoyang. After the war the eunuchs held power and Yu Chao’en was mighty, and the Shence Army rose again on that account; a clan like the Chengs, outstanding for its military merit, could not escape being ground down.",
  // 769
  "程锋道边望尘不拜被构陷，趋庭请罪跪两个时辰方罢——「此人长此以往要失分寸，而我不能。这些事桩桩件件，到往后都是证据」；又有人以夫人西域出身揣度其凭妻室勾连内外。程凯秋冬旧患卧病中致信宣杨请其看顾，一封信耗去不少心神，岚川云收拢纸砚扶其卧下；宣杨自洛阳歌楼联络点得信赴程府，及时搜出被偷藏的文书，凭蛛丝马迹反将一军，度过危机":
    "Cheng Feng, at the roadside, did not bow to the dust of a great man’s carriage, and was falsely accused; he hurried to court to ask for punishment and knelt for four hours before it was dropped: “If this man carries on like this he will lose all sense of measure, and I cannot. Every one of these things will be evidence later.” Others too speculated that, his wife being from the Western Regions, he used her to make connections inside and outside. Cheng Kai, laid up in autumn and winter with his old illness, wrote to Xuan Yang asking her to look out for his brother; the one letter cost him much of his strength, and Lanchuan Yun gathered up the paper and inkstone and helped him lie down. Xuan Yang got the letter at the liaison post in a Luoyang singing house and went to the Cheng house, found in time the documents someone had secretly hidden there, and following the faintest traces turned the tables, and the crisis passed.",
  // 770
  "大历五年四月，帝（李俶）设计绞杀鱼朝恩，凌雪阁不少为此谋划；宣杨往天策府告程凯：监军伏诛，魏谦兄弟可以瞑目，兄长也没白受——末次相见，「我们阁中是树，你们是碑」「树…树啊，它比碑长久」":
    "Fourth month of the fifth year of Dali: the emperor (Li Chu) contrived to have Yu Chao’en strangled, and many in the Lingxue Pavilion had a hand in the planning; Xuan Yang went to the Tiance Command to tell Cheng Kai: the Army Monitor has been put to death, our brother Wei Qian can close his eyes in peace, and your elder brother did not suffer for nothing. Their last meeting: “In our Pavilion we are trees; you are steles.” “Trees… trees, yes. They last longer than steles.”",
  "仲夏，林叶矢及冠，岚川云赠之护身短刀，言及短刀来历；是年腊月，程凯病故，叶矢事以父礼，服丧三年，愈发有心事——念及岚川从此在唐土无亲无故，唯一念想是父兄早年亡于长安、再未东还，于是发愿：「如能解她苦厄，我当成行」，为她渡海送故人归乡":
    "Midsummer: Hayashi Kyōya came of age, and Lanchuan Yun gave him a short blade for his protection, telling him where it came from; in the twelfth month of that year Cheng Kai died, and Kyōya mourned him as a father for three years, more and more weighed down with thought: knowing that Lanchuan now had no kin left in the Tang lands, and that her one remaining wish was for her father and brother, who had died in Chang’an years before and never gone back east, he made a vow, “If I can ease her grief, I will go”: to cross the sea for her and take the departed home.",
  "杜甫流寓湖南，与侨居的御史苏涣唱和；冬，杜甫卒于湘江舟中（待核；卒月不详，系于孟冬）。底色：苏涣为彭涣原型，其后半生取舍待定":
    "Du Fu, a wanderer in Hunan, exchanged poems with the censor Su Huan, also living there far from home; in winter Du Fu died in a boat on the Xiang River. Background: Su Huan is the model for Peng Huan; what to take from the second half of Su Huan’s life is undecided.",
  "程凯病故。自府城告破留下伤病不愈，四十七岁危重，到那时候才、或者说不得不渐渐跟自己和解——名字、家族、命运种种。程锋曾提出接回家中安养，他不听；项旌为校尉，到他寝房外站岗，看人病重觉得心里不安。程凯去后几年，李庭深上书乞骸骨":
    "Cheng Kai died of illness. Wounded and ill, never healed since the Command fell, gravely ill at forty-seven, only then (or rather, only because he had to) did he gradually make peace with himself: his name, his family, his fate and all the rest. Cheng Feng had offered to take him home to rest and recover, and he would not; Xiang Jing, by then a Commandant, stood guard outside his bedroom, uneasy to see him so ill. A few years after Cheng Kai’s death, Li Tingshen begged leave to retire.",
  "年底，宣杨回门派闻天策府知节殿病故，检得程凯忌日与师父高垣去世同一天——不过隔了十八年":
    "At the year’s end Xuan Yang, back at her school, heard that Zhijie Hall of the Tiance Command (Cheng Kai) had died of illness, and, looking it up, found that the day of Cheng Kai’s death was the same as the day her master Gao Yuan had died: only eighteen years apart.",
  // 771
  "程凯亡后，程锋领命往山南西道，镇梁州，以御京师；程宇随其去。梁州是入蜀的北门：程铎若如待定稿所写闲置成都，兄弟二人隔一条金牛道，一在门口，一在门里":
    "After Cheng Kai’s death, Cheng Feng was ordered to Shannan West Circuit to hold Liangzhou and guard the approaches to the capital; Cheng Yu went with him. Liangzhou was the northern gate into Shu: if Cheng Duo was left idle at Chengdu, as the draft still to be settled has it, the two brothers had only the Jinniu road between them, one at the gate and one inside it.",
  "萨珊波斯余部犹在吐火罗地区活动，入贡之记录至是年犹存":
    "Remnants of Sasanian Persia were still active in the region of Tokharistan, and records of their tribute survive down to this year.",
  // 772
  "程宇得知吐蕃陷河陇、西北尽在其手，屡屡请命，终得率一小队护送诏使赴北庭（是年诏赐北庭曹令忠姓李，史），为果毅都尉，此后音讯断绝":
    "Cheng Yu, learning that the Tibetans had taken Hexi and Longyou and held all the north-west, asked again and again to go, and at last was allowed to lead a small troop escorting an imperial envoy to Beiting (that year an edict granted Cao Lingzhong of Beiting the surname Li; historical), as Vice Commandant; after that nothing more was heard of him.",
  // 773
  "林叶矢为程凯服丧期满，发愿渡海送岚川云父兄遗刀归乡；时无遣唐使船，候船":
    "His mourning for Cheng Kai over, Hayashi Kyōya vowed to cross the sea and take the blades left by Lanchuan Yun’s father and brother home; there were no embassy ships then, and he waited for a ship.",
  // 778
  "宝龟遣唐使归航，第一船遇风破损，小野石根等三十八人、唐使赵宝英等二十五人失踪；藤原清河之女喜娘随残船漂流六日抵天草西仲岛——林叶矢携刀登此船，欲送刀主还乡，以全岚川云夙愿，然海道无常，不见归帆":
    "The Hōki embassy to the Tang sailed home; the first ship was damaged in a storm, and thirty-eight people including Ono no Iwane, and twenty-five including the Tang envoy Zhao Baoying, were lost; Fujiwara no Kiyokawa’s daughter Kijō drifted six days on the wreck and reached Nishinakajima in Amakusa. Hayashi Kyōya had boarded this ship with the blade, meaning to take its owner home and fulfil Lanchuan Yun’s long-held wish; but the sea road is unsure, and no returning sail was seen.",
  // 780
  "程锋亡故":
    "Cheng Feng died.",
  // 781
  "北庭使者经回纥道抵长安，北庭将吏叙官超七资（史）":
    "Envoys from Beiting reached Chang’an by the Uighur road, and the officers and officials of Beiting were promoted seven grades beyond the usual (historical).",
  // 790
  "北庭陷落，程宇随杨袭古退守西州——出兵后十八年未得归返":
    "Beiting fell, and Cheng Yu fell back with Yang Xigu to hold Xizhou: eighteen years since he set out, and he had never come home.",
  // 792
  "程宇殉于西州":
    "Cheng Yu fell at Xizhou.",
};
